/* Lecture 9 video lecture data: chapters, slide start times, timed bilingual transcript (generated). */
window.LEC = {"num":9,"videoBase":"https://wabyking.github.io/nlp2026-videos-2/lecture09/","parts":[{"n":1,"title":"Why Medical AI? Domains, Giants and Timing","blurb":"Why build a domain-specific model at all, why medicine is the domain worth it, and why the moment for medical AI is now.","file":"lecture09_part1.mp4","poster":"lecture09_part1.jpg","duration":501.1,"first":1,"last":9,"slides":[{"n":1,"title":"Title: Lecture 9","t":0.8},{"n":2,"title":"About Me","t":65.05},{"n":3,"title":"Contents","t":122.71},{"n":4,"title":"1 Why Medical AI?","t":189.84},{"n":5,"title":"Why Work on a Specific Domain? (1) Competing with Giants","t":216.02},{"n":6,"title":"Why Work on a Specific Domain? (2) From General to Professional","t":276.1},{"n":7,"title":"Why Work on a Specific Domain? (3) Benefits vs. Costs","t":329.25},{"n":8,"title":"Why Medicine?","t":383.77},{"n":9,"title":"Why Medical AI Now?","t":431.2}],"sents":[[0.8,3.38,1,"Good morning everyone, and welcome back.","大家早上好，欢迎回来。"],[3.73,13.18,1,"Last week was all about your final projects and research sharing, and the week before that we spent a whole lecture on LLM agents and harness engineering.","上周我们讲的是大家的期末项目和研究分享，再之前一周，我们用了整整一讲来讨论 LLM 智能体和 harness 工程。"],[13.53,23.23,1,"Today we do something a bit different: instead of a new technique, we take one domain, medicine, and see what happens when everything you've learned so far meets the real world.","今天有点不一样：我们不讲新技术，而是聚焦一个领域——医学，看看你们学过的一切遇到真实世界时会发生什么。"],[23.58,25.82,1,"Medicine is a great stress test.","医学是一个绝佳的压力测试。"],[26.17,35.28,1,"Pre-training, supervised fine-tuning, RLHF, reasoning with RL, multimodal models, agents: every one of them shows up today.","预训练、监督微调、RLHF、基于强化学习的推理、多模态模型、智能体：今天每一样都会出现。"],[35.63,42.77,1,"But now the stakes are high, the data are messy and private, and good on the benchmark is not good enough.","但现在风险很高，数据杂乱又涉及隐私，而且仅仅在基准测试上表现好是远远不够的。"],[43.12,49.77,1,"A lot of what I'll show is from our own group at CUHK-Shenzhen, starting with HuatuoGPT.","我今天展示的很多内容来自我们港中大（深圳）自己的团队，从 HuatuoGPT 讲起。"],[50.12,53.29,1,"I'm not choosing it because it's the only work out there.","我选它，并不是因为它是这个领域唯一的工作。"],[53.64,59.14,1,"I'm choosing it because I can tell you the inside story, including the things that didn't work.","而是因为我可以告诉你们背后的真实故事，包括那些没有成功的尝试。"],[59.49,63.65,1,"The title says where we're heading: generalist medical AI.","标题已经说明了我们的方向：通用医学人工智能。"],[64.9,69.07,2,"A quick word about me, so you know where today's perspective comes from.","先简单介绍一下我自己，让大家知道今天的视角从何而来。"],[69.42,77.4,2,"I did my PhD at the University of Padova, and I've been at CUHK-Shenzhen since two thousand twenty-two.","我在帕多瓦大学读的博士，从 2022 年起在港中大（深圳）工作。"],[77.75,86.15,2,"My appointment is shared between the School of Data Science and the School of Medicine, plus the Shenzhen Loop Area Institute, SLAI.","我同时任职于数据科学学院和医学院，以及深圳河套学院，也就是 SLAI。"],[86.5,93.75,2,"That dual role is exactly why medicine became our main application area: I sit between the AI people and the doctors.","正是这种双重身份，让医学成了我们的主要应用方向：我正好处在 AI 研究者和医生之间。"],[94.1,97.62,2,"My research falls into four buckets, all around agents.","我的研究可以分为四大块，都围绕智能体展开。"],[97.97,108.56,2,"How they plan and reason, how they perceive audio, images and signals, how they interact with humans, and where they get applied, with medicine as the flagship.","智能体如何规划和推理，如何感知音频、图像和信号，如何与人交互，以及应用在哪里，其中医学是旗舰方向。"],[108.91,116.23,2,"Almost everything you'll see today is open-sourced under the name FreedomIntelligence on Hugging Face and GitHub.","今天你们看到的几乎所有成果，都以 FreedomIntelligence 的名义在 Hugging Face 和 GitHub 上开源了。"],[116.58,121.31,2,"So if something catches your eye for a project, you can download it and play with it.","所以如果有什么东西让你对项目感兴趣，可以直接下载下来玩一玩。"],[122.56,125.79,3,"Here's the roadmap for today, in three acts.","这是今天的路线图，分为三幕。"],[126.14,138.94,3,"First, foundations: why medical AI at all, the story of HuatuoGPT, our first medical LLM, and then a definition of generalist medical AI, or GMAI.","第一幕是基础：为什么要做医学 AI，我们第一个医学大模型 HuatuoGPT 的故事，以及通用医学人工智能，也就是 GMAI 的定义。"],[139.29,149.15,3,"Second, the roadmap: the capabilities a generalist medical model needs, which are perception, reasoning, generation and multilinguality.","第二幕是路线图：一个通用医学模型需要的能力，包括感知、推理、生成和多语言。"],[149.5,152.07,3,"And then the challenges blocking the way.","然后是挡在路上的各种挑战。"],[152.42,159.05,3,"Third, the vision: why I think the next leap comes from environments rather than from bigger models.","第三幕是愿景：为什么我认为下一次飞跃来自环境，而不是更大的模型。"],[159.4,166.57,3,"Then real applications, and finally an outlook that includes some thoughts on AI entrepreneurship.","然后是真实的应用，最后是展望，其中包括一些关于 AI 创业的思考。"],[166.92,171.07,3,"Look at the box on the right, because it's the thesis of the whole lecture.","请看右边这个框，它是整堂课的核心论点。"],[171.42,173.99,3,"Generalist medical AI is the goal.","通用医学 AI 是目标。"],[174.34,177.62,3,"Trustworthy medical AI is the way to get there.","可信医学 AI 是通往目标的道路。"],[177.97,183.69,3,"And environments, meaning simulated patients, hospitals and cells, are the engine.","而环境，也就是模拟的病人、医院和细胞，是驱动的引擎。"],[184.04,188.44,3,"If you remember only three sentences from today, make it those three.","如果今天你只记住三句话，那就记住这三句。"],[189.69,192.9,4,"Let's start with the most basic question: why medical AI?","我们从最基本的问题开始：为什么要做医学 AI？"],[193.25,195.33,4,"The one-line answer is on the slide.","一句话的答案就在这里。"],[195.68,201.99,4,"Medicine is where language models can create enormous value, and also where a mistake can hurt someone.","医学是语言模型能创造巨大价值的地方，同时也是一个错误就可能伤害到人的地方。"],[202.34,206.43,4,"That combination is what makes it both attractive and hard.","正是这种组合，让它既有吸引力又很困难。"],[206.78,214.62,4,"Over the next few slides I'll give you three angles: why pick a specific domain at all, why medicine in particular, and why now.","接下来几页，我会从三个角度来讲：为什么要选一个特定领域，为什么偏偏是医学，以及为什么是现在。"],[215.87,222.0,5,"First, why should a university lab work on a specific domain instead of general-purpose models?","首先，一个大学实验室为什么要做特定领域，而不是通用模型？"],[222.35,225.36,5,"Honestly, part of the answer is strategy.","说实话，部分原因是策略。"],[225.71,230.71,5,"In the general domain you're competing with giant companies that have tens of thousands of GPUs.","在通用领域，你是在和拥有数万张 GPU 的巨头公司竞争。"],[231.06,238.38,5,"If we try to out-train them on general chatbots, we lose, and we waste resources on an over-crowded race.","如果我们想在通用聊天机器人上比他们训练得更好，我们会输，而且会把资源浪费在一场过度拥挤的竞赛里。"],[238.73,240.17,5,"Look at the two triangles.","看这两个三角形。"],[240.52,245.52,5,"On the left, general AGI: one huge, expensive black triangle.","左边是通用 AGI：一个巨大而昂贵的黑色三角形。"],[245.87,250.84,5,"On the right, medical AGI is a smaller triangle sitting inside the big one.","右边，医学 AGI 是嵌在大三角形里面的一个小三角形。"],[251.19,255.18,5,"The idea is that medicine is a sandbox for AGI.","这里的想法是：医学是 AGI 的沙盒。"],[255.53,263.95,5,"It needs most of the same ingredients, like knowledge, reasoning, multimodal perception, interaction with humans and safety.","它需要大部分相同的要素，比如知识、推理、多模态感知、与人的交互以及安全性。"],[264.3,268.57,5,"But it's a scoped setting you can actually afford to study.","但它是一个有边界的场景，你真正负担得起去研究。"],[268.92,274.7,5,"So a domain isn't a retreat from the big questions; it's a cheaper place to ask them.","所以，做一个领域并不是逃避大问题，而是在一个更便宜的地方去追问这些大问题。"],[275.95,278.99,6,"The second reason is about where the frontier is moving.","第二个原因，关乎前沿正在往哪里移动。"],[279.34,286.57,6,"LLMs are already good at general problems: writing an email, summarizing an article, answering trivia.","大模型已经很擅长通用问题了：写邮件、总结文章、回答常识问题。"],[286.92,289.46,6,"The next step is professional problems.","下一步是专业问题。"],[289.81,297.51,6,"Here's a nice way to think about it: can an LLM do a task that would take an average professional five hours?","有一个很好的思考方式：大模型能不能完成一个普通专业人士需要五个小时才能做完的任务？"],[297.86,308.55,6,"For a doctor, think of reviewing a complicated patient: reading months of records, looking at images, checking lab trends, consulting guidelines, and writing a plan.","对医生来说，想象一下审阅一个复杂病例：读几个月的病历、看影像、查化验趋势、查阅指南，再写出治疗方案。"],[308.9,314.56,6,"That kind of long, expert, high-stakes task is exactly where today's models still struggle.","这种耗时长、需要专业知识、风险又高的任务，恰恰是今天的模型仍然吃力的地方。"],[314.91,320.54,6,"And medicine gives us lots of such tasks with clear real-world value.","而医学为我们提供了大量这样的任务，并且有明确的现实价值。"],[320.89,327.85,6,"If you want to measure whether AI can do real professional work, medicine is one of the best testbeds we have.","如果你想衡量 AI 能否胜任真正的专业工作，医学是我们手里最好的试验场之一。"],[329.1,333.02,7,"Third, think of it as benefits versus costs.","第三，可以把它看作收益与成本的权衡。"],[333.37,338.42,7,"On the benefit side, working on valuable applications makes research sustainable.","在收益这一边，做有价值的应用能让研究可持续。"],[338.77,345.36,7,"When what you build actually helps people, you get partners, data and funding, and the work keeps going.","当你做的东西真正帮到了人，你就会得到合作伙伴、数据和资金，工作就能持续下去。"],[345.71,352.9,7,"Healthcare is a huge part of every economy: in most countries it accounts for roughly five to twenty percent of GDP.","医疗是每个经济体中的重要组成部分：在大多数国家，它大约占 GDP 的百分之五到百分之二十。"],[353.25,354.32,7,"Everyone needs it.","每个人都需要它。"],[354.67,362.68,7,"The same logic pushed us into multilingual models, like Arabic LLMs, which connect to the Belt and Road context.","同样的逻辑也让我们走进了多语言模型，比如阿拉伯语大模型，它与一带一路的背景相关。"],[363.03,367.73,7,"And into education, where agents can change how people learn.","还有教育领域，智能体可以改变人们的学习方式。"],[368.08,373.1,7,"On the cost side, a focused domain needs far less compute than chasing general AGI.","在成本这一边，专注一个领域所需的算力，远少于追逐通用 AGI。"],[373.45,376.8,7,"So the balance tips clearly: more benefit, less cost.","所以天平明显倾斜：收益更多，成本更少。"],[377.15,382.37,7,"That's a decision framework you can reuse when you pick your own research topics.","这是一个决策框架，你们选择自己的研究课题时也可以拿来用。"],[383.62,387.62,8,"So why medicine specifically, rather than law or finance?","那为什么偏偏是医学，而不是法律或金融？"],[387.97,389.1,8,"Four criteria.","有四条标准。"],[389.45,392.69,8,"It benefits a huge population, literally everyone.","它惠及庞大的人群，实际上是每一个人。"],[393.04,402.2,8,"It is challenging enough: medicine combines knowledge, multimodal evidence, uncertainty and interaction, so it pushes the technology.","它足够有挑战性：医学融合了知识、多模态证据、不确定性和交互，因此能推动技术进步。"],[402.55,407.9,8,"It can attract sustainable funding, from hospitals, governments and industry.","它能吸引可持续的资金，来自医院、政府和产业界。"],[408.25,415.1,8,"And as a university, it lets us do public-welfare work, which is part of why universities exist.","而且作为大学，它让我们可以做公益性的工作，这本来就是大学存在的意义之一。"],[415.45,417.97,8,"Very few domains tick all four boxes.","很少有领域能同时满足这四条。"],[418.32,425.48,8,"Finance has funding but less of a public-welfare angle; some social-good areas have impact but little funding.","金融有资金，但公益属性较弱；一些社会公益领域有影响力，却缺少资金。"],[425.83,429.8,8,"Medicine has all four, which is why we've stayed with it.","医学四条全占，这就是我们一直坚持做它的原因。"],[431.05,435.32,9,"And why now? Three forces line up at the same time.","那为什么是现在？三股力量同时汇聚到了一起。"],[435.67,439.91,9,"Demand: populations are aging, and chronic disease is rising.","第一是需求：人口在老龄化，慢性病在增加。"],[440.26,446.58,9,"The WHO projects a shortfall of around ten to eleven million health workers by twenty thirty.","世界卫生组织预计，到 2030 年，医疗卫生人员的缺口大约在一千万到一千一百万。"],[446.93,450.35,9,"On top of that, good doctors concentrate in big cities.","此外，好医生都集中在大城市。"],[450.7,460.98,9,"Capability: Google's AMIE, published in Nature in twenty twenty-five, was tested in a blinded OSCE-style study with patient actors.","第二是能力：谷歌的 AMIE 于 2025 年发表在 Nature 上，它在一个有病人扮演者参与的盲法 OSCE 式研究中接受了测试。"],[461.33,466.59,9,"Specialists rated it above primary-care physicians on thirty of thirty-two axes.","专科医生在 32 个维度中的 30 个上，给它的评分都高于初级保健医生。"],[466.94,471.09,9,"And reasoning and multimodal models keep improving.","而推理模型和多模态模型还在不断进步。"],[471.44,477.19,9,"Adoption: OpenEvidence reports that about sixty-five percent of US physicians use it.","第三是落地应用：OpenEvidence 称，大约百分之六十五的美国医生在使用它。"],[477.54,484.96,9,"And in China we have regional deployments like HuatuoGPT in Longgang, which covers about five million people.","在中国，我们也有区域性部署，比如在龙岗部署的 HuatuoGPT，覆盖约五百万人口。"],[485.31,490.01,9,"The sentence at the bottom is the key insight: the gap is no longer exam scores.","底部这句话是关键洞见：差距已经不在考试分数上了。"],[490.36,494.64,9,"It's trust, workflow integration and evidence of real-world benefit.","而在于信任、融入工作流程，以及真实世界获益的证据。"],[494.99,499.3,9,"Keep that in mind, because it shapes the whole second half of the lecture.","请记住这一点，因为它决定了这堂课的整个后半部分。"]]},{"n":2,"title":"The Story of HuatuoGPT: Data, Hybrid SFT and RLMF","blurb":"How HuatuoGPT was built: Huatuo-26M data, hybrid SFT mixing doctors' answers with LLM-distilled dialogues, and RL with mixed feedback.","file":"lecture09_part2.mp4","poster":"lecture09_part2.jpg","duration":903.4,"first":10,"last":25,"slides":[{"n":10,"title":"2 The Story of HuatuoGPT","t":0.8},{"n":11,"title":"Timeline of Our Medical LLMs","t":28.49},{"n":12,"title":"Starting from Data","t":95.71},{"n":13,"title":"Huatuo-26M: The Largest Chinese Medical QA Dataset","t":159.72},{"n":14,"title":"HuatuoGPT: Training Recipe","t":208.84},{"n":15,"title":"Motivation: Doctors vs. ChatGPT","t":264.96},{"n":16,"title":"HuatuoGPT: Two-Stage Training","t":338.73},{"n":17,"title":"Stage 1: SFT with Hybrid Data","t":402.69},{"n":18,"title":"Hybrid Data (1): Polish Doctors' Answers with an LLM","t":457.15},{"n":19,"title":"Hybrid Data (2): Let the LLM Play a Doctor","t":509.54},{"n":20,"title":"Hybrid SFT Data in Numbers","t":569.71},{"n":21,"title":"Training Loss","t":618.38},{"n":22,"title":"Stage 2: RL with Mixed Feedback (RLMF)","t":674.63},{"n":23,"title":"RLMF: Reward Model Training","t":733.61},{"n":24,"title":"RLMF: Reward Curve","t":788.4},{"n":25,"title":"Training Details","t":842.85}],"sents":[[0.8,1.87,10,"That's the why.","这就是为什么。"],[2.22,11.48,10,"Now let me tell you our own story, because it shows concretely how the general recipe from earlier lectures changes when you apply it to medicine.","现在我来讲讲我们自己的故事，因为它具体展示了前几讲的通用方法在应用到医学时会发生怎样的变化。"],[11.83,16.72,10,"HuatuoGPT was our first medical LLM, and it taught us three lessons.","HuatuoGPT 是我们第一个医学大模型，它教会了我们三件事。"],[17.07,27.09,10,"I'll unpack them in three parts: the data must look like doctors, the knowledge must actually be injected, and evaluation is much harder than it looks.","我会分三部分展开：数据必须像医生，知识必须真正注入进去，而评测远比看起来要难。"],[28.34,33.81,11,"Here's the timeline of our medical LLMs, so you can see the arc before we dive into details.","这是我们医学大模型的时间线，让大家在深入细节之前先看到整体脉络。"],[34.16,37.39,11,"Don't try to read every line; look at the direction of travel.","不用逐行去读，看它前进的方向就好。"],[37.74,45.71,11,"We started in twenty twenty-three with HuatuoGPT, which focused on talking like a doctor, plus the Huatuo-26M dataset.","我们在 2023 年从 HuatuoGPT 起步，它专注于像医生一样说话，同时还有 Huatuo-26M 数据集。"],[46.06,54.78,11,"Then HuatuoGPT-II focused on knowledge, then Apollo went multilingual, then HuatuoGPT-Vision added images.","接着 HuatuoGPT-II 专注于知识，然后 Apollo 走向多语言，再然后 HuatuoGPT-Vision 加入了图像。"],[55.13,63.14,11,"In late twenty twenty-four we had real deployment in local hospitals, and Apollo-2 scaled to fifty languages.","2024 年下半年，我们在本地医院实现了真正的部署，Apollo-2 扩展到了 50 种语言。"],[63.49,68.75,11,"And HuatuoGPT-o1 brought o1-style reasoning into medicine.","HuatuoGPT-o1 则把 o1 式的推理带进了医学。"],[69.1,78.32,11,"In twenty twenty-five came video generation with MedGen, and full-modality traditional Chinese medicine with ShizhenGPT.","2025 年，又有了做视频生成的 MedGen，以及支持全模态的中医大模型 ShizhenGPT。"],[78.67,86.94,11,"So the story is: style, then knowledge, then languages, then modalities, then reasoning, then deployment.","所以整个故事是：先是风格，然后是知识，然后是语言，然后是模态，然后是推理，再然后是部署。"],[87.29,94.31,11,"Each step was triggered by a limitation of the previous one, and that's how I'll walk you through it.","每一步都是由前一步的局限所触发的，我也会按这个顺序带大家走一遍。"],[95.56,97.23,12,"Everything started from data.","一切都从数据开始。"],[97.58,106.96,12,"Before we trained anything, we built Huatuo-26M, a Chinese medical question-answering dataset with about twenty-six million QA pairs.","在训练任何模型之前，我们先构建了 Huatuo-26M，一个包含约两千六百万问答对的中文医学问答数据集。"],[107.31,108.71,12,"Look at the table on the left.","看左边这张表。"],[109.06,117.33,12,"The vast majority, about twenty-five million pairs, come from online consultation records: real patients asking real doctors.","其中绝大部分，大约两千五百万对，来自在线问诊记录：真实的病人在问真实的医生。"],[117.68,121.6,12,"Smaller parts come from encyclopedias and knowledge bases.","较小的部分来自百科全书和知识库。"],[121.95,127.98,12,"Notice the lengths: questions average about forty-five characters and answers about one hundred twenty.","注意长度：问题平均大约 45 个字符，答案大约 120 个字符。"],[128.33,135.68,12,"Encyclopedia answers are long, around five hundred forty characters, while knowledge-base answers are very short.","百科全书的答案很长，大约 540 个字符，而知识库的答案则非常短。"],[136.03,143.84,12,"The sunburst on the right shows how patient questions typically begin, which gives you a feel for what people actually ask.","右边的旭日图展示了病人提问通常是怎么开头的，让你感受一下人们实际在问什么。"],[144.19,150.02,12,"The point is that real doctor-patient interaction exists at massive scale online.","重点是，真实的医患互动在网上大规模存在。"],[150.37,158.32,12,"That's a resource most general datasets don't have, and it's the raw material for a model that sounds like a doctor.","这是大多数通用数据集所没有的资源，也是训练一个说话像医生的模型的原材料。"],[159.57,164.08,13,"To put that scale in perspective, here's a comparison with other QA datasets.","为了直观感受这个规模，这里把它和其他问答数据集做了对比。"],[164.43,170.46,13,"The medical ones above the bold line range from a few thousand to around a hundred thousand questions.","粗线以上的医学数据集，规模从几千到大约十万个问题不等。"],[170.81,178.78,13,"Huatuo-26M is two orders of magnitude larger than the previous largest medical QA dataset.","Huatuo-26M 比之前最大的医学问答数据集还要大两个数量级。"],[179.13,187.3,13,"Below the line are general-domain datasets, and only PAQ, which is automatically generated from Wikipedia, is bigger.","粗线以下是通用领域的数据集，只有 PAQ 比它更大，而 PAQ 是从维基百科自动生成的。"],[187.65,190.54,13,"The takeaway isn't just bragging about size.","这里的重点不只是炫耀规模。"],[190.89,199.39,13,"With this much real consultation data, you can study things that were impossible before: training retrieval and training generators.","有了这么多真实的问诊数据，你可以研究以前做不到的事情：训练检索模型、训练生成模型。"],[199.74,207.44,13,"And, as we'll see, you can use doctors' answers as references for both fine-tuning and reward signals.","而且，我们后面会看到，还可以把医生的回答作为参考，同时用于微调和奖励信号。"],[208.69,215.86,14,"Here's the overall training recipe for HuatuoGPT, and it should look very familiar from Lectures five and six.","这是 HuatuoGPT 的整体训练方案，大家在第五讲和第六讲应该已经很熟悉了。"],[216.21,219.94,14,"It's the classic three-stage pipeline, adapted to a domain.","它就是经典的三阶段流程，只是针对一个领域做了适配。"],[220.29,222.2,14,"First, a pre-trained backbone.","第一，一个预训练的基座模型。"],[222.55,230.54,14,"We tried several open Chinese-capable models of that time, like Bloom-7B, Ziya-13B and Baichuan.","我们尝试了当时几个支持中文的开源模型，比如 Bloom-7B、Ziya-13B 和 Baichuan。"],[230.89,240.15,14,"And we continued pre-training on about five billion tokens of medical text: textbooks, web data and clinical guidelines.","并在约五十亿 token 的医学文本上做了继续预训练：包括教科书、网络数据和临床指南。"],[240.5,246.32,14,"Second, fine-tuning on a careful mixture of instruction-following data and multi-turn conversations.","第二，在精心混合的指令跟随数据和多轮对话数据上做微调。"],[246.67,254.69,14,"Third, an RLHF-style stage, where ChatGPT gives the feedback but doctors' real answers serve as the reference.","第三，一个类似 RLHF 的阶段，由 ChatGPT 提供反馈，但以医生的真实回答作为参考。"],[255.04,263.56,14,"The interesting design decisions are in the details of stages two and three, so let's look at why we needed them in the first place.","有意思的设计决策都在第二和第三阶段的细节里，那我们先看看最初为什么需要它们。"],[264.81,272.02,15,"Why not simply train on doctors' replies, or simply copy ChatGPT? Let's compare the two directly.","为什么不直接用医生的回复训练，或者直接模仿 ChatGPT？我们来直接对比一下两者。"],[272.37,275.65,15,"Here a user says, I have a stomachache.","这里，用户说：我肚子痛。"],[276.0,284.36,15,"ChatGPT, on the left, gives a long, well-organized answer with bullet points, but it asks no follow-up questions.","左边的 ChatGPT 给出了一个很长、条理清晰、带要点列表的回答，但它没有追问任何问题。"],[284.71,294.17,15,"The doctor, on the right, asks where the pain is, how long it has lasted, and what you ate, and then reaches a diagnosis over several turns.","右边的医生会问疼在哪里、持续多久了、吃了什么，经过几轮对话才得出诊断。"],[294.52,302.08,15,"But doctors' instructions can be very brief: that is fine in spoken communication, but a bit short as written text.","但医生的回复可能非常简短：口头交流时没问题，但作为书面交流就有点太短了。"],[302.43,309.58,15,"Even when a doctor's reply is long, it usually lacks good presentation quality, with no tables or bullet points.","即使医生的回复很长，通常也缺乏好的呈现质量，比如不会用表格和要点列表。"],[309.93,316.76,15,"And doctors' replies often jump straight to conclusions without the intermediate steps, so the reasoning is lost.","而且医生的回复常常很跳跃，直接给结论，没有中间过程，导致推理过程丢失了。"],[317.11,321.33,15,"For example: you are pregnant, take this drug, with no explanation.","比如：你怀孕了，吃这个药，没有任何解释。"],[321.68,330.48,15,"Training only on doctors' data also hurts instruction following: the user asks three questions, and the doctor answers only one of them.","只用医生的数据训练还会损害指令跟随能力：用户问了三个问题，医生只回答了其中一个。"],[330.83,337.33,15,"So ChatGPT is reading-friendly, while doctors are orally-friendly and truly diagnostic.","所以，ChatGPT 适合阅读，而医生适合口头交流，并且真正在做诊断。"],[338.58,342.69,16,"So doctors and ChatGPT have complementary strengths.","所以，医生和 ChatGPT 各有所长，可以互补。"],[343.04,349.01,16,"Doctors ask follow-up questions and carry real expertise, but their replies are short and jumpy.","医生会追问，也具备真正的专业知识，但他们的回复简短又跳跃。"],[349.36,356.03,16,"ChatGPT is well-organized and friendly, but it rarely asks questions and doesn't behave like a doctor.","ChatGPT 条理清晰、态度友好，但很少提问，行为也不像医生。"],[356.38,358.54,16,"The natural idea: combine them.","自然的想法就是：把两者结合起来。"],[358.89,362.14,16,"That's the HuatuoGPT design in one picture.","这张图就是 HuatuoGPT 的整体设计。"],[362.49,367.81,16,"Stage one, on the left in red, is supervised fine-tuning on hybrid data.","第一阶段，左边红色的部分，是在混合数据上做监督微调。"],[368.16,377.22,16,"That means real doctor data polished by an LLM, plus LLM-distilled data that is pushed to behave more like a doctor.","也就是用大模型润色过的真实医生数据，加上被引导得更像医生的大模型蒸馏数据。"],[377.57,386.64,16,"Stage two, on the right in blue, is reinforcement learning from mixed feedback, where both ChatGPT and doctors contribute to the reward.","第二阶段，右边蓝色的部分，是基于混合反馈的强化学习，ChatGPT 和医生都为奖励做出贡献。"],[386.99,389.39,16,"The four checkmarks are the target behaviour.","这四个对勾就是目标行为。"],[389.74,399.3,16,"Doctor-like, patient-friendly, instruction-following, and interactive in diagnosis, meaning it asks questions when information is missing.","像医生、对病人友好、遵循指令，以及在诊断中具有交互性，也就是信息不足时会主动提问。"],[399.65,401.29,16,"Let's look at each stage.","我们逐个来看每个阶段。"],[402.54,406.67,17,"Stage one has four kinds of data, arranged in a two-by-two grid.","第一阶段有四类数据，排成一个二乘二的网格。"],[407.02,413.7,17,"One axis is the source: real-world data from doctors versus distilled data from ChatGPT.","一个维度是来源：来自医生的真实数据，和来自 ChatGPT 的蒸馏数据。"],[414.05,420.34,17,"The other axis is the format: single-turn question answering versus multi-turn diagnostic conversations.","另一个维度是形式：单轮问答，和多轮诊断对话。"],[420.69,424.51,17,"The trick is in the two arrows pointing toward hybrid data.","关键在于指向混合数据的这两个箭头。"],[424.86,432.46,17,"Real doctor data gets LLM-polished, which makes it more patient-friendly: same medical content, better presentation.","真实医生数据经过大模型润色，变得对病人更友好：医学内容不变，呈现更好。"],[432.81,437.86,17,"Distilled ChatGPT data gets role-enhanced, which makes it more like a doctor.","ChatGPT 蒸馏数据经过角色增强，变得更像医生。"],[438.21,443.31,17,"We prompt the LLM to play a specific medical role and to ask follow-up questions.","我们通过提示让大模型扮演特定的医学角色，并主动追问。"],[443.66,446.68,17,"So each source is pushed toward the strengths of the other.","所以，每种来源都被推向另一方的长处。"],[447.03,455.75,17,"The real data brings expertise, the distilled data brings fluency, and after these two transformations they meet in the middle.","真实数据带来专业性，蒸馏数据带来流畅性，经过这两种变换，它们在中间汇合。"],[457.0,459.54,18,"Here's what polishing looks like in practice.","这是润色在实际中的样子。"],[459.89,465.25,18,"We give ChatGPT the patient's question and the doctor's real reply as a reference.","我们把病人的问题和医生的真实回复作为参考，一起交给 ChatGPT。"],[465.6,472.46,18,"And we ask it to answer as HuatuoGPT: like a doctor, gentle and caring, with more detail.","然后让它以 HuatuoGPT 的身份回答：像医生一样，温和而体贴，并且更加详细。"],[472.81,478.39,18,"Importantly, if a diagnosis isn't possible yet, it should ask for more information.","重要的是，如果还无法做出诊断，它应该询问更多信息。"],[478.74,484.08,18,"Why give the doctor's reply as a reference instead of just asking ChatGPT to answer?","为什么要把医生的回复作为参考，而不是直接让 ChatGPT 回答？"],[484.43,487.39,18,"Because the reference anchors the medical content.","因为参考回复锚定了医学内容。"],[487.74,492.68,18,"ChatGPT handles the style: uniform, fluent, instruction-following.","ChatGPT 负责风格：统一、流畅、遵循指令。"],[493.03,498.89,18,"But the substance, what the doctor actually concluded, comes from a real expert.","但实质内容，也就是医生实际得出的结论，来自真正的专家。"],[499.24,503.78,18,"That reduces hallucination compared with pure distillation.","与纯蒸馏相比，这减少了幻觉。"],[504.13,508.14,18,"You can think of it as the LLM rewriting, not inventing.","你可以把它理解为大模型在改写，而不是在编造。"],[509.39,515.39,19,"The other direction is distilled data that we push to be more doctor-like, in two steps.","另一个方向，是把蒸馏数据推得更像医生，分两步进行。"],[515.74,523.61,19,"Step one, on the left, is self-instruct, which you may remember from the instruction-tuning part of Lecture five.","第一步，左边，是 self-instruct，大家可能还记得第五讲指令微调部分讲过它。"],[523.96,530.1,19,"We ask ChatGPT to design diverse triples of role, instruction and input.","我们让 ChatGPT 设计多样化的角色、指令、输入三元组。"],[530.45,538.04,19,"The roles are medical, like a respiratory physician, and the instructions are varied and concrete.","角色都是医学相关的，比如呼吸科医生，而指令则多样而具体。"],[538.39,546.87,19,"Step two, on the right: for each generated question, ChatGPT answers while playing that medical role, patiently and thoroughly.","第二步，右边：对每个生成的问题，ChatGPT 扮演对应的医学角色，耐心而全面地回答。"],[547.22,552.45,19,"It asks follow-up questions when information is missing, and adds advice at the end.","信息不足时它会追问，最后还会补充建议。"],[552.8,554.68,19,"The role is the key ingredient.","角色是关键要素。"],[555.03,557.94,19,"A generic assistant gives a generic answer.","一个通用助手只会给出泛泛的回答。"],[558.29,568.31,19,"Telling the model you are an experienced respiratory physician changes both the content and the behaviour, especially that habit of asking before concluding.","告诉模型你是一位经验丰富的呼吸科医生，会同时改变内容和行为，尤其是先提问再下结论的习惯。"],[569.56,575.26,20,"Here's the final mix in numbers: about two hundred twenty-six thousand examples in total.","这是最终数据混合的具体数字：总共大约二十二万六千条样本。"],[575.61,581.93,20,"Roughly one hundred thirty thousand come from ChatGPT, split between instructions and conversations.","大约十三万条来自 ChatGPT，分为指令和对话两类。"],[582.28,589.54,20,"And about ninety-six thousand come from doctors, again split between single-turn QA and multi-turn conversations.","大约九万六千条来自医生，同样分为单轮问答和多轮对话。"],[589.89,591.03,20,"Two things to notice.","有两点值得注意。"],[591.38,597.04,20,"First, it's fairly balanced between the two sources; we deliberately didn't let one dominate.","第一，两种来源相当均衡；我们刻意不让任何一方占主导。"],[597.39,603.85,20,"Second, compare this with the twenty-six million pairs in Huatuo-26M.","第二，把它和 Huatuo-26M 的两千六百万对比较一下。"],[604.2,610.84,20,"For fine-tuning, a carefully curated couple of hundred thousand examples beats dumping in everything.","对于微调来说，精心挑选的二十来万条样本，胜过把所有数据一股脑倒进去。"],[611.19,616.98,20,"That's a recurring lesson from instruction tuning: quality and diversity matter more than volume.","这是指令微调中反复出现的教训：质量和多样性比数量更重要。"],[618.23,622.58,21,"A small but important engineering detail: how you compute the loss.","一个虽小但很重要的工程细节：如何计算损失。"],[622.93,629.95,21,"In both cases, we compute the loss only on the model's responses, not on the system prompt or the patient's input.","在两种情况下，我们都只在模型的回复上计算损失，而不在系统提示或病人的输入上计算。"],[630.3,633.36,21,"We don't want the model learning to imitate patients.","我们不希望模型学着去模仿病人。"],[633.71,636.24,21,"For single-turn data, that's one response.","对于单轮数据，就是一条回复。"],[636.59,643.84,21,"For multi-turn data, we keep the whole conversation in one sequence and compute the loss on every HuatuoGPT turn at once.","对于多轮数据，我们把整段对话放在一个序列里，一次性在每一轮 HuatuoGPT 的回复上计算损失。"],[644.19,649.49,21,"We don't split a ten-turn conversation into ten separate training examples.","我们不会把一段十轮的对话拆成十个独立的训练样本。"],[649.84,657.65,21,"Splitting would repeat the same context many times, which wastes compute, and it would over-weight the early turns.","拆分会让同样的上下文重复很多次，浪费算力，还会让前面几轮的权重过高。"],[658.0,663.15,21,"Keeping the dialogue intact also teaches the model how a consultation unfolds over time.","保持对话完整，还能教会模型一次问诊是如何随时间展开的。"],[663.5,673.23,21,"And we mix single-turn and multi-turn data in the same training run, so the model learns both to answer directly and to hold a conversation.","而且我们在同一次训练中混合单轮和多轮数据，让模型既学会直接回答，也学会进行对话。"],[674.48,677.01,22,"Now stage two: reinforcement learning.","现在来看第二阶段：强化学习。"],[677.36,679.7,22,"Remember the options from Lecture six.","回忆一下第六讲里的几种选择。"],[680.05,688.13,22,"Classic RLHF uses human preference labels; in medicine those humans need to be doctors, which is expensive and slow.","经典的 RLHF 使用人类偏好标注；在医学中这些人必须是医生，既昂贵又缓慢。"],[688.48,692.98,22,"RLAIF uses an AI judge instead, which is cheap.","RLAIF 则改用 AI 作为评判者，成本很低。"],[693.33,699.13,22,"But in medicine an AI judge can be medically wrong, and its judgments can be unstable.","但在医学中，AI 评判者可能在医学上出错，而且它的判断可能不稳定。"],[699.48,704.88,22,"Our compromise is RLMF, reinforcement learning from mixed feedback.","我们的折中方案是 RLMF，即基于混合反馈的强化学习。"],[705.23,714.14,22,"The judge is still ChatGPT, so it's cheap and scalable, but every judgment is anchored to a real doctor's answer for the same question.","评判者仍然是 ChatGPT，所以成本低、可扩展，但每次评判都锚定在同一问题的真实医生回答上。"],[714.49,718.89,22,"The doctor provides correctness; the AI provides scale.","医生提供正确性，AI 提供规模。"],[719.24,727.0,22,"This pattern, an AI judge grounded in an expert reference, shows up again and again in later medical work.","这种以专家参考为依据的 AI 评判模式，在后来的医学工作中一再出现。"],[727.35,732.21,22,"That includes the rubric-based evaluation you'll see near the end.","包括你们在课程接近尾声时会看到的基于评分细则的评测。"],[733.46,735.95,23,"Here's how the reward model is trained.","下面是奖励模型的训练方式。"],[736.3,741.61,23,"For a question, we sample two responses, A and B, from the fine-tuned model.","对于一个问题，我们从微调后的模型中采样两个回复，A 和 B。"],[741.96,751.07,23,"ChatGPT scores both on a one-to-ten scale, considering accuracy, conciseness and similarity to the doctor's standard answer.","ChatGPT 按一到十分给两个回复打分，考虑准确性、简洁性，以及与医生标准答案的相似度。"],[751.42,753.1,23,"The full prompt is on the right.","完整的提示词在右边。"],[753.45,759.1,23,"Look at the diagram: we ask twice, once with A first and once with B first.","看这张图：我们问两次，一次 A 在前，一次 B 在前。"],[759.45,765.23,23,"LLM judges have a known position bias; they tend to prefer whichever answer comes first.","大模型评判者有一个众所周知的位置偏差：它们倾向于偏好排在前面的那个答案。"],[765.58,771.73,23,"So we keep a preference pair only if both orderings agree; that's the agreement box in the middle.","所以只有当两种顺序的判断一致时，我们才保留这个偏好对，这就是中间的“一致”框。"],[772.08,778.21,23,"Those consistent pairs train a reward model, and the reward model then drives PPO.","这些一致的偏好对用来训练奖励模型，然后由奖励模型驱动 PPO。"],[778.56,787.0,23,"This order-swapping trick is cheap, and you should use it any time you build an LLM-as-judge pipeline, including in your projects.","这个交换顺序的技巧成本很低，只要你搭建以大模型为评判者的流程，包括在你们的项目中，都应该用上它。"],[788.25,792.45,24,"And here's what the reward looks like during PPO training.","这是 PPO 训练过程中奖励的变化情况。"],[792.8,799.74,24,"On the left, mean reward rises from about zero to above one over roughly fifteen thousand steps.","左边，平均奖励在大约一万五千步内从零左右上升到一以上。"],[800.09,804.72,24,"It's noisy, as RL curves always are, but the trend is clear.","曲线有噪声，强化学习的曲线总是这样，但趋势很清楚。"],[805.07,811.72,24,"On the right are samples logged during training, in Chinese: the prompt, the model's output, and the reward.","右边是训练中记录的中文样本：提示、模型输出和奖励值。"],[812.07,819.89,24,"Higher-reward answers tend to address the patient directly, explain the likely condition, and give concrete treatment considerations.","奖励更高的回答往往会直接回应病人，解释可能的病情，并给出具体的治疗考虑。"],[820.24,822.4,24,"And they close with a caring sentence.","并且以一句关怀的话结尾。"],[822.75,827.79,24,"That's the behaviour we wanted from mixing doctor correctness with ChatGPT style.","这正是我们希望通过结合医生的正确性和 ChatGPT 的风格所得到的行为。"],[828.14,834.75,24,"One caution from Lecture six applies here: a rising reward means the model is pleasing the reward model.","第六讲中的一个提醒在这里同样适用：奖励上升，只说明模型在讨好奖励模型。"],[835.1,841.45,24,"Whether it's actually a better doctor needs separate evaluation, which is exactly where we go next.","它是否真的成了更好的医生，需要单独评测，而这正是我们接下来要讲的。"],[842.7,845.14,25,"For completeness, here are the training details.","为了完整起见，这里列出训练细节。"],[845.49,856.36,25,"The final model was built on Ziya-LLaMA-13B, implemented in PyTorch with Hugging Face Accelerate and the trlx library for RL.","最终模型基于 Ziya-LLaMA-13B 构建，用 PyTorch 实现，并使用 Hugging Face 的 Accelerate 和用于强化学习的 trlx 库。"],[856.71,862.11,25,"And it was trained with ZeRO across eight A100 eighty-gigabyte GPUs.","并使用 ZeRO 策略在八张 80G 显存的 A100 GPU 上训练。"],[862.46,871.46,25,"For SFT: learning rate five times ten to the minus five, batch size one hundred twenty-eight, context length two thousand forty-eight.","SFT 阶段：学习率为 5e-5，批大小为 128，上下文长度为 2048。"],[871.81,878.09,25,"For RLMF: a much smaller learning rate of ten to the minus six, and a rollout size of sixty-four.","RLMF 阶段：学习率小得多，为 1e-6，rollout 大小为 64。"],[878.44,888.58,25,"And a KL coefficient of zero point one, the term that keeps the policy from drifting too far from the SFT model, as you saw in Lecture six.","KL 系数为 0.1，正如第六讲所讲，这一项防止策略偏离 SFT 模型太远。"],[888.93,891.77,25,"The thing to notice is the budget. Eight GPUs.","需要注意的是预算：只有八张 GPU。"],[892.12,895.97,25,"This is academic-scale work, which supports the earlier argument.","这是学术规模的工作，它印证了前面的观点。"],[896.32,901.52,25,"In a focused domain, a small lab can still build something useful and competitive.","在一个聚焦的领域里，一个小实验室依然可以做出有用且有竞争力的东西。"]]},{"n":3,"title":"How Do We Evaluate a Medical LLM?","blurb":"Single-turn and multi-turn tests, human evaluation, the CMB benchmark and its leaderboard, and an expert consistency study exposing the limits of current evaluation.","file":"lecture09_part3.mp4","poster":"lecture09_part3.jpg","duration":777.8,"first":26,"last":40,"slides":[{"n":26,"title":"2.2 How Do We Evaluate a Medical LLM?","t":0.8},{"n":27,"title":"Evaluation: Single-Turn Questions","t":28.35},{"n":28,"title":"Single-Turn Questions in 10 Intents","t":69.19},{"n":29,"title":"Single-Turn Results","t":124.85},{"n":30,"title":"Evaluation: Multi-Turn Conversations","t":190.65},{"n":31,"title":"Multi-Turn Results","t":240.99},{"n":32,"title":"Human Evaluation","t":289.77},{"n":33,"title":"Medical QA Benchmarks","t":340.94},{"n":34,"title":"CMB: A Comprehensive Medical Benchmark in Chinese","t":399.7},{"n":35,"title":"CMB Online Leaderboard","t":459.4},{"n":36,"title":"How to Evaluate Medical LLMs?","t":509.61},{"n":37,"title":"Expert Consistency Study with Medlinker (1)","t":565.26},{"n":38,"title":"Expert Consistency Study with Medlinker (2)","t":619.05},{"n":39,"title":"Limitations of Current Evaluation","t":670.94},{"n":40,"title":"Insights for Future Evaluation","t":722.21}],"sents":[[0.8,6.14,26,"We've built the model; the obvious next question is whether it's any good.","模型已经建好了，接下来显而易见的问题是：它到底好不好？"],[6.49,9.11,26,"This turned out to be much harder than we expected.","事实证明，这比我们预想的要难得多。"],[9.46,19.31,26,"Leaderboards saturate and leak into training data, doctors disagree with each other, and real medicine is interactive rather than a one-shot answer.","排行榜会饱和，还会泄漏进训练数据；医生之间意见不一；而且真实的医疗是交互式的，而不是一次性的回答。"],[19.66,26.95,26,"In this part I'll show how we evaluated HuatuoGPT, and why evaluation became a research problem in its own right.","这一部分，我会展示我们如何评测 HuatuoGPT，以及为什么评测本身成了一个研究问题。"],[28.2,33.57,27,"We started with single-turn questions, following the pairwise setup popularized by Vicuna.","我们从单轮问题开始，沿用 Vicuna 推广的成对比较设置。"],[33.92,39.97,27,"Take one question, send it to two models, get two answers, and ask a judge which one is better.","拿一个问题，发给两个模型，得到两个答案，再请评判者判断哪个更好。"],[40.32,44.77,27,"We used two kinds of judges: GPT-4 and real doctors.","我们使用了两类评判者：GPT-4 和真实的医生。"],[45.12,49.98,27,"GPT-4 is cheap and fast; doctors are the ground truth but expensive.","GPT-4 便宜又快；医生是金标准，但很昂贵。"],[50.33,55.58,27,"Running both lets you check whether the cheap judge agrees with the expensive one.","两者都用，就可以检验便宜的评判者是否与昂贵的评判者一致。"],[55.93,60.6,27,"Pairwise comparison is also easier for humans than absolute scoring.","对人来说，成对比较也比绝对打分更容易。"],[60.95,67.79,27,"It's hard to say whether an answer is a seven or an eight, but much easier to say which of two is better.","很难说一个答案该打七分还是八分，但要说两个答案中哪个更好就容易多了。"],[69.04,70.87,28,"Which questions did we use?","我们用了哪些问题？"],[71.22,80.13,28,"We wanted coverage of what patients actually ask, so we took the ten intent categories from KUAKE-QIC in the CBLUE benchmark.","我们希望覆盖病人真正会问的问题，因此采用了 CBLUE 基准中 KUAKE-QIC 的十个意图类别。"],[80.48,91.37,28,"Diagnosis, etiology, treatment, care advice, lab interpretation, disease description, consequences, precautions, effects and costs.","诊断、病因、治疗、就医建议、化验解读、疾病描述、后果、注意事项、功效和费用。"],[91.72,93.96,28,"Each has an example on the slide.","每一类在这里都有一个例子。"],[94.31,102.57,28,"What does an elevated hs-CRP mean is lab interpretation; how much does metformin cost is costs.","“超敏 C 反应蛋白升高意味着什么”属于化验解读；“二甲双胍多少钱”属于费用。"],[102.92,114.05,28,"The pipeline on the right: start from the validation set, rank candidate questions with ChatGPT, filter by hand, and end up with one hundred questions.","右边的流程是：从验证集出发，用 ChatGPT 对候选问题排序，再人工筛选，最终得到一百个问题。"],[114.4,119.25,28,"One hundred is small, but each comparison involves careful judging by doctors.","一百个问题不算多，但每一次比较都需要医生仔细评判。"],[119.6,123.45,28,"So the bottleneck is human effort, not question supply.","所以瓶颈在于人力，而不是问题的来源。"],[124.7,126.68,29,"Here are the single-turn results.","这是单轮问题的结果。"],[127.03,131.28,29,"Left is GPT-4 as judge, right is doctors as judge.","左边是 GPT-4 作为评判者，右边是医生作为评判者。"],[131.63,136.3,29,"Green means HuatuoGPT wins, orange is a tie, red is a loss.","绿色表示 HuatuoGPT 胜，橙色表示平局，红色表示负。"],[136.65,142.98,29,"Against earlier Chinese medical models like BenTsao and DoctorGLM, HuatuoGPT wins almost everything.","对比早期的中文医学模型，比如 BenTsao 和 DoctorGLM，HuatuoGPT 几乎全胜。"],[143.33,149.86,29,"Against ChatGPT it wins more than it loses, forty-seven to thirty-two under GPT-4.","对比 ChatGPT，它胜多负少，在 GPT-4 评判下是 47 比 32。"],[150.21,155.27,29,"And it's roughly even under doctors, thirty-five to thirty-three.","在医生评判下大致持平，35 比 33。"],[155.62,162.56,29,"Against GPT-4 it clearly loses, about thirty-one to fifty-two, and twenty-two to fifty-four.","对比 GPT-4，它明显落败，大约 31 比 52，以及 22 比 54。"],[162.91,163.72,29,"Two lessons.","有两点启示。"],[164.07,171.82,29,"First, a thirteen-billion-parameter model with good domain data can match ChatGPT on this kind of question, but not GPT-4.","第一，一个拥有优质领域数据的 130 亿参数模型，在这类问题上可以媲美 ChatGPT，但比不上 GPT-4。"],[172.17,179.99,29,"Second, look at how GPT-4's judgments and the doctors' judgments line up in direction across the rows.","第二，看看 GPT-4 的判断和医生的判断在各行上的方向是多么一致。"],[180.34,189.25,29,"That agreement is what gives us some confidence in using GPT-4 as a cheaper judge, though not as a replacement for doctors.","正是这种一致性，让我们有一定信心把 GPT-4 当作更便宜的评判者，但它不能取代医生。"],[190.5,195.18,30,"Single-turn questions miss what makes doctors doctors: the back-and-forth.","单轮问题缺失了医生之所以为医生的关键：来回的交流。"],[195.53,199.86,30,"So we also evaluated multi-turn consultations.","所以我们还评测了多轮问诊。"],[200.21,202.89,30,"The setup: start from a patient case.","设置是这样的：从一个病例出发。"],[203.24,209.88,30,"ChatGPT plays the patient, using the case information, and the model under test plays the doctor.","ChatGPT 根据病例信息扮演病人，被测模型扮演医生。"],[210.23,214.06,30,"They talk for several turns, producing a full conversation.","它们交谈若干轮，生成一段完整的对话。"],[214.41,221.12,30,"Do the same with a second model on the same case, and then GPT-4 or doctors compare the two whole conversations.","对同一病例用第二个模型重复这个过程，然后由 GPT-4 或医生比较这两段完整的对话。"],[221.47,227.04,30,"This is an early version of the simulated-patient idea that will come back in a big way later.","这是模拟病人这一思路的早期版本，后面它会以更重要的形式回归。"],[227.39,231.49,30,"That's when we talk about scaling standardized patients and environments.","也就是当我们讨论规模化的标准化病人和环境的时候。"],[231.84,239.59,30,"Here it's just an evaluation tool, but notice that once you have a simulated patient, you've built a tiny environment.","在这里它只是一个评测工具，但请注意，一旦有了模拟病人，你就已经搭建了一个微型环境。"],[240.84,246.96,31,"In multi-turn conversations HuatuoGPT does even better relative to the baselines.","在多轮对话中，HuatuoGPT 相对于基线模型表现得更好。"],[247.31,254.63,31,"Against DoctorGLM it wins about ninety-seven percent under GPT-4 and ninety-six percent under doctors.","对比 DoctorGLM，在 GPT-4 评判下胜率约为百分之九十七，在医生评判下为百分之九十六。"],[254.98,263.36,31,"Against ChatGPT it wins sixty-two percent under GPT-4 and fifty-four percent under doctors, with only about thirty percent losses.","对比 ChatGPT，在 GPT-4 评判下胜率为百分之六十二，医生评判下为百分之五十四，负的比例只有约百分之三十。"],[263.71,267.35,31,"Why is the gap bigger here than in single-turn?","为什么这里的差距比单轮问题更大？"],[267.7,272.98,31,"Because this is exactly where the doctor data and role-play training pay off.","因为这正是医生数据和角色扮演训练发挥作用的地方。"],[273.33,282.05,31,"HuatuoGPT asks follow-up questions and gathers information like a doctor, while ChatGPT tends to dump a long generic answer in the first turn.","HuatuoGPT 会像医生一样追问、收集信息，而 ChatGPT 往往在第一轮就抛出一大段泛泛的回答。"],[282.4,288.37,31,"So the training design shows up directly in the evaluation that most resembles real consultation.","所以，训练设计的效果直接体现在最接近真实问诊的那项评测中。"],[289.62,293.5,32,"Here's what the human evaluation looked like in practice.","这是人工评测在实际中的样子。"],[293.85,303.48,32,"On the left is the annotation interface: a doctor sees a patient question and two anonymous model answers, and picks A, B or a tie.","左边是标注界面：医生看到一个病人的问题和两个匿名模型的回答，然后选择 A 更好、B 更好或平局。"],[303.83,308.68,32,"The guidelines at the top tell doctors to penalize vague, generic replies.","顶部的标注指南要求医生给笼统、泛化的回答打低分。"],[309.03,315.99,32,"They reward answers that act like a real consultation, including asking the patient questions.","并奖励那些像真实问诊一样的回答，包括会向病人提问的回答。"],[316.34,320.62,32,"And they consider richness, professional accuracy and a warm tone.","同时还要考虑回答的丰富度、专业准确性和温暖的语气。"],[320.97,326.54,32,"On the right is the doctors' verdict on the multi-turn comparison, the same chart you just saw.","右边是医生对多轮对比的评判结果，就是你们刚才看到的那张图。"],[326.89,331.55,32,"I show it because people often ask what doctor evaluation means concretely.","我之所以展示它，是因为大家经常问医生评测具体指的是什么。"],[331.9,339.54,32,"It means real doctors, a fixed rubric, blind comparison, and a lot of patient, expensive work.","它意味着真实的医生、固定的评分细则、盲评对比，以及大量耐心而昂贵的工作。"],[340.79,351.41,33,"Besides pairwise judging, we also ran HuatuoGPT on existing Chinese medical QA benchmarks: cMedQA2, webMedQA and Huatuo-26M.","除了成对评判，我们还在已有的中文医学问答基准上测试了 HuatuoGPT：cMedQA2、webMedQA 和 Huatuo-26M。"],[351.76,357.09,33,"We used classic automatic metrics like BLEU, ROUGE and Distinct.","使用的是经典的自动指标，比如 BLEU、ROUGE 和 Distinct。"],[357.44,361.68,33,"HuatuoGPT is the best among the LLMs on most columns.","在大多数列上，HuatuoGPT 都是大模型中最好的。"],[362.03,370.94,33,"But look at the fine-tuned T5 rows: a small model trained directly on each dataset often scores higher on BLEU and ROUGE.","但看看微调后的 T5 这几行：一个直接在各数据集上训练的小模型，BLEU 和 ROUGE 分数往往更高。"],[371.29,374.55,33,"Does that mean T5 is a better doctor? Of course not.","这是否意味着 T5 是更好的医生？当然不是。"],[374.9,380.19,33,"N-gram metrics reward copying the short, terse wording of the reference answer.","n-gram 指标奖励的是照搬参考答案那种简短、简练的措辞。"],[380.54,385.83,33,"And a chat model that explains more and asks questions gets penalized for it.","而一个解释更多、会提问的对话模型反而因此被扣分。"],[386.18,391.52,33,"That's the lesson: overlap metrics from machine translation are a poor fit for medical dialogue.","这就是教训：来自机器翻译的重叠类指标并不适合医疗对话。"],[391.87,398.3,33,"We needed benchmarks that test knowledge and clinical reasoning directly, which brings us to CMB.","我们需要能直接考察知识和临床推理的基准，这就引出了 CMB。"],[399.55,404.52,34,"CMB, a Comprehensive Medical Benchmark in Chinese, has two parts.","CMB，即中文综合医学基准，包含两个部分。"],[404.87,411.4,34,"On the left, CMB-Exam: multiple-choice questions taken from real Chinese professional exams.","左边是 CMB-Exam：取自中国真实职业考试的选择题。"],[411.75,423.03,34,"They are organized by profession, physicians, nurses, pharmacists and technicians, plus medical disciplines and graduate entrance exams, and by career stage.","它们按职业组织，包括医师、护士、药师、技师，还有医学学科和研究生入学考试，并按职业阶段划分。"],[423.38,427.76,34,"It tests breadth of knowledge the way the medical system itself tests people.","它以医疗体系考核人的方式，来测试知识的广度。"],[428.11,433.71,34,"On the right, CMB-Clin: real, complex clinical cases.","右边是 CMB-Clin：真实而复杂的临床病例。"],[434.06,440.72,34,"Each has a description, with the chief complaint, physical exam, and lab and imaging results.","每个病例都有一段描述，包含主诉、体格检查，以及化验和影像结果。"],[441.07,449.05,34,"That's followed by a sequence of questions: analyze the history, give a diagnosis with its basis, then the treatment principles.","接着是一系列问题：分析病史，给出诊断及其依据，然后是治疗原则。"],[449.4,453.44,34,"That's closer to how a clinician actually thinks through a case.","这更接近临床医生实际分析病例的思路。"],[453.79,458.0,34,"Together, the two parts measure knowledge and its application.","两部分合在一起，衡量的是知识及其应用。"],[459.25,466.36,35,"We put CMB online as a public leaderboard, and many companies started using it to report their models.","我们把 CMB 放到网上，做成公开排行榜，很多公司开始用它来报告自己的模型。"],[466.71,472.8,35,"Columns are different exam types, physician and nursing exams at different levels, and rows are models.","列是不同类型的考试，包括不同级别的医师考试和护理考试，行则是各个模型。"],[473.15,476.09,35,"Here's an uncomfortable detail I want you to see.","这里有一个让人不太舒服的细节，我想让大家看看。"],[476.44,483.84,35,"In this snapshot GPT-4 scored about fifty-eight on average, while our original HuatuoGPT scored about thirty-one.","在这个快照中，GPT-4 的平均分约为 58，而我们最初的 HuatuoGPT 只有约 31。"],[484.19,489.29,35,"Remember, HuatuoGPT beat ChatGPT in the conversational comparisons.","要记得，HuatuoGPT 在对话对比中是赢了 ChatGPT 的。"],[489.64,492.75,35,"Yet on a knowledge exam it falls well behind.","然而在知识考试中，它却远远落后。"],[493.1,497.63,35,"So HuatuoGPT talked like a doctor but didn't know enough medicine.","所以，HuatuoGPT 说话像医生，但医学知识却不够。"],[497.98,502.25,35,"Style isn't knowledge, and conversational win rates can hide that.","风格不等于知识，而对话中的胜率可能会掩盖这一点。"],[502.6,508.21,35,"This finding is what led directly to HuatuoGPT-II, which we'll see in a moment.","正是这个发现，直接催生了 HuatuoGPT-II，我们马上就会看到。"],[509.46,514.39,36,"Let's step back and organize the evaluation methods we've seen. There are two families.","我们退一步，把看过的评测方法梳理一下。它们分为两大类。"],[514.74,524.2,36,"On the left, evaluation without a reference answer: you show a judge two responses, or one response, and ask for a judgment.","左边是没有参考答案的评测：给评判者看两个回答或一个回答，请它作出判断。"],[524.55,529.35,36,"The judge can be GPT-4, cheap but possibly biased.","评判者可以是 GPT-4，便宜但可能有偏差。"],[529.7,535.27,36,"Or doctors, trustworthy but expensive and not always consistent with each other.","也可以是医生，值得信赖但昂贵，而且彼此之间未必一致。"],[535.62,543.4,36,"On the right, evaluation with a reference: large-scale benchmarks with known answers, like CMB-Exam.","右边是有参考答案的评测：拥有已知答案的大规模基准，比如 CMB-Exam。"],[543.75,551.08,36,"Scalable and reproducible, but limited to questions with clear right answers, and vulnerable to data leakage.","它可扩展、可复现，但仅限于有明确正确答案的问题，而且容易受到数据泄漏的影响。"],[551.43,556.21,36,"Each family covers the other's blind spot, so in practice you need both.","每一类都能弥补另一类的盲区，所以在实践中两者都需要。"],[556.56,563.86,36,"Next, I want to show you what the most expensive end of the spectrum looks like: a real study with doctors and patients.","接下来，我想给大家看看最昂贵的那一端是什么样子：一项有真实医生和病人参与的研究。"],[565.11,571.69,37,"This is a study by Medlinker, a Chinese medical company, on their model MedGPT, not ours.","这是中国医疗公司医联针对他们自己的模型 MedGPT 做的研究，不是我们的。"],[572.04,576.53,37,"I include it because it's one of the most careful real-world evaluations I've seen.","我之所以放进来，是因为它是我见过的最严谨的真实世界评测之一。"],[576.88,578.2,37,"Here is the design.","这是研究的设计。"],[578.55,580.49,37,"Real patients consult online.","真实的病人在线上问诊。"],[580.84,588.68,37,"An intern doctor acts as an interface, relaying between the patient and either a real doctor or MedGPT.","一名实习医生充当中间人，在病人与真实医生或 MedGPT 之间传递信息。"],[589.03,594.63,37,"The real doctors span a range: attending, associate chief and chief physicians.","真实医生覆盖了不同级别：主治医师、副主任医师和主任医师。"],[594.98,600.03,37,"They work at secondary hospitals, tertiary hospitals and top-ten tertiary hospitals.","他们来自二级医院、三甲医院和排名前十的三甲医院。"],[600.38,604.27,37,"A committee of experts then rates the consultation results.","然后由专家委员会对问诊结果进行评议。"],[604.62,612.19,37,"This is basically a clinical-trial-style comparison: real patients, real doctors as controls, blinded expert review.","这基本上是一种临床试验式的对比：真实病人、真实医生作为对照、专家盲评。"],[612.54,617.65,37,"It's the gold standard, and it's very expensive, as you'll see from the numbers on the next slide.","这是金标准，而且非常昂贵，下一页的数字会让你们看到这一点。"],[618.9,620.52,38,"Here are the results.","这是结果。"],[620.87,627.51,38,"Overall, MedGPT scored seven point two, while the real doctors in the comparison scored seven point five.","总体上，MedGPT 得分 7.2，而对照组的真实医生得分 7.5。"],[627.86,629.98,38,"So it's close, but not equal.","所以很接近，但并不相等。"],[630.33,636.92,38,"Broken down by dimension, it's best at natural-language consultation and interaction, eight point zero.","按维度拆分来看，它最擅长的是自然语言问诊与交互，得分 8.0。"],[637.27,641.1,38,"And it's weaker at treatment recommendations, six point seven.","而在治疗建议上较弱，得分 6.7。"],[641.45,648.42,38,"By department, it ranges from six point zero in geriatric respiratory medicine to eight point four in urology.","按科室来看，从老年呼吸科的 6.0 到泌尿外科的 8.4 不等。"],[648.77,655.18,38,"Now look at the bottom right: ninety-one patients, ten doctors, seven expert reviewers.","再看右下角：91 名病人、10 名医生、7 名评审专家。"],[655.53,660.24,38,"That's a lot of effort for ninety-one patients, and it's still a small sample.","为了 91 名病人花了这么多精力，而且样本量依然很小。"],[660.59,663.46,38,"That's the fundamental tension in medical evaluation.","这就是医学评测中的根本矛盾。"],[663.81,669.54,38,"The most trustworthy method doesn't scale, and the scalable methods aren't fully trustworthy.","最值得信赖的方法无法规模化，而可规模化的方法又不完全值得信赖。"],[670.79,676.4,39,"Let me summarize the limitations of current evaluation, because they define the research agenda.","我来总结一下当前评测的局限，因为它们决定了研究的方向。"],[676.75,682.99,39,"LLMs complement doctors rather than replace them, so beat the doctor may be the wrong framing.","大模型是辅助医生而不是取代医生，所以“打败医生”可能是一个错误的提法。"],[683.34,690.46,39,"Clinical practice is multimodal: images, signals, physical exams. But most benchmarks are text-only.","临床实践是多模态的：影像、信号、体格检查。但大多数基准只有文本。"],[690.81,695.0,39,"Diagnosis is interactive and happens under incomplete information.","诊断是交互式的，而且是在信息不完整的情况下进行的。"],[695.35,700.34,39,"But most benchmarks hand the model a complete vignette and ask for one answer.","但大多数基准给模型一个完整的病例描述，只要一个答案。"],[700.69,707.52,39,"Medical knowledge is specialized and hard to verify, so even building good test questions needs experts.","医学知识高度专业、难以验证，所以即使是构建好的测试题也需要专家。"],[707.87,714.93,39,"And human evaluation is costly, subjective and hard to reproduce, as the ninety-one-patient study showed.","而人工评测成本高、主观且难以复现，正如那项 91 名病人的研究所显示的。"],[715.28,720.81,39,"Every one of these points will come back later in the lecture with a proposed fix.","这里的每一点，在后面的课程中都会再次出现，并给出相应的解决思路。"],[722.06,726.3,40,"So what should future evaluation look like? Four properties.","那么未来的评测应该是什么样的？有四个特性。"],[726.65,733.64,40,"It should be difficult enough to require complex diagnostic reasoning, not something top models already saturate.","它应该足够难，需要复杂的诊断推理，而不是顶尖模型已经刷满分的东西。"],[733.99,742.13,40,"It should be multimodal: X-ray, CT, fMRI, EEG, audio, because that's what clinicians actually look at.","它应该是多模态的：X 光、CT、功能磁共振、脑电、音频，因为这些才是临床医生实际要看的。"],[742.48,748.04,40,"It should be free of data leakage, so models can't have seen the test questions during pre-training.","它应该没有数据泄漏，保证模型在预训练时不可能见过测试题。"],[748.39,753.85,40,"And it should be automatic and open, but built on experts' subjective experience.","而且它应该是自动化、开放的，但建立在专家的主观经验之上。"],[754.2,759.8,40,"That last point sounds contradictory, but OpenAI's HealthBench shows how to do it.","最后一点听起来自相矛盾，但 OpenAI 的 HealthBench 展示了如何做到。"],[760.15,766.73,40,"Doctors write detailed rubrics for each case, and then a model grades responses against those rubrics.","医生为每个病例撰写详细的评分细则，然后由模型依据这些细则给回答打分。"],[767.08,771.43,40,"Expert judgment is captured once and then applied at scale.","专家的判断只需采集一次，就能大规模应用。"],[771.78,775.9,40,"Keep rubrics in mind; they'll come back as a reward signal for training, too.","请记住评分细则，它们之后还会作为训练的奖励信号再次出现。"]]},{"n":4,"title":"HuatuoGPT-II and the Idea of Generalist Medical AI","blurb":"Injecting medical knowledge with HuatuoGPT-II, lessons from a fresh pharmacist exam, and what a language-centric generalist medical AI ladder looks like.","file":"lecture09_part4.mp4","poster":"lecture09_part4.jpg","duration":571.5,"first":41,"last":51,"slides":[{"n":41,"title":"2.3 HuatuoGPT-II: Injecting Medical Knowledge","t":0.8},{"n":42,"title":"HuatuoGPT-II: Methodology","t":27.22},{"n":43,"title":"HuatuoGPT-II: State of the Art for a While","t":98.59},{"n":44,"title":"2024 Pharmacist Exam: Rethinking an Evolving Exam","t":159.17},{"n":45,"title":"What HuatuoGPT Taught Us","t":225.47},{"n":46,"title":"3 What Is Generalist Medical AI?","t":286.1},{"n":47,"title":"What Is Generalist Medical AI (GMAI)?","t":312.69},{"n":48,"title":"Why Is Generalist Medical AI Language-Centric?","t":371.29},{"n":49,"title":"GMAI: Top-Down or Bottom-Up?","t":421.65},{"n":50,"title":"A Ladder towards Generalist Medical AI","t":472.58},{"n":51,"title":"Roadmap to Generalist Medical AI","t":530.97}],"sents":[[0.8,6.67,41,"That closes our evaluation detour, and it left us with an uncomfortable finding.","评测这段插曲到此结束，它给我们留下了一个令人不安的发现。"],[7.02,11.81,41,"The first HuatuoGPT talked like a doctor but failed licensing exams.","第一代 HuatuoGPT 说话像医生，却通不过执业资格考试。"],[12.16,15.47,41,"Knowledge has to go into the model, not only style.","知识必须进入模型，而不仅仅是风格。"],[15.82,18.26,41,"HuatuoGPT-II was our answer.","HuatuoGPT-II 就是我们的答案。"],[18.61,25.82,41,"How do you inject a large amount of medical knowledge efficiently, without breaking the model's ability to follow instructions?","如何高效地注入大量医学知识，同时又不破坏模型遵循指令的能力？"],[27.07,34.42,42,"The standard way to add domain knowledge is two stages: continue pre-training on domain text, then fine-tune on instructions.","注入领域知识的标准做法分两个阶段：先在领域文本上继续预训练，再在指令数据上微调。"],[34.77,39.26,42,"The problem is that the two stages have very different data distributions.","问题在于，这两个阶段的数据分布差别很大。"],[39.61,47.51,42,"Pre-training text is raw prose, fine-tuning data is question-answer pairs, and switching between them causes instability and forgetting.","预训练文本是原始的文章，微调数据是问答对，在两者之间切换会导致不稳定和遗忘。"],[47.86,52.6,42,"HuatuoGPT-II's idea is to unify everything into one format.","HuatuoGPT-II 的思路是把所有数据统一成一种格式。"],[52.95,62.16,42,"Start from about one point one terabytes of Chinese and English medical text: books, web pages, encyclopedias and literature.","从大约 1.1TB 的中英文医学文本出发：包括书籍、网页、百科全书和医学文献。"],[62.51,72.56,42,"Use an LLM to rewrite that raw text into instruction-style question-answer pairs, about five point two five million of them, while keeping the knowledge.","用大模型把这些原始文本改写成指令式的问答对，大约五百二十五万条，同时保留其中的知识。"],[72.91,79.4,42,"Separately, we have one hundred forty-two thousand real medical questions answered by GPT-4.","另外，我们还有十四万二千个真实的医学问题，由 GPT-4 来回答。"],[79.75,82.76,42,"Then train on both together in a single stage.","然后把两者放在一起，在单一阶段中训练。"],[83.11,89.4,42,"We use a sampling schedule that shifts from the knowledge-heavy data toward the fine-tuning data over time.","采用一种采样调度，随着训练推进，从以知识为主的数据逐渐转向微调数据。"],[89.75,97.19,42,"The key move is converting pre-training data into the same input-output format as fine-tuning data, so there's no distribution jump.","关键一步是把预训练数据转换成和微调数据相同的输入输出格式，这样就不会出现分布跳变。"],[98.44,99.49,43,"And it worked.","而且它奏效了。"],[99.84,109.56,43,"This table is from the twenty twenty-three Chinese pharmacist licensure exam, both the Western pharmacy track and the traditional Chinese medicine track.","这张表来自 2023 年的中国执业药师资格考试，包括西药和中药两个方向。"],[109.91,117.06,43,"The original HuatuoGPT averages about twenty-four, barely above guessing, which confirms what CMB told us.","最初的 HuatuoGPT 平均只有约 24 分，勉强高于瞎猜，这印证了 CMB 告诉我们的结论。"],[117.41,125.89,43,"HuatuoGPT-II at thirty-four billion parameters averages sixty-four, well ahead of GPT-4's forty-eight.","340 亿参数的 HuatuoGPT-II 平均得分 64，远超 GPT-4 的 48。"],[126.24,129.47,43,"Even the 7B version is close to GPT-4.","即使是 7B 版本也接近 GPT-4。"],[129.82,135.84,43,"Now the methodological point, at the bottom of the slide, which matters more than the numbers.","现在来看底部这条方法论上的要点，它比数字本身更重要。"],[136.19,144.49,43,"This exam was held in October twenty twenty-three, after our model was trained, so the questions could not have leaked into the training data.","这场考试在 2023 年 10 月举行，在我们的模型训练完成之后，所以试题不可能泄漏进训练数据。"],[144.84,149.16,43,"A fresh exam is one of the cleanest ways to test an LLM.","一场全新的考试，是测试大模型最干净的方法之一。"],[149.51,157.77,43,"Remember this when you design your own evaluations: if you can find test data created after your model's training cutoff, use it.","大家设计自己的评测时请记住：如果能找到在模型训练截止之后才产生的测试数据，就用它。"],[159.02,164.53,44,"A year later we repeated the experiment on the twenty twenty-four pharmacist exam.","一年后，我们在 2024 年的药师考试上重复了这个实验。"],[164.88,178.57,44,"Last year's HuatuoGPT2-34B still passes and stays slightly ahead of GPT-4o, zero point six eight four versus zero point six seven six on average.","去年的 HuatuoGPT2-34B 依然能通过考试，并且略微领先 GPT-4o，平均分 0.684 对 0.676。"],[178.92,190.25,44,"But look at the bottom row: Qwen2.5-72B, a general-purpose model, now scores about seventy-seven percent, clearly the best.","但看最下面一行：通用模型 Qwen2.5-72B 现在的得分约为百分之七十七，明显是最好的。"],[190.6,200.15,44,"Models like LLaMA-3.1-70B and Claude do only moderately, especially on traditional Chinese medicine.","LLaMA-3.1-70B 和 Claude 这类模型表现一般，尤其是在中药方面。"],[200.5,205.08,44,"The honest lesson: a domain advantage built on data is temporary.","坦白说，教训是：建立在数据上的领域优势是暂时的。"],[205.43,210.87,44,"General models keep absorbing more medical knowledge, and within a year or so they catch up.","通用模型不断吸收更多的医学知识，大约一年左右就能追上来。"],[211.22,214.63,44,"So simply adding domain knowledge isn't a long-term moat.","所以，仅仅增加领域知识并不能构成长期的护城河。"],[214.98,224.07,44,"That realization is part of why we later moved toward reasoning, multimodality and, eventually, environments.","正是这一认识，促使我们后来转向推理、多模态，并最终走向环境。"],[225.32,229.05,45,"Let me close the HuatuoGPT story with four lessons.","我用四条经验来结束 HuatuoGPT 的故事。"],[229.4,231.39,45,"Data must look like doctors.","数据必须像医生。"],[231.74,238.39,45,"Real doctor replies carry expertise, LLM-distilled replies carry patience and structure; mix both.","真实医生的回复带有专业性，大模型蒸馏的回复带有耐心和结构；两者要混合。"],[238.74,240.41,45,"Knowledge must be injected.","知识必须被注入。"],[240.76,249.27,45,"Style without knowledge fails licensing exams, and HuatuoGPT-II solved that by unifying pre-training and fine-tuning.","只有风格没有知识，就通不过执业考试，HuatuoGPT-II 通过统一预训练和微调解决了这个问题。"],[249.62,251.91,45,"Evaluation is a research problem.","评测本身是一个研究问题。"],[252.26,257.93,45,"Benchmarks saturate and leak, doctors disagree, and real diagnosis is interactive.","基准会饱和和泄漏，医生之间意见不一，而真实的诊断是交互式的。"],[258.28,261.17,45,"And deployment needs workflows.","以及，部署需要工作流程。"],[261.52,268.89,45,"A model isn't a product: triage, family-doctor services and medical records each needed their own integration.","模型不等于产品：分诊、家庭医生服务和病历，每一项都需要各自的集成。"],[269.24,271.63,45,"We'll see that in the applications part.","这一点我们会在应用部分看到。"],[271.98,274.57,45,"The red line at the bottom is the bridge.","底部这行红字是承上启下的桥梁。"],[274.92,281.69,45,"All of these lessons point beyond a single model, toward a system that is general and trustworthy.","所有这些经验都指向单一模型之外，指向一个通用且可信的系统。"],[282.04,284.7,45,"So what exactly is that goal?","那么，这个目标究竟是什么？"],[285.95,291.17,46,"HuatuoGPT was one model for one kind of task: text consultation.","HuatuoGPT 是针对一类任务的一个模型：文本问诊。"],[291.52,293.69,46,"Medicine is much bigger than that.","而医学远比这宽广得多。"],[294.04,300.88,46,"In this part we define the long-term goal, generalist medical AI: one model for every medical task.","这一部分，我们来定义长期目标——通用医学人工智能：一个模型完成所有医学任务。"],[301.23,305.04,46,"I'll also argue that the road there isn't a straight line.","我还会论证，通往那里的道路并不是一条直线。"],[305.39,311.29,46,"It runs through specialist models and, crucially, through earning trust.","它要经过专科模型，而且关键是要经过赢得信任这一关。"],[312.54,320.28,47,"Generalist medical AI, or GMAI, is the medical analogue of artificial general intelligence.","通用医学人工智能，也就是 GMAI，是通用人工智能 AGI 在医学领域的对应物。"],[320.63,325.99,47,"The term was popularized by a twenty twenty-three Nature paper by Moor and colleagues.","这个术语因 Moor 等人 2023 年发表在 Nature 上的一篇论文而广为人知。"],[326.34,332.76,47,"The definition: one model that serves every medical application with little adaptation.","它的定义是：一个模型，只需很少的适配，就能服务所有医学应用。"],[333.11,334.86,47,"Look at the hub-and-spoke picture.","看这张中心辐射式的图。"],[335.21,343.43,47,"Medical Q and A, image analysis, clinical diagnosis, patient triage and treatment planning all hang off one central model.","医学问答、影像分析、临床诊断、病人分诊和治疗规划，全都挂在一个中心模型上。"],[343.78,346.96,47,"Instead of each task having its own separate system.","而不是每个任务各自拥有独立的系统。"],[347.31,349.1,47,"Why want this? Two reasons.","为什么要这样？有两个原因。"],[349.45,357.84,47,"Mutual benefit between tasks: what a model learns from reading radiology reports helps it interpret images, and vice versa.","第一，任务之间相互促进：模型从阅读放射报告中学到的东西有助于它解读影像，反之亦然。"],[358.19,362.77,47,"That matters a lot in medicine, where each individual task has limited data.","这在医学中非常重要，因为每个单独任务的数据都很有限。"],[363.12,369.89,47,"And deployment efficiency: a hospital would much rather maintain one system than fifty.","第二，部署效率：医院更愿意维护一个系统，而不是五十个。"],[371.14,376.97,48,"Why build GMAI around language rather than, say, around vision? Three reasons.","为什么要以语言而不是视觉为中心来构建 GMAI？有三个原因。"],[377.32,380.01,48,"Language carries massive knowledge.","语言承载着海量的知识。"],[380.36,384.86,48,"A sentence like the sun rises in the east encodes a fact about the world.","像“太阳从东方升起”这样一句话，就编码了一个关于世界的事实。"],[385.21,390.08,48,"And medical textbooks encode centuries of clinical knowledge the same way.","而医学教科书以同样的方式编码了几百年积累的临床知识。"],[390.43,398.48,48,"Language is the interface between humans and machines: patients describe symptoms in words, doctors write notes in words.","语言是人与机器之间的接口：病人用语言描述症状，医生用语言书写病历。"],[398.83,405.27,48,"And language can reason and plan; it's the medium of thought, which is why chain-of-thought works.","而且语言能够推理和规划；它是思维的媒介，这也是思维链之所以有效的原因。"],[405.62,410.75,48,"So we put the LLM at the center and extend it in four directions.","所以，我们把大模型放在中心，向四个方向扩展。"],[411.1,416.42,48,"More modalities in, more modalities out, longer context, and better reasoning.","更多模态的输入、更多模态的输出、更长的上下文，以及更好的推理。"],[416.77,420.25,48,"Those four directions are basically the roadmap for part four.","这四个方向基本上就是第四部分的路线图。"],[421.5,424.1,49,"There are two ways to get to GMAI.","通往 GMAI 有两条路。"],[424.45,431.96,49,"Top-down, on the left: a company like OpenAI trains one giant model for everything and pushes it down into medicine.","左边是自上而下：像 OpenAI 这样的公司训练一个包揽一切的巨型模型，再把它下沉到医学领域。"],[432.31,443.24,49,"Bottom-up, on the right: build many specialized multimodal models, a pathology model, a dental model, an EEG model, and gradually merge them into a whole.","右边是自下而上：构建许多专门的多模态模型，比如病理模型、口腔模型、脑电模型，再逐步把它们融合成一个整体。"],[443.59,447.98,49,"These approaches aren't rivals; look at the arrows between them.","这两种路线并不是对手；看看它们之间的箭头。"],[448.33,452.22,49,"Big companies provide better backbones that specialists build on.","大公司提供更好的基座模型，供专科模型在其上构建。"],[452.57,458.78,49,"Specialists provide better insights, better data and better benchmarks that flow back into general models.","专科模型则提供更好的洞见、数据和基准，反哺通用模型。"],[459.13,463.12,49,"For a university lab, bottom-up is where we can contribute.","对一个大学实验室来说，自下而上才是我们能做出贡献的地方。"],[463.47,471.18,49,"We're not going to out-train the giants, but we can build the specialized pieces that require hospital partnerships and domain expertise.","我们不可能在训练上胜过巨头，但我们可以构建那些需要医院合作和领域专业知识的专门模块。"],[472.43,475.35,50,"Here's another way to look at the path: a ladder.","看待这条路径的另一种方式是：一架梯子。"],[475.7,481.42,50,"The horizontal axis is trust earned in practice; the vertical one is generality.","横轴是在实践中赢得的信任，纵轴是通用性。"],[481.77,487.68,50,"Level one is medical Q and A tools: they answer questions but take no responsibility for decisions.","第一级是医学问答工具：它们回答问题，但不对决策承担责任。"],[488.03,495.81,50,"Level two is trustworthy specialist agents: one specialty, grounded in evidence, calibrated, auditable.","第二级是可信的专科智能体：单一专科、有证据支撑、经过校准、可审计。"],[496.16,505.26,50,"Level three is clinical copilots inside the workflow: many specialties, working inside real hospital systems under supervision.","第三级是融入工作流程的临床副驾驶：覆盖多个专科，在监督下于真实的医院系统中工作。"],[505.61,512.23,50,"Level four is generalist medical AI: one model, any task, any modality.","第四级是通用医学 AI：一个模型，任何任务，任何模态。"],[512.58,516.12,50,"Notice the ladder moves up and to the right together.","注意，这架梯子是同时向上和向右延伸的。"],[516.47,520.85,50,"You don't get generality without first earning trust in practice.","不先在实践中赢得信任，就不可能获得通用性。"],[521.2,529.57,50,"Honestly, I'd say the field is currently between Level two and Level three, and that's where most of the interesting work is right now.","坦白说，我认为这个领域目前处于第二级和第三级之间，而这正是当前最有意思的工作所在。"],[530.82,533.09,51,"Here's the overview of what comes next.","这是接下来内容的概览。"],[533.44,540.44,51,"To move toward GMAI, a model needs perception, meaning multimodal input and longer context.","要走向 GMAI，模型需要感知能力，也就是多模态输入和更长的上下文。"],[540.79,543.44,51,"Cognition, meaning better reasoning.","认知能力，也就是更好的推理。"],[543.79,550.56,51,"Interaction, meaning multimodal generation and agent simulation, such as a twin hospital.","交互能力，也就是多模态生成，以及智能体模拟，比如孪生医院。"],[550.91,555.41,51,"And multilingual support, so it can serve patients in any language.","以及多语言支持，使它能用任何语言为病人服务。"],[555.76,565.39,51,"Then there are the challenges: the tension between generalist and specialized models, trustworthiness and interpretability, and the lack of challenging benchmarks.","然后是挑战：通用模型与专科模型之间的张力、可信性与可解释性，以及缺乏有挑战性的基准。"],[565.74,569.68,51,"We'll walk through the capabilities first, then the challenges.","我们先逐一讲能力，再讲挑战。"]]},{"n":5,"title":"Perception: Vision, Speech, Signals and Long Context","blurb":"Teaching models to perceive: ALLaVA and VLFeedback data, HuatuoGPT-Vision, speech, motion, EEG, ShizhenGPT for TCM, and LongLLaVA for huge medical images.","file":"lecture09_part5.mp4","poster":"lecture09_part5.jpg","duration":1121.2,"first":52,"last":72,"slides":[{"n":52,"title":"4 The Roadmap: Perception, Reasoning, Generation, Languages","t":0.8},{"n":53,"title":"Perception: Multimodal LLMs","t":28.15},{"n":54,"title":"Perception: Starting from Data (ALLaVA-4V)","t":86.06},{"n":55,"title":"Perception: Multimodal LLMs Trained on ALLaVA","t":144.51},{"n":56,"title":"Better Data, Better Models","t":186.0},{"n":57,"title":"VLFeedback: Preference Data for Vision–Language Models","t":237.5},{"n":58,"title":"DPO with VLFeedback on Qwen-VL","t":302.08},{"n":59,"title":"HuatuoGPT-Vision: Injecting Medical Visual Knowledge","t":352.96},{"n":60,"title":"Impact of HuatuoGPT-Vision","t":416.28},{"n":61,"title":"Perception: Speech (1) Five Levels of Speech Understanding","t":455.35},{"n":62,"title":"Perception: Speech (2) Soundwave","t":514.56},{"n":63,"title":"Perception: Motion (MotionLLM)","t":574.82},{"n":64,"title":"Perception: EEG (WaveMind)","t":626.06},{"n":65,"title":"Perception: Traditional Chinese Medicine — ShizhenGPT","t":682.89},{"n":66,"title":"ShizhenGPT: Architecture","t":745.06},{"n":67,"title":"ShizhenGPT: Understanding Physiological Signals","t":800.87},{"n":68,"title":"Long Context: Medical Images Are Huge","t":859.54},{"n":69,"title":"Long Context: LongLLaVA","t":908.31},{"n":70,"title":"Long Context Application 1: High-Resolution Images","t":966.69},{"n":71,"title":"Long Context Application 2: Video Understanding","t":1015.6},{"n":72,"title":"Long Context Application 3: Mobile Agents","t":1061.85}],"sents":[[0.8,6.68,52,"That gives us the target. Now let's see what it takes in terms of capabilities.","目标有了。现在我们来看看，在能力上需要具备什么。"],[7.03,13.78,52,"A generalist doctor must see and hear, reason, explain, and speak every patient's language.","一名全科医生必须能看、能听、能推理、能解释，还要会说每位病人的语言。"],[14.13,22.06,52,"So this part has four sections: perception and long context, reasoning, generation and simulation, and multilinguality.","所以这一部分有四节：感知与长上下文、推理、生成与模拟，以及多语言。"],[22.41,26.75,52,"For each, I'll show the key idea and the work we did on it.","对每一节，我都会展示核心思想以及我们在这方面做的工作。"],[28.0,33.51,53,"This is a map of our multimodal work, so you know what's coming; no need to read the references.","这是我们多模态工作的全景图，让大家知道接下来要讲什么；参考文献不必细读。"],[33.86,36.65,53,"Roughly, the projects fall into three groups.","大致来说，这些项目分为三组。"],[37.0,47.54,53,"Perception, the model's eyes and ears: image-text data with ALLaVA, preference learning with VLFeedback, evaluation with MLLM-Bench and MileBench.","感知，也就是模型的眼睛和耳朵：ALLaVA 做图文数据，VLFeedback 做偏好学习，MLLM-Bench 和 MileBench 做评测。"],[47.89,56.5,53,"Then speech with Soundwave, motion with MotionLLM, and full-modality traditional Chinese medicine with ShizhenGPT.","还有 Soundwave 做语音，MotionLLM 做动作，ShizhenGPT 做全模态的中医。"],[56.85,67.52,53,"Generation, the model's mouth and hands: speech-to-speech with EchoX, image generation with Janus-4o, and medical video with MedGen.","生成，也就是模型的嘴和手：EchoX 做语音到语音，Janus-4o 做图像生成，MedGen 做医学视频。"],[67.87,72.27,53,"And reasoning over modalities: Video-R1.","以及跨模态推理：Video-R1。"],[72.62,77.77,53,"Many of these aren't medical at first glance. That's on purpose.","其中很多乍看之下并不是医学的。这是有意为之。"],[78.12,84.66,53,"General multimodal techniques usually have to be developed before you can specialize them for medicine.","通用的多模态技术通常要先发展起来，然后才能针对医学进行专门化。"],[85.91,90.56,54,"For perception, as with HuatuoGPT, we started from data.","在感知方面，和 HuatuoGPT 一样，我们也从数据开始。"],[90.91,97.48,54,"The problem in early twenty twenty-four: open vision-language models were trained on short, noisy image captions.","2024 年初的问题是：开源视觉语言模型是在简短、嘈杂的图像描述上训练的。"],[97.83,101.76,54,"So they couldn't describe images in detail or reason about them.","所以它们无法详细描述图像，也无法对图像进行推理。"],[102.11,108.82,54,"ALLaVA's idea is simple. Take images, for example from LAION, and give them to GPT-4V.","ALLaVA 的思路很简单。拿一些图像，比如来自 LAION 的，交给 GPT-4V。"],[109.17,117.55,54,"Ask it to do three things in one go: write a detailed caption, pose a complex question about the image, and give a detailed answer.","让它一次完成三件事：写一段详细的描述，针对图像提出一个复杂的问题，再给出详细的回答。"],[117.9,122.98,54,"Do the same for Vision-FLAN tasks, asking for captions plus detailed answers.","对 Vision-FLAN 的任务也这样做，要求生成描述加详细回答。"],[123.33,126.95,54,"Captioning first and then asking a question matters.","先描述、再提问，这一点很重要。"],[127.3,135.76,54,"It forces the model to look carefully at the image before reasoning, so the question and answer are grounded in what it just described.","它迫使模型在推理之前先仔细看图，让问题和回答都建立在它刚刚描述的内容之上。"],[136.11,143.11,54,"It's the same synthetic-data distillation idea you saw in the LLM lectures, applied to vision.","这就是你们在大模型那几讲中见过的合成数据蒸馏思想，只是应用到了视觉上。"],[144.36,149.16,55,"One nice signal that data like this is useful: other people adopt it.","这类数据有用的一个好信号是：别人在采用它。"],[149.51,159.85,55,"This is Cambrian-1, a fully open, vision-centric study of multimodal LLMs from NYU, with Yann LeCun and Saining Xie among the authors.","这是 Cambrian-1，来自纽约大学的一项完全开放、以视觉为中心的多模态大模型研究，作者包括 Yann LeCun 和谢赛宁。"],[160.2,167.5,55,"When they curated their seven-million-example instruction-tuning dataset, they included ALLaVA as one of the sources.","在整理他们七百万条样本的指令微调数据集时，他们把 ALLaVA 作为其中一个数据来源。"],[167.85,170.73,55,"It's the item highlighted in the red box.","就是红框里标出的那一项。"],[171.08,179.36,55,"I mention this not for credit, but because in research, data releases often have more lasting impact than model releases.","我提这个不是为了邀功，而是因为在研究中，发布数据往往比发布模型有更持久的影响。"],[179.71,184.6,55,"Models get overtaken in months; a good dataset keeps being reused.","模型几个月就会被超越，而一个好的数据集会被持续复用。"],[185.85,188.99,56,"Here's the direct evidence that the data helps.","这是数据有效的直接证据。"],[189.34,196.08,56,"On the left, two small vision-language models, MobileVLM-v2 and Mipha-3B.","左边是两个小型视觉语言模型，MobileVLM-v2 和 Mipha-3B。"],[196.43,202.87,56,"Blue bars are the original models; yellow bars are the same models with their training data replaced by ALLaVA.","蓝色柱是原始模型；黄色柱是把训练数据替换成 ALLaVA 后的同一模型。"],[203.22,208.04,56,"The yellow bars are higher on most benchmarks, sometimes by a lot.","在大多数基准上黄色柱都更高，有时高出很多。"],[208.39,217.24,56,"MMVP goes from about nineteen to twenty-five for MobileVLM, and LLaVA-Bench from fifty-three to sixty-five.","对 MobileVLM 来说，MMVP 从约 19 提升到 25，LLaVA-Bench 从 53 提升到 65。"],[217.59,228.06,56,"On the right, our own ALLaVA model, using only a two point seven billion parameter Phi-2 backbone, is competitive with much bigger 7B and 13B models on many columns.","右边，我们自己的 ALLaVA 模型只用了 27 亿参数的 Phi-2 作为基座，就在许多列上能与大得多的 7B 和 13B 模型竞争。"],[228.41,231.5,56,"Same architecture, better data, better model.","同样的架构，更好的数据，更好的模型。"],[231.85,236.1,56,"That's the theme of this slide and, really, of the first half of today.","这是这一页的主题，其实也是今天前半部分的主题。"],[237.35,244.14,57,"After SFT data comes preference data, exactly like the text pipeline in Lecture six.","SFT 数据之后是偏好数据，和第六讲中的文本流程完全一样。"],[244.49,254.2,57,"VLFeedback, from the Silkie paper, a collaboration with Lingpeng Kong's group at HKU, is preference data for vision-language models.","VLFeedback 来自 Silkie 论文，是与港大孔令鹏团队的合作成果，它是面向视觉语言模型的偏好数据。"],[254.55,255.84,57,"Here's how it's built.","下面是它的构建方式。"],[256.19,263.31,57,"Collect instructions from many sources: LLaVA, M3IT, LLaVA-Med and red-teaming sets.","从多个来源收集指令：LLaVA、M3IT、LLaVA-Med，以及红队测试数据集。"],[263.66,267.35,57,"Generate responses with a pool of different vision-language models.","用一个由不同视觉语言模型组成的模型池来生成回答。"],[267.7,276.97,57,"Then GPT-4V rates the responses along three dimensions: helpfulness, visual faithfulness, and ethical considerations.","然后由 GPT-4V 从三个维度给回答打分：有用性、视觉忠实度和伦理考量。"],[277.32,281.51,57,"Look at the example: does the tent have a red and black checkered pattern?","看这个例子：帐篷上有没有红黑格子图案？"],[281.86,285.78,57,"Several models say yes, but the pattern is actually on the umbrella.","好几个模型都说有，但这个图案其实在雨伞上。"],[286.13,289.56,57,"Model B gets it right and wins on faithfulness.","模型 B 答对了，在忠实度上胜出。"],[289.91,293.73,57,"That's hallucination being caught by the preference signal.","这就是偏好信号捕捉到了幻觉。"],[294.08,300.68,57,"That matters enormously in medicine, where a model seeing a lesion that isn't there is dangerous.","这在医学中极其重要，因为模型如果“看到”一个并不存在的病灶，是非常危险的。"],[301.93,306.71,58,"And here's the result of training on that preference data with DPO.","这是用 DPO 在这些偏好数据上训练的结果。"],[307.06,314.0,58,"Silkie, which is Qwen-VL-Chat plus DPO on VLFeedback, improves on every benchmark in the bottom row.","Silkie，也就是在 VLFeedback 上用 DPO 训练的 Qwen-VL-Chat，在最下面一行的每个基准上都有提升。"],[314.35,322.49,58,"Perception and cognition on MME, hallucination on MMHal-Bench, MM-Vet, MathVista and MMMU.","包括 MME 的感知和认知、MMHal-Bench 的幻觉、MM-Vet、MathVista 和 MMMU。"],[322.84,324.4,58,"Compare with the other rows.","和其他行比较一下。"],[324.75,332.71,58,"LLaVA-RLHF and other preference methods give mixed results, up on some benchmarks and down on others.","LLaVA-RLHF 和其他偏好方法效果参差不齐，在一些基准上提升，在另一些上下降。"],[333.06,341.46,58,"Even simple heuristics like treating the longest answer as best, or GPT-4V's own answer as best, hurt performance.","就连一些简单的启发式方法，比如把最长的回答当作最好的，或者把 GPT-4V 自己的回答当作最好的，也会损害性能。"],[341.81,347.12,58,"What works is fine-grained AI feedback across a diverse response pool.","真正有效的，是在多样化回答池上的细粒度 AI 反馈。"],[347.47,351.56,58,"It's preference distillation, RLAIF for vision.","这就是偏好蒸馏，视觉版的 RLAIF。"],[352.81,356.24,59,"Now we bring this into medicine: HuatuoGPT-Vision.","现在我们把这些带进医学：HuatuoGPT-Vision。"],[356.59,361.88,59,"The challenge: medical image-text data is scarce, and public sources are noisy.","挑战在于：医学图文数据稀缺，公开数据源又很嘈杂。"],[362.23,369.55,59,"PubMed papers contain millions of medical images, but captions are often short and refer to things like figure three, arrow.","PubMed 论文里有数百万张医学图像，但图注往往很短，还会出现“见图三箭头”之类的指代。"],[369.9,371.53,59,"So we built PubMedVision.","所以我们构建了 PubMedVision。"],[371.88,378.35,59,"Take images from PubMed papers, and keep both the caption and the inline mentions from the paper's text.","从 PubMed 论文中提取图像，同时保留图注和论文正文中对该图的引用描述。"],[378.7,382.84,59,"Filter down to about nine hundred fifteen thousand high-quality medical images.","筛选后得到约九十一万五千张高质量医学图像。"],[383.19,390.6,59,"Then give each image plus its context to GPT-4V, which reformats it into two kinds of data.","然后把每张图像连同上下文交给 GPT-4V，由它改写成两类数据。"],[390.95,394.32,59,"Alignment VQA, describing the image in detail.","一类是对齐式视觉问答，对图像进行详细描述。"],[394.67,400.61,59,"And instruction-tuning VQA, answering questions in various dialogue scenarios.","另一类是指令微调式视觉问答，在各种对话场景中回答问题。"],[400.96,404.32,59,"That gives about one point three million examples.","这样总共得到约一百三十万条数据。"],[404.67,409.42,59,"The key idea: the surrounding text from the paper acts as a denoising signal.","核心思想是：论文中的上下文文字充当了去噪信号。"],[409.77,414.88,59,"So the descriptions are grounded in what the authors actually said about the image.","因此这些描述都建立在作者对图像的实际表述之上。"],[416.13,417.95,60,"And here's the impact.","这是它带来的影响。"],[418.3,423.07,60,"On the left is the MMMU benchmark's Health and Medicine leaderboard at the time.","左边是当时 MMMU 基准中健康与医学方向的排行榜。"],[423.42,432.71,60,"HuatuoGPT-Vision-34B ranked right behind GPT-4V, ahead of many larger and commercial models.","HuatuoGPT-Vision-34B 仅次于 GPT-4V，领先于许多更大的模型和商业模型。"],[433.06,438.46,60,"On the right, our Hugging Face page; the 7B model became quite popular.","右边是我们的 Hugging Face 页面；其中 7B 模型相当受欢迎。"],[438.81,441.53,60,"Downloads peaked around two hundred thousand a month.","下载量最高时每月约二十万次。"],[441.88,449.28,60,"So the recipe that worked for text, curated medical data carefully reformatted by a strong model, transfers to vision.","所以在文本上奏效的方法——精心整理的医学数据，再由强模型仔细改写——同样可以迁移到视觉上。"],[449.63,453.95,60,"Images are just one modality, though. Doctors also listen.","不过，图像只是一种模态。医生还会听。"],[455.2,457.02,61,"Moving from vision to speech.","从视觉转到语音。"],[457.37,466.82,61,"In medicine, sound carries a lot of information: a cough, breathing, how fluent someone's speech is, signs of depression in tone of voice.","在医学中，声音承载着大量信息：咳嗽、呼吸、说话是否流利，以及语调中透露的抑郁迹象。"],[467.17,470.38,61,"A text transcript throws all of that away.","而文字转录会把这些全部丢掉。"],[470.73,475.9,61,"This roadmap from our group defines five levels of speech understanding for LLMs.","我们团队提出的这份路线图，为大模型定义了语音理解的五个层级。"],[476.25,481.12,61,"Level one is basic speech recognition: turn speech into text.","第一级是基础的语音识别：把语音转成文字。"],[481.47,486.83,61,"Level two is paralinguistic perception: prosody, rhythm, pitch.","第二级是副语言感知：韵律、节奏、音高。"],[487.18,491.53,61,"Level three is non-semantic comprehension: emotion and context.","第三级是非语义理解：情绪和语境。"],[491.88,502.0,61,"Level four is the speech specialist. Look at the example: a medical specialist hearing a patient's cough and understanding what it implies.","第四级是语音专家。看这个例子：一位医学专家听到病人的咳嗽，并理解它意味着什么。"],[502.35,506.89,61,"Level five is speech AGI, a superhuman assistant.","第五级是语音 AGI，一个超越人类的助手。"],[507.24,513.16,61,"Most current speech LLMs are around levels one and two. Medicine needs level four.","目前大多数语音大模型处于第一到第二级。而医学需要的是第四级。"],[514.41,518.68,62,"Soundwave is our work on making speech LLMs data-efficient.","Soundwave 是我们提升语音大模型数据效率的工作。"],[519.03,523.91,62,"The core problem is that speech and text representations live in different spaces.","核心问题在于，语音和文本的表示处于不同的空间。"],[524.26,528.84,62,"And speech sequences are much longer than text for the same content.","而且对于同样的内容，语音序列要比文本长得多。"],[529.19,531.31,62,"Look at the three training stages.","看这三个训练阶段。"],[531.66,543.97,62,"In the alignment stage, an adapter maps audio-encoder outputs into the LLM's embedding space, trained with a CTC loss, so speech frames line up with text tokens.","在对齐阶段，一个适配器把音频编码器的输出映射到大模型的嵌入空间，用 CTC 损失训练，让语音帧与文本 token 对齐。"],[544.32,551.3,62,"In the shrinking stage, a second adapter compresses the long speech sequence down to something closer to text length.","在压缩阶段，第二个适配器把冗长的语音序列压缩到接近文本的长度。"],[551.65,558.71,62,"Then in the SFT stage, the model is instruction-tuned with LoRA on top of the two adapters.","然后在 SFT 阶段，在两个适配器之上用 LoRA 进行指令微调。"],[559.06,562.16,62,"Gray modules are frozen; orange ones are trained.","灰色模块是冻结的，橙色模块是训练的。"],[562.51,568.57,62,"The result: better performance than Qwen2-Audio using about one-fiftieth of the training data.","结果是：只用了约五十分之一的训练数据，就取得了比 Qwen2-Audio 更好的性能。"],[568.92,573.42,62,"Solve alignment explicitly, and you don't need brute-force scale.","显式地解决对齐问题，就不需要靠蛮力堆规模。"],[574.67,577.25,63,"Another modality: human motion.","另一种模态：人体动作。"],[577.6,584.81,63,"MotionLLM, a collaboration, understands human behaviour from both videos and 3D motion sequences.","MotionLLM 是一项合作工作，它能从视频和三维动作序列中理解人类行为。"],[585.16,590.29,63,"Look at the architecture: the input can be either video frames or motion data.","看这个架构：输入既可以是视频帧，也可以是动作数据。"],[590.64,597.29,63,"Each has its own encoder and a V-L translator that maps it into the LLM's token space.","每种输入都有自己的编码器，以及一个 V-L 转换器，把它映射到大模型的 token 空间。"],[597.64,605.1,63,"Training has two stages: first train only the translator so the LLM learns to read the new modality.","训练分为两个阶段：先只训练转换器，让大模型学会读取新的模态。"],[605.45,607.59,63,"Then instruction-tune with LoRA.","然后用 LoRA 进行指令微调。"],[607.94,609.98,63,"Why does this matter for medicine?","这对医学为什么重要？"],[610.33,617.9,63,"Gait analysis, rehabilitation, fall risk in the elderly, movement disorders like Parkinson's.","步态分析、康复训练、老年人跌倒风险，以及帕金森病这类运动障碍。"],[618.25,624.66,63,"A model that can understand and describe how someone moves opens up a whole class of clinical assessments.","一个能理解并描述人如何运动的模型，可以开启一整类临床评估。"],[625.91,628.34,64,"Even further from text: brain signals.","离文本更远的是：脑信号。"],[628.69,632.65,64,"WaveMind is our work toward a conversational EEG foundation model.","WaveMind 是我们迈向可对话的脑电基础模型的工作。"],[633.0,640.72,64,"The idea in the left circle: map EEG, text annotations and images into one unified embedding space.","左边圆圈里的想法是：把脑电、文本标注和图像映射到一个统一的嵌入空间中。"],[641.07,646.3,64,"Some EEG recordings come with text labels, such as clinical event annotations.","有些脑电记录带有文本标签，比如临床事件标注。"],[646.65,654.47,64,"Others come from experiments where people looked at images, so the brain signal can be aligned with the visual stimulus.","另一些来自让人观看图像的实验，所以脑信号可以与视觉刺激对齐。"],[654.82,661.92,64,"Once everything shares a space, you can attach an LLM and literally chat about an EEG recording.","一旦所有东西共享一个空间，就可以接上大模型，真正地围绕一段脑电记录进行对话。"],[662.27,668.64,64,"As in the examples on the right: ask what event is happening in this EEG, and the model answers.","就像右边的例子：问“这段脑电里发生了什么事件”，模型就会回答。"],[668.99,673.83,64,"EEG is high-dimensional, noisy and hard for non-experts to read.","脑电是高维的、嘈杂的，非专业人士很难读懂。"],[674.18,681.49,64,"A model that can explain it in language would be valuable for neurology and for brain-computer interfaces.","一个能用语言解释脑电的模型，对神经科学和脑机接口都很有价值。"],[682.74,689.24,65,"Here's a project that pulls many modalities together: ShizhenGPT, for traditional Chinese medicine.","这个项目把多种模态汇聚在一起：面向中医的 ShizhenGPT。"],[689.59,696.82,65,"TCM diagnosis classically uses four methods: looking, listening and smelling, asking, and feeling the pulse.","中医诊断传统上使用四种方法：望、闻、问、切。"],[697.17,704.52,65,"Many of those are non-textual: the tongue, complexion, voice, body odor, pulse waveform.","其中很多是非文本的：舌象、面色、声音、体味、脉搏波形。"],[704.87,706.74,65,"Look at the training curve at the top.","看上方的训练曲线。"],[707.09,712.82,65,"Pre-training stage one uses about eleven point nine billion tokens of TCM text.","预训练第一阶段使用了约一百一十九亿个中医文本 token。"],[713.17,719.76,65,"Stage two adds about three point six billion multimodal tokens: text plus images and sound.","第二阶段又加入了约三十六亿个多模态 token：文本加上图像和声音。"],[720.11,727.33,65,"Then instruction tuning covers images, sound, pulse, odor and ECG, each paired with text.","然后，指令微调覆盖了图像、声音、脉搏、气味和心电，每种都与文本配对。"],[727.68,734.88,65,"As far as we know, it's the first unified model that supports seeing, smelling, listening and pulse for TCM.","据我们所知，它是第一个在中医中同时支持望、闻、听、切的统一模型。"],[735.23,743.66,65,"And TCM is a nice stress test for GMAI, because it forces you to handle modalities that standard multimodal models ignore entirely.","而中医对 GMAI 来说是一个很好的压力测试，因为它迫使你处理那些常规多模态模型完全忽略的模态。"],[744.91,750.48,66,"Here's the architecture in more detail, and it's pleasantly simple. There are three core modules.","这是更详细的架构，它简洁得令人愉快。一共有三个核心模块。"],[750.83,756.79,66,"The LLM backbone understands, integrates and reasons over medical knowledge.","大模型基座负责理解、整合并推理医学知识。"],[757.14,765.77,66,"A vision encoder plus adapter turns images and video, tongue, palm, herbs, eyes, into tokens; that's the looking.","视觉编码器加适配器把图像和视频，包括舌头、手掌、草药、眼睛，转换成 token；这对应“望”。"],[766.12,773.16,66,"And a single shared signal encoder plus adapter handles sound, pulse, odor and ECG.","而一个共享的信号编码器加适配器，负责处理声音、脉搏、气味和心电。"],[773.51,778.09,66,"That covers listening and smelling, and pulse taking.","这对应“闻”和“切”。"],[778.44,785.74,66,"The design choice worth noticing: one encoder for all the one-dimensional signals, rather than a separate encoder for each.","值得注意的设计选择是：所有一维信号共用一个编码器，而不是每种信号各用一个。"],[786.09,793.36,66,"Pulse, ECG and audio are all time series, so sharing the encoder means each benefits from the others' data.","脉搏、心电和音频都是时间序列，所以共享编码器意味着每种信号都能从其他信号的数据中获益。"],[793.71,799.47,66,"Again, that's the mutual-benefit argument for generalist models, at the architecture level.","这又一次体现了通用模型的相互促进论点，只不过是在架构层面上。"],[800.72,803.83,67,"How well does it understand physiological signals?","它对生理信号的理解能力如何？"],[804.18,808.59,67,"Compare the last column, the model's accuracy, with the random baseline.","把最后一列，也就是模型的准确率，和随机基线比较一下。"],[808.94,818.63,67,"Some results are impressive: about eighty percent accuracy at detecting pregnancy from the pulse, a binary task, against fifty percent chance.","有些结果令人印象深刻：通过脉诊检测怀孕的准确率约为百分之八十，这是一个二分类任务，随机水平是百分之五十。"],[818.98,825.35,67,"ECG heartbeat classification reaches eighty-three percent, against twenty percent chance.","心电心搏分类达到百分之八十三，而随机水平是百分之二十。"],[825.7,829.25,67,"Others are clearly above chance but still modest.","另一些结果明显高于随机水平，但仍然一般。"],[829.6,836.51,67,"Classifying diseases from the pulse among nine classes reaches about twenty-one percent, against eleven.","通过脉诊在九个类别中做疾病分类，准确率约为百分之二十一，而随机水平是百分之十一。"],[836.86,839.41,67,"I want you to read tables like this honestly.","我希望大家能实事求是地解读这样的表格。"],[839.76,844.72,67,"These are first steps in modalities nobody had put into an LLM before.","这是在以前从未有人放进大模型的模态上迈出的第一步。"],[845.07,853.42,67,"The right summary is that the signals carry real information and the model can use it, but there's a long way to go before clinical use.","正确的总结是：这些信号确实携带了真实的信息，模型也能利用它，但离临床应用还有很长的路要走。"],[853.77,858.14,67,"By the way, the column header TCM-Omni is the project's earlier name.","顺便说一下，列标题 TCM-Omni 是这个项目早先的名字。"],[859.39,865.68,68,"After modalities, the second perception challenge is context length. Medical images are huge.","讲完模态，感知的第二个挑战是上下文长度。医学图像非常大。"],[866.03,869.08,68,"On the left is a pathology whole-slide image.","左边是一张病理全切片图像。"],[869.43,877.11,68,"At full resolution these are gigapixel images, and the region of interest the pathologist cares about is a tiny patch.","在全分辨率下，这些是十亿像素级的图像，而病理医生关心的感兴趣区域只是其中很小的一块。"],[877.46,882.8,68,"On the right, an MRI study isn't one image but many slices.","右边，一次核磁共振检查不是一张图，而是很多个切面。"],[883.15,886.68,68,"And a patient's history might include several studies over time.","而一个病人的病史可能包含不同时间的多次检查。"],[887.03,892.37,68,"If each image becomes hundreds or thousands of tokens, you quickly need very long inputs.","如果每张图像都变成成百上千个 token，你很快就需要非常长的输入。"],[892.72,898.99,68,"And as you know from the Transformer lecture, attention cost grows quadratically with sequence length.","而正如 Transformer 那一讲所讲，注意力的计算成本随序列长度呈平方增长。"],[899.34,906.91,68,"So long multimodal context isn't a nice-to-have in medicine; it's a requirement, and it's computationally hard.","所以，长多模态上下文在医学中不是锦上添花，而是必需品，而且在计算上很困难。"],[908.16,910.13,69,"First we measured the problem.","首先，我们对问题进行了度量。"],[910.48,916.98,69,"MileBench, our long-context multimodal benchmark, tests models with more and more images per question.","MileBench 是我们的长上下文多模态基准，它让每个问题包含越来越多的图像来测试模型。"],[917.33,925.91,69,"Look at the left plot: as the number of images grows from one to more than a hundred, open-source models drop by around forty percent.","看左边的图：当图像数量从一张增加到一百多张时，开源模型的性能下降了约百分之四十。"],[926.26,930.8,69,"And the gap to closed models grows to about forty-five percent.","而与闭源模型的差距扩大到约百分之四十五。"],[931.15,933.76,69,"Then we built LongLLaVA to address it.","然后，我们构建了 LongLLaVA 来解决这个问题。"],[934.11,940.64,69,"The architecture on the right is a hybrid: mostly Mamba layers, which scale linearly with sequence length.","右边的架构是一种混合结构：大部分是 Mamba 层，其计算量随序列长度线性增长。"],[940.99,949.09,69,"With a few Transformer layers for precise attention, plus mixture-of-experts layers and 2D pooling to compress image tokens.","再加上少量用于精确注意力的 Transformer 层，以及混合专家层和用于压缩图像 token 的二维池化。"],[949.44,954.49,69,"This lets the model handle up to around a thousand images efficiently on modest hardware.","这让模型能够在普通硬件上高效处理多达约一千张图像。"],[954.84,965.29,69,"The broader lesson from the efficiency side of the course: hybrid architectures are a practical way to get long context without paying the full quadratic price.","从课程中关于效率的部分来看，更广泛的启示是：混合架构是一种实用的方法，可以获得长上下文而不必付出完整的平方代价。"],[966.54,971.41,70,"Why does long context matter beyond counting images? Here are three applications.","除了图像数量之外，长上下文为什么重要？这里有三个应用。"],[971.76,974.1,70,"First, high-resolution images.","第一，高分辨率图像。"],[974.45,977.68,70,"This is the AnyRes scheme from LLaVA-NeXT.","这是 LLaVA-NeXT 中的 AnyRes 方案。"],[978.03,987.28,70,"A vision encoder has a fixed input size, so a high-resolution image is split into a grid of tiles, each encoded separately.","视觉编码器的输入尺寸是固定的，所以一张高分辨率图像会被切分成网格状的小块，每块单独编码。"],[987.63,991.58,70,"Plus there is a resized global view of the whole image.","此外还有一张缩放后的整图全局视图。"],[991.93,995.21,70,"All those tokens are flattened and fed to the LLM.","所有这些 token 被展平后输入大模型。"],[995.56,1000.43,70,"With a two-by-two grid you already have five times the tokens of one image.","用二乘二的网格，token 数量就已经是单张图像的五倍了。"],[1000.78,1009.76,70,"Go finer, four-by-four, eight-by-eight, sixteen-by-sixteen, as you would for pathology or a detailed X-ray, and the token count explodes.","再切得更细，四乘四、八乘八、十六乘十六，就像处理病理图像或精细的 X 光片时那样，token 数量就会爆炸式增长。"],[1010.11,1014.2,70,"So better resolution directly means longer context.","所以，更高的分辨率直接意味着更长的上下文。"],[1015.45,1017.34,71,"Second application: video.","第二个应用：视频。"],[1017.69,1022.39,71,"A video is just many frames, and each frame is many spatial tokens.","视频就是许多帧，而每一帧又包含许多空间 token。"],[1022.74,1028.66,71,"In this architecture from the video-LLM literature, frames go through a ViT.","在这个来自视频大模型文献的架构中，各帧先经过一个 ViT。"],[1029.01,1032.42,71,"A temporal module models how things change across frames.","时序建模模块负责刻画画面在帧与帧之间如何变化。"],[1032.77,1037.65,71,"And everything is projected into tokens the LLM reads along with the text.","然后所有内容被投影成 token，与文本一起输入大模型。"],[1038.0,1044.09,71,"Even a short clip sampled at a few frames per second produces thousands of tokens.","即使是一段很短的视频，每秒只采样几帧，也会产生数千个 token。"],[1044.44,1052.04,71,"In medicine, think of endoscopy or surgical videos, ultrasound sweeps, or a patient's gait recording.","在医学中，想想内窥镜或手术视频、超声扫查，或者病人的步态录像。"],[1052.39,1060.45,71,"All of these need a model that can hold a lot of visual context at once and reason about change over time.","这些都需要一个能同时容纳大量视觉上下文、并能对随时间的变化进行推理的模型。"],[1061.7,1065.8,72,"Third application: agents, which connects to Lecture seven.","第三个应用：智能体，这和第七讲相关联。"],[1066.15,1073.15,72,"This is Mobile-Agent-v2, from Alibaba and collaborators, an assistant that operates a phone.","这是阿里巴巴及合作者提出的 Mobile-Agent-v2，一个能操作手机的助手。"],[1073.5,1080.67,72,"The task here: search for today's Lakers game result, then open Notes and write a sports news item about it.","这里的任务是：搜索今天湖人队的比赛结果，然后打开备忘录，写一条相关的体育新闻。"],[1081.02,1086.76,72,"Look at the bottom left: the input is an interleaved history of screenshots and operations.","看左下角：输入是截图和操作交错排列的历史记录。"],[1087.11,1090.53,72,"That's about twelve thousand tokens after seven steps.","七步之后就有大约一万二千个 token。"],[1090.88,1096.96,72,"The agent must remember what it saw several screens ago, the score, to complete a later step.","智能体必须记住几屏之前看到的内容，也就是比分，才能完成后面的步骤。"],[1097.31,1105.95,72,"Splitting the work across planning, decision and reflection agents raises accuracy from about fifty-one to eighty-seven percent.","把工作拆分给规划、决策和反思三个智能体，准确率就从约百分之五十一提升到百分之八十七。"],[1106.3,1108.87,72,"It's like automated software testing.","这就像自动化的软件测试。"],[1109.22,1119.37,72,"And a medical agent navigating a hospital information system faces exactly this problem: long, multimodal histories of screens and actions.","而一个在医院信息系统中操作的医疗智能体，面对的正是这个问题：由屏幕和操作构成的冗长多模态历史。"]]},{"n":6,"title":"Reasoning and Generation: HuatuoGPT-o1 to MedGen","blurb":"From math to medical reasoning with verifiable problems and long chain-of-thought in HuatuoGPT-o1, then generating speech, images, medical video and simulated worlds.","file":"lecture09_part6.mp4","poster":"lecture09_part6.jpg","duration":855.5,"first":73,"last":88,"slides":[{"n":73,"title":"4.2 Reasoning","t":0.8},{"n":74,"title":"From Math Reasoning to Medical Reasoning","t":27.05},{"n":75,"title":"On the Verifier","t":83.5},{"n":76,"title":"Mathematical Modeling: ORLM","t":145.74},{"n":77,"title":"Mathematical Modeling with Deep Thinking","t":205.83},{"n":78,"title":"Background: Complex Reasoning and Long CoT (1)","t":261.89},{"n":79,"title":"Background: Complex Reasoning and Long CoT (2)","t":305.78},{"n":80,"title":"Motivation: Verifiable Questions from Math to Medicine","t":361.1},{"n":81,"title":"Where Are Verifiable Problems in Medicine?","t":407.02},{"n":82,"title":"HuatuoGPT-o1: Medical Complex Reasoning","t":474.14},{"n":83,"title":"Video-R1: RL for Video Reasoning","t":540.31},{"n":84,"title":"4.3 Generation and Simulation","t":598.32},{"n":85,"title":"Generation: Speech-to-Speech (EchoX)","t":623.96},{"n":86,"title":"Generation: Images (Janus-4o)","t":691.4},{"n":87,"title":"Generation: Medical Video (MedGen)","t":749.99},{"n":88,"title":"Generation: Micro-World Simulation (MicroVerse)","t":804.44}],"sents":[[0.8,5.31,73,"We've covered how the model sees and remembers. Now: how it thinks.","我们已经讲了模型如何看和如何记忆。现在来讲：它如何思考。"],[5.66,10.3,73,"Medicine needs reasoning that can be checked, not just fluent explanations.","医学需要可以被检验的推理，而不仅仅是流畅的解释。"],[10.65,19.23,73,"Math showed us how to train that, with verifiable rewards, as you saw in Lecture six with o1 and DeepSeek-R1.","数学向我们展示了如何训练这种能力：用可验证的奖励，正如第六讲中 o1 和 DeepSeek-R1 所展示的。"],[19.58,25.65,73,"In this section I'll show how we built up reasoning expertise on math first, and then brought it to medicine.","这一节，我会展示我们如何先在数学上积累推理方面的经验，再把它带到医学中。"],[26.9,33.84,74,"Before medical reasoning, our group spent a lot of time on mathematical reasoning, and this slide lists that work.","在做医学推理之前，我们团队在数学推理上花了很多时间，这一页列出了相关工作。"],[34.19,36.87,74,"No need to read the references; here's the map.","参考文献不必细读，我来给大家梳理一下脉络。"],[37.22,42.97,74,"Some papers scale data: MathScale synthesizes large amounts of math instruction data.","有些论文在扩展数据：MathScale 合成了大量数学指令数据。"],[43.32,48.44,74,"Some work on verifiers: OVM, outcome-supervised value models.","有些研究验证器：OVM，即结果监督的价值模型。"],[48.79,56.24,74,"Some tackle mathematical modeling, turning real-world problems into math: ORLM and the Mamo benchmark.","有些处理数学建模问题，把现实问题转化为数学：比如 ORLM 和 Mamo 基准。"],[56.59,66.52,74,"And some study how reasoning models think: adaptive reasoning with QFFT, code-integrated reasoning with CoRT, and models learning from peers.","还有些研究推理模型如何思考：QFFT 做自适应推理，CoRT 做代码融合推理，以及模型向同伴学习。"],[66.87,71.52,74,"Why start with math? Because math gives you clean, checkable answers.","为什么从数学开始？因为数学给出的是干净、可检验的答案。"],[71.87,75.68,74,"That makes it the best playground for developing reasoning methods.","这让它成为开发推理方法的最佳试验场。"],[76.03,82.1,74,"Once the methods work, you can ask how to transfer them to messier domains like medicine.","一旦方法奏效，就可以思考如何把它们迁移到医学这类更复杂的领域。"],[83.35,88.07,75,"One idea from that work is worth understanding: the verifier.","这些工作中有一个思想值得理解：验证器。"],[88.42,94.4,75,"To guide reasoning step by step, you'd like to know whether a partial solution is on the right track.","为了一步步引导推理，你希望知道一个部分解是否走在正确的方向上。"],[94.75,96.94,75,"There are two ways to train such a scorer.","训练这样的打分器有两种方式。"],[97.29,104.41,75,"Process supervision, at the bottom of the right figure, labels every intermediate step as correct or wrong.","过程监督，在右图下方，把每一个中间步骤标注为对或错。"],[104.76,109.15,75,"That is expensive, because humans have to check each step.","这很昂贵，因为需要人逐步检查。"],[109.5,116.51,75,"Outcome supervision, at the top, only labels the final answer, and copies that label back onto every step.","结果监督，在上方，只标注最终答案，再把这个标签复制回每一个步骤。"],[116.86,122.05,75,"The assumption on the slide makes this work: a step is good if the final answer turned out correct.","这里的假设让这个方法得以成立：如果最终答案是对的，那每一步就是好的。"],[122.4,125.79,75,"That sounds crude, but look at the left figure.","这听起来很粗糙，但看看左边的图。"],[126.14,133.82,75,"What the model then learns isn't whether this step is correct, but how likely this partial path is to lead to a correct answer.","模型学到的不是“这一步对不对”，而是“这条部分路径有多大可能通向正确答案”。"],[134.17,139.24,75,"That is a value function, exactly the quantity you want for planning and search.","这就是一个价值函数，恰恰是规划和搜索所需要的量。"],[139.59,144.34,75,"That's OVM. Cheap labels, and the right thing to optimize.","这就是 OVM。标注便宜，而且优化的目标是对的。"],[145.59,152.22,76,"Another branch is mathematical modeling: turning a messy real-world description into a formal optimization problem.","另一个分支是数学建模：把杂乱的现实描述转化为形式化的优化问题。"],[152.57,160.04,76,"Look at the example: a toy manufacturer with profits, wood and steel constraints, and some logical conditions.","看这个例子：一家玩具厂，有利润、木材和钢材约束，以及一些逻辑条件。"],[160.39,166.73,76,"The model must define decision variables, write the objective, and formalize all constraints.","模型必须定义决策变量、写出目标函数，并把所有约束形式化。"],[167.08,170.69,76,"That includes tricky logical ones, highlighted in red.","包括那些棘手的逻辑约束，就是红色高亮的部分。"],[171.04,178.46,76,"ORLM, built with Cardinal Operations, was the first open LLM trained specifically for optimization modeling.","ORLM 是我们与杉数科技合作构建的，是第一个专门为优化建模训练的开源大模型。"],[178.81,183.56,76,"The company upgraded it into its COLORMind platform, which is used in production.","该公司把它升级为 COLORMind 平台，已投入实际生产使用。"],[183.91,190.66,76,"And the paper was published in Operations Research, a top journal in that field, not an AI venue.","论文发表在运筹学领域的顶级期刊 Operations Research 上，而不是 AI 会议上。"],[191.01,198.59,76,"The connection to medicine: hospital scheduling, resource allocation and treatment planning are all optimization problems.","它与医学的联系在于：医院排班、资源分配和治疗规划都是优化问题。"],[198.94,204.43,76,"Real-world reasoning often means building the right model of the problem first.","现实世界中的推理，往往意味着首先要为问题建立正确的模型。"],[205.68,209.29,77,"And here's how this evolved once reasoning models arrived.","下面是推理模型出现后，这件事是如何演进的。"],[209.64,213.84,77,"The top shows the traditional, non-reflective pipeline.","上方是传统的非反思式流程。"],[214.19,222.15,77,"The LLM writes a math model and code, then a separate step runs the code, and you take whatever comes out.","大模型写出数学模型和代码，然后由一个单独的步骤运行代码，输出什么就用什么。"],[222.5,225.47,77,"If the formulation is wrong, nobody notices.","如果建模本身错了，没有人会发现。"],[225.82,230.09,77,"The bottom shows reflective generation with a large reasoning model.","下方是用大型推理模型进行的反思式生成。"],[230.44,238.0,77,"Think, write the model, write code, actually execute it inside the reasoning, and observe the output.","思考、写模型、写代码，在推理过程中真正执行代码，并观察输出。"],[238.35,243.41,77,"Then revise if something looks off, looping back as needed.","如果发现不对就修改，根据需要循环回去。"],[243.76,245.93,77,"This is the CALM-then-STORM work.","这就是 CALM Before the STORM 这项工作。"],[246.28,252.14,77,"The point is that reasoning models get much better when they can test their own intermediate work with tools.","关键在于，当推理模型能用工具检验自己的中间结果时，它们会变得好得多。"],[252.49,260.49,77,"A doctor does the same: form a hypothesis, order a test, look at the result, revise.","医生也是这样做的：提出假设，开检查单，看结果，再修正。"],[261.74,264.7,78,"Let me remind you of the background from Lecture six.","我来回顾一下第六讲的背景。"],[265.05,269.61,78,"When OpenAI released o1, it showed a huge jump on reasoning-heavy tasks.","OpenAI 发布 o1 时，它在推理密集型任务上展现了巨大的飞跃。"],[269.96,277.61,78,"Look at the bars: on AIME competition math, GPT-4o scored about thirteen, o1 about eighty-three.","看柱状图：在 AIME 竞赛数学上，GPT-4o 约得 13 分，o1 约得 83 分。"],[277.96,282.83,78,"Similar jumps on competitive programming and on PhD-level science questions.","在编程竞赛和博士级科学问题上，也有类似的飞跃。"],[283.18,285.63,78,"The two scatter plots at the bottom show why.","下方的两个散点图说明了原因。"],[285.98,290.97,78,"Accuracy keeps improving with more train-time compute, meaning more RL.","准确率随着训练时算力的增加，也就是更多的强化学习，而不断提高。"],[291.32,295.64,78,"And with more test-time compute, meaning longer thinking.","也随着测试时算力的增加，也就是更长的思考，而不断提高。"],[295.99,300.15,78,"That was a paradigm shift: from scaling pre-training to scaling reasoning.","这是一次范式转变：从扩展预训练，转向扩展推理能力。"],[300.5,304.38,78,"Our natural question was whether this works in medicine too.","我们自然要问：这在医学中是否同样有效？"],[305.63,309.71,79,"And there was a second motivation, specific to domain adaptation.","还有第二个动机，专门针对领域适配。"],[310.06,318.61,79,"Recall the lesson from the twenty twenty-four pharmacist exam: domain fine-tuning and continued pre-training may be reaching their limits.","回想 2024 年药师考试的教训：领域微调和继续预训练可能正在触及极限。"],[318.96,323.02,79,"Two reasons. First, real-world medical data is finite.","两个原因。第一，真实世界的医学数据是有限的。"],[323.37,327.45,79,"We're approaching the point of using all of it that's publicly available.","我们正在接近用尽所有公开可用数据的地步。"],[327.8,337.59,79,"Second, general-purpose LLMs keep growing, and their training data already covers most of the medical knowledge we'd add through domain adaptation.","第二，通用大模型在不断壮大，它们的训练数据已经覆盖了我们通过领域适配想要加入的大部分医学知识。"],[337.94,344.73,79,"The photo is Ilya Sutskever at NeurIPS twenty twenty-four, saying pre-training as we know it will end.","照片里是 Ilya Sutskever 在 NeurIPS 2024 上的演讲，他说我们所熟知的预训练将会终结。"],[345.08,349.68,79,"Compute keeps growing, but data doesn't; we have only one internet.","算力在不断增长，但数据没有；我们只有一个互联网。"],[350.03,355.12,79,"If simply adding medical text no longer gives a big edge, the next lever is reasoning.","如果仅仅增加医学文本已经不能带来大的优势，那下一个杠杆就是推理。"],[355.47,359.7,79,"That means teaching the model to use what it already knows more effectively.","也就是教会模型更有效地运用它已经掌握的知识。"],[360.95,364.44,80,"So why did RL for reasoning work so well in math?","那么，为什么用于推理的强化学习在数学上效果这么好？"],[364.79,373.32,80,"Look at the two examples: a simple GSM8K word problem with answer seventy-two, and a hard AIME problem with answer sixty.","看这两个例子：一道简单的 GSM8K 应用题，答案是 72；一道很难的 AIME 题，答案是 60。"],[373.67,376.43,80,"They share two properties that make RL possible.","它们有两个共同的特性，让强化学习成为可能。"],[376.78,383.17,80,"First, the answer is definitive and unique, so you can check it automatically: a number either matches or it doesn't.","第一，答案是确定且唯一的，所以可以自动检验：数字要么对得上，要么对不上。"],[383.52,389.95,80,"Second, guessing the answer is hard, so the model can't get rewarded by luck; it has to actually reason.","第二，答案很难猜中，所以模型无法靠运气得到奖励，它必须真正进行推理。"],[390.3,392.78,80,"Medicine is the opposite in some ways.","医学在某些方面恰恰相反。"],[393.13,399.09,80,"The reasoning process often lacks clear steps, and many questions don't have one unique answer.","其推理过程往往缺乏清晰的步骤，很多问题也没有唯一的答案。"],[399.44,405.62,80,"So the challenge: where can we find medical problems that are verifiable in this math-like sense?","所以挑战在于：在哪里能找到像数学那样可验证的医学问题？"],[406.87,409.08,81,"Our answer: medical exams.","我们的答案是：医学考试。"],[409.43,418.57,81,"RL with verifiable rewards works well in general domains, as the open o1-style projects and later DeepSeek-R1 showed.","正如开源的 o1 类项目以及后来的 DeepSeek-R1 所表明的，基于可验证奖励的强化学习在通用领域效果很好。"],[418.92,422.38,81,"But we needed medical problems with checkable answers.","但我们需要的是答案可检验的医学问题。"],[422.73,430.73,81,"Look at the left pipeline. Start from closed-set exam questions, the MedQA and MedMCQA training sets.","看左边的流程。从封闭式考题出发，也就是 MedQA 和 MedMCQA 的训练集。"],[431.08,432.62,81,"Select the challenging ones.","挑选其中有难度的题目。"],[432.97,437.02,81,"Then use GPT-4o to filter and transform them.","然后用 GPT-4o 进行筛选和改造。"],[437.37,446.38,81,"The transformation is key: remove the multiple-choice options and turn the question into an open-ended one with a single ground-truth answer.","改造是关键：去掉选择题选项，把题目变成只有一个标准答案的开放式问题。"],[446.73,454.52,81,"Look at the example: a traveller from India with fever, chills and jaundice; the answer is cerebral edema.","看这个例子：一位从印度旅行回来的病人，发热、寒战、黄疸；答案是脑水肿。"],[454.87,459.91,81,"Without the options, the model can't eliminate its way to the answer; it has to reason.","没有了选项，模型就无法靠排除法得出答案，它必须进行推理。"],[460.26,468.84,81,"On the right, a medical verifier, an LLM, checks whether the model's final answer matches the ground truth, even if the wording differs.","右边，一个医学验证器，也就是一个大模型，检查模型的最终答案是否与标准答案一致，即使措辞不同也能判断。"],[469.19,472.74,81,"Now we have math-style verifiable problems for medicine.","这样，我们就有了数学式的可验证医学问题。"],[473.99,477.93,82,"Here's HuatuoGPT-o1, in two stages.","这是 HuatuoGPT-o1，分为两个阶段。"],[478.28,482.21,82,"Stage one, learning complex reasoning, on the left.","第一阶段在左边：学习复杂推理。"],[482.56,489.32,82,"For a verifiable problem, the model produces an initial reasoning and answer, and the verifier checks it.","对于一个可验证问题，模型先给出初始的推理和答案，然后由验证器检查。"],[489.67,499.38,82,"If it's wrong, the model applies one of four search strategies: backtracking, exploring a new path, verification, or correction, and tries again.","如果答错，模型就采用四种搜索策略之一：回溯、探索新路径、验证或纠正，然后再试一次。"],[499.73,505.34,82,"It repeats until the verifier says correct, or restarts after too many tries.","如此反复，直到验证器判定正确，或者尝试次数过多后重新开始。"],[505.69,513.41,82,"The successful search trajectory is then rewritten into a natural, long chain of thought, the complex CoT box.","成功的搜索轨迹随后被改写成自然的长思维链，也就是这个复杂思维链框。"],[513.76,519.09,82,"It has thinking like, wait, let me reconsider, followed by a formal response.","里面有诸如“等等，让我再想想”这样的思考，然后是正式的回答。"],[519.44,521.61,82,"That data is used for SFT.","这些数据用于 SFT。"],[521.96,529.6,82,"Stage two, on the right: RL with PPO, where the verifier provides the reward on new verifiable problems.","第二阶段在右边：用 PPO 做强化学习，由验证器在新的可验证问题上提供奖励。"],[529.95,538.91,82,"So it's the o1 recipe adapted to medicine: search for good reasoning, distill it, then reinforce it with verifiable rewards.","所以这就是适配到医学上的 o1 方法：搜索好的推理，把它蒸馏下来，再用可验证奖励加以强化。"],[540.16,543.76,83,"The same idea extends to multimodal reasoning.","同样的思路也可以扩展到多模态推理。"],[544.11,551.78,83,"Video-R1, a collaboration led by Xiangyu Yue's group at CUHK, applies R1-style RL to video.","Video-R1 是由香港中文大学岳翔宇团队牵头的合作工作，把 R1 式的强化学习应用到视频上。"],[552.13,558.65,83,"There's a catch with video: a model might answer correctly while ignoring time, just looking at individual frames.","视频有一个陷阱：模型可能只看单独的几帧、忽略时间顺序，也能答对。"],[559.0,563.26,83,"So the paper proposes T-GRPO, temporal GRPO.","所以论文提出了 T-GRPO，也就是时序 GRPO。"],[563.61,569.14,83,"For each question, the model sees the frames in their real order, and also randomly shuffled.","对每个问题，模型既看按真实顺序排列的帧，也看随机打乱的帧。"],[569.49,571.67,83,"Answers from both groups are scored.","两组的回答都会被打分。"],[572.02,577.42,83,"If the model does better with the correct order, it gets an extra temporal reward.","如果模型在正确顺序下表现更好，就能获得额外的时序奖励。"],[577.77,582.28,83,"That explicitly encourages it to use temporal information.","这就明确地鼓励模型利用时间信息。"],[582.63,590.03,83,"The general lesson: when you design RL rewards, think about the shortcuts the model could take, and design the reward to close them.","普遍的启示是：设计强化学习奖励时，要想到模型可能走的捷径，并设计奖励把它们堵住。"],[590.38,596.92,83,"For medicine, a temporal reward like this matters for things like disease progression, where order is everything.","对医学来说，这样的时序奖励对疾病进展这类问题很重要，因为在那里顺序就是一切。"],[598.17,601.06,84,"So far the model perceives and reasons.","到目前为止，模型能感知，也能推理。"],[601.41,611.48,84,"A generalist medical AI must also produce things: speech for a voice assistant, images and videos for education, and eventually whole simulated worlds.","而一个通用医学 AI 还必须能生成内容：为语音助手生成语音，为教育生成图像和视频，最终还要生成完整的模拟世界。"],[611.83,617.5,84,"Generation is also how we build the simulated patients and environments in part six.","生成也是我们在第六部分构建模拟病人和环境的方式。"],[617.85,622.56,84,"Let's look at speech, images, video, and then micro-world simulation.","我们依次来看语音、图像、视频，然后是微观世界模拟。"],[623.81,630.47,85,"First, speech output. EchoX is our work on end-to-end speech-to-speech LLMs.","首先是语音输出。EchoX 是我们关于端到端语音到语音大模型的工作。"],[630.82,635.19,85,"The problem it tackles is called the acoustic-semantic gap.","它要解决的问题叫做声学与语义之间的鸿沟。"],[635.54,644.95,85,"If you train a model directly to output speech tokens, those tokens are mostly about sound, not meaning, and the model's reasoning ability degrades.","如果直接训练模型输出语音 token，这些 token 主要关乎声音而非语义，模型的推理能力就会下降。"],[645.3,646.93,85,"Look at the three stages.","看这三个阶段。"],[647.28,652.36,85,"Stage one trains a speech-to-text LLM: it hears and understands.","第一阶段训练一个语音到文本的大模型：它能听懂。"],[652.71,658.7,85,"Stage two trains a text-to-codec decoder: it turns text into speech tokens.","第二阶段训练一个文本到编码的解码器：把文本转成语音 token。"],[659.05,661.02,85,"Stage three is echo training.","第三阶段是回声训练。"],[661.37,670.3,85,"The speech-to-text model generates a text response, and the text-to-codec decoder turns that text into target speech tokens.","语音到文本模型生成文本回答，文本到编码解码器再把这段文本转换成目标语音 token。"],[670.65,677.39,85,"And an echo decoder learns to produce those tokens directly from the LLM's hidden states.","而回声解码器学习直接从大模型的隐藏状态生成这些 token。"],[677.74,681.99,85,"So speech generation stays tied to the semantic representation.","这样，语音生成就始终与语义表示绑定在一起。"],[682.34,690.0,85,"It achieves decent speech-to-speech performance with only about six thousand hours of data, which is small for this field.","它只用了约六千小时的数据，就取得了不错的语音到语音性能，这在该领域算是很少的数据量。"],[691.25,695.53,86,"Next, image generation, and the recipe will feel familiar.","接下来是图像生成，这个方法大家会觉得很熟悉。"],[695.88,703.34,86,"ShareGPT-4o-Image is a dataset we distilled from GPT-4o's image generation.","ShareGPT-4o-Image 是我们从 GPT-4o 的图像生成能力中蒸馏出来的数据集。"],[703.69,707.28,86,"It has about forty-five thousand text-to-image examples.","它包含约四万五千条文生图样本。"],[707.63,718.94,86,"And forty-six thousand text-and-image-to-image editing examples, like convert to Ghibli style, or replace with a brick-built train.","以及四万六千条文本加图像到图像的编辑样本，比如“转换成吉卜力风格”或者“替换成积木搭的火车”。"],[719.29,727.44,86,"We used it to fine-tune Janus-Pro, an open model that does both understanding and generation, giving Janus-4o.","我们用它微调了 Janus-Pro，一个既能理解又能生成的开源模型，从而得到 Janus-4o。"],[727.79,733.42,86,"On the right you see both modes: text to image, and text plus image to image.","右边可以看到两种模式：文生图，以及文本加图像生成图像。"],[733.77,736.93,86,"It's the same move we made with ALLaVA for understanding.","这和我们在理解方面用 ALLaVA 所做的是同一招。"],[737.28,743.44,86,"Use the strongest available model to create high-quality training data, then teach an open model.","用现有最强的模型来创造高质量的训练数据，再用它来教开源模型。"],[743.79,748.59,86,"Distillation is one of the most reliable tools an academic lab has.","蒸馏是学术实验室手中最可靠的工具之一。"],[749.84,753.77,87,"Now in medicine: MedGen, for medical video generation.","现在回到医学：用于医学视频生成的 MedGen。"],[754.12,761.97,87,"General video models produce beautiful clips, but ask them for a medical scenario and you often get nonsense anatomy or wrong procedures.","通用视频模型能生成漂亮的片段，但让它们生成医学场景，往往会出现荒谬的解剖结构或错误的操作流程。"],[762.32,766.03,87,"The five categories on the slide show the range of uses.","这里的五个类别展示了它的应用范围。"],[766.38,772.23,87,"Science popularization, like demonstrating physiotherapy; and surgical simulation.","科普，比如演示理疗；以及手术模拟。"],[772.58,778.65,87,"Medical animation, organs and blood flow; and medical imaging, such as CT sweeps.","医学动画，比如器官和血流；以及医学影像，比如 CT 扫描序列。"],[779.0,785.63,87,"And patient simulation: people showing symptoms like headache, nausea or abdominal pain.","还有病人模拟：展示头痛、恶心或腹痛等症状的人。"],[785.98,792.46,87,"The key, again, was data: a large set of medical videos with fine-grained annotations.","关键又是数据：大量带有细粒度标注的医学视频。"],[792.81,796.37,87,"So the model learns what each scene should actually contain.","让模型学会每个场景实际上应该包含什么。"],[796.72,803.04,87,"That patient-simulation row will matter later: it's how we make virtual patients that look ill.","病人模拟这一行后面会很重要：我们就是用它来制作看起来真的生病的虚拟病人。"],[804.29,808.41,88,"Going even smaller: MicroVerse, generating the micro-world.","再往更小的尺度走：MicroVerse，生成微观世界。"],[808.76,816.27,88,"The prompts on the left ask for things like an animation of lung alveoli with capillaries and blood flow.","左边的提示词要求生成诸如带有毛细血管和血流的肺泡动画。"],[816.62,823.08,88,"Cell division from one cell to two to four, and DNA being transcribed into RNA by polymerase.","从一个细胞分裂成两个再到四个的细胞分裂，以及 DNA 在聚合酶作用下转录成 RNA。"],[823.43,828.1,88,"Compare the columns: a real video, then Sora, then Veo3.","比较这几列：真实视频，然后是 Sora，然后是 Veo3。"],[828.45,834.38,88,"Look at whether the generated motion is biologically correct, not just whether it's pretty.","要看生成的运动在生物学上是否正确，而不只是好不好看。"],[834.73,843.42,88,"General video models produce attractive images but often get the science wrong, like the wrong division pattern or unrealistic structures.","通用视频模型生成的画面很吸引人，但科学上常常出错，比如错误的分裂方式或不真实的结构。"],[843.77,849.6,88,"This matters for education, but it's also a first step toward simulating biology.","这对教育很重要，同时也是迈向生物学模拟的第一步。"],[849.95,853.66,88,"That connects to the virtual cells I'll talk about in part six.","这与我将在第六部分讲到的虚拟细胞相关联。"]]},{"n":7,"title":"Multilinguality and Challenges on the Way","blurb":"Bringing medical AI to six billion people with AceGPT and Apollo, then the open challenges: decentralized data, specialists vs. generalists, interpretability and benchmarking.","file":"lecture09_part7.mp4","poster":"lecture09_part7.jpg","duration":919.1,"first":89,"last":106,"slides":[{"n":89,"title":"4.4 Multilinguality","t":0.8},{"n":90,"title":"Starting Point: AceGPT, a Localized Arabic LLM","t":27.9},{"n":91,"title":"AceGPT: Overall Pipeline","t":71.07},{"n":92,"title":"Democratizing Medical AI to 6 Billion People","t":120.89},{"n":93,"title":"Complementarity between Languages","t":174.45},{"n":94,"title":"Apollo: Multilingual Medical LLMs","t":230.63},{"n":95,"title":"Generalizing to More Languages","t":283.18},{"n":96,"title":"Apollo-2: Medical LLMs for 50 Languages","t":318.69},{"n":97,"title":"5 Challenges on the Way","t":376.91},{"n":98,"title":"Challenge 1: Decentralized Data","t":402.06},{"n":99,"title":"To Specialize or Not?","t":453.73},{"n":100,"title":"Specialized vs. Generalist Medical LLMs","t":507.03},{"n":101,"title":"Divide and Conquer: Specialist Models","t":571.31},{"n":102,"title":"From Many Specialist Models to One Foundation Model","t":619.11},{"n":103,"title":"Challenge 2: Interpretation — Post-hoc Explanation","t":687.54},{"n":104,"title":"Interpretability: How Do Models Generalize?","t":749.76},{"n":105,"title":"Compositional Generalization in Medical Imaging","t":803.14},{"n":106,"title":"Challenge 3: Benchmarking in the Community","t":854.52}],"sents":[[0.8,4.54,89,"The last capability on the roadmap is language coverage.","路线图上的最后一项能力是语言覆盖。"],[4.89,10.26,89,"Medical knowledge is universal: a vaccine works the same way in Arabic as in English.","医学知识是普适的：疫苗在阿拉伯语世界和英语世界里的作用方式是一样的。"],[10.61,12.29,89,"But medical data isn't.","但医学数据并非如此。"],[12.64,19.96,89,"Most of it is in English and Chinese, and about six billion people speak languages with very little medical data.","大部分医学数据是英文和中文的，而大约六十亿人说的语言几乎没有医学数据。"],[20.31,26.5,89,"This section is about closing that gap, and it actually started with a non-medical project.","这一节讲的就是如何弥合这道鸿沟，而它其实始于一个非医学的项目。"],[27.75,35.53,90,"Our starting point was AceGPT, a localized Arabic LLM released in September two thousand twenty-three.","我们的起点是 AceGPT，一个本地化的阿拉伯语大模型，发布于二零二三年九月。"],[35.88,39.02,90,"At the time, it was the leading open-source Arabic model.","当时，它是领先的开源阿拉伯语模型。"],[39.37,48.37,90,"On the Arabic Vicuna benchmark, its automatic evaluation surpassed ChatGPT and MBZUAI's JAIS.","在 Arabic Vicuna 基准上，它的自动评测结果超过了 ChatGPT 和 MBZUAI 的 JAIS。"],[48.72,52.13,90,"And it was getting around ten thousand downloads a month.","而且它每月有大约一万次下载。"],[52.48,54.45,90,"The key word here is localized.","这里的关键词是“本地化”。"],[54.8,59.72,90,"A good Arabic model isn't an English model that happens to output Arabic.","一个好的阿拉伯语模型，并不是一个恰好输出阿拉伯语的英文模型。"],[60.07,67.07,90,"It has to reflect Arabic culture and values: what's polite, what's appropriate, local knowledge and norms.","它必须体现阿拉伯的文化和价值观：什么是礼貌的，什么是得体的，以及当地的知识和规范。"],[67.42,69.67,90,"Translation alone doesn't get you there.","仅靠翻译是做不到这一点的。"],[70.92,76.75,91,"The pipeline is the standard three-stage LLM recipe, but localized at every stage.","整个流程就是标准的三阶段大模型训练配方，只不过每个阶段都做了本地化。"],[77.1,78.79,91,"We start from Llama 2.","我们从 Llama 2 出发。"],[79.14,83.96,91,"First, localized pre-training: continued pre-training on Arabic text.","第一，本地化预训练：在阿拉伯语文本上做继续预训练。"],[84.31,93.05,91,"Second, localized instruction tuning, with instructions and responses written for Arabic users rather than translated from English.","第二，本地化指令微调：指令和回答都是为阿拉伯语用户编写的，而不是从英文翻译过来的。"],[93.4,99.82,91,"And third, localized RLAIF, with preference data and queries that reflect local values.","第三，本地化 RLAIF：偏好数据和查询都体现当地的价值观。"],[100.17,102.6,91,"The result is AceGPT-chat.","最终得到的就是 AceGPT-chat。"],[102.95,109.7,91,"This is a nice example of how the generic recipe from Lectures five and six is really a template.","这是一个很好的例子，说明第五讲和第六讲中的通用配方其实是一个模板。"],[110.05,114.93,91,"The structure stays the same; what changes is the data at each stage.","结构保持不变，变化的是每个阶段的数据。"],[115.28,119.49,91,"Domain adaptation and language adaptation are two versions of the same idea.","领域适配和语言适配，其实是同一个思想的两种版本。"],[120.74,123.74,92,"From Arabic, we moved to multilingual medicine.","从阿拉伯语出发，我们转向了多语言医疗。"],[124.09,125.9,92,"The motivation has two parts.","动机有两个方面。"],[126.25,130.36,92,"First, medical knowledge is largely language-agnostic.","第一，医学知识在很大程度上与语言无关。"],[130.71,137.9,92,"Take the example on the slide: being vaccinated reduces the symptoms of COVID-19, and that is true in every language.","看幻灯片上的例子：接种疫苗可以减轻新冠的症状，这在任何语言中都成立。"],[138.25,142.11,92,"But second, many languages lack rich medical corpora.","但第二，许多语言缺乏丰富的医学语料。"],[142.46,147.41,92,"The map shows the world by official language, with bars for life expectancy.","这张地图按官方语言给世界着色，橙色柱子表示人口预期寿命。"],[147.76,154.84,92,"There's a visible link between where medical resources are scarce and where people speak languages with little medical data.","可以明显看到，医疗资源匮乏的地方，和人们所说的语言缺少医学数据的地方，是有关联的。"],[155.19,164.8,92,"By covering six major languages, English, Chinese, French, Spanish, Arabic and Hindi, you can reach about six billion people.","只要覆盖六种主要语言，英语、中文、法语、西班牙语、阿拉伯语和印地语，就能触达大约六十亿人。"],[165.15,173.05,92,"That's the idea behind this project, which became Apollo: lightweight medical models that democratize medical AI.","这就是这个项目背后的想法，它后来发展成了 Apollo：用轻量级的医疗模型让医疗 AI 普惠大众。"],[174.3,178.91,93,"A key finding from Apollo is that languages complement each other.","Apollo 的一个关键发现是：不同语言之间是互补的。"],[179.26,184.47,93,"Look at this table, all built on a small Qwen 1.8B base model.","看这张表，所有模型都基于一个小的 Qwen 1.8B 基座。"],[184.82,187.67,93,"The middle block trains a separate model for each language.","中间这一块是为每种语言单独训练一个模型。"],[188.02,192.56,93,"The gray cells on the diagonal show each model on its own language.","对角线上的灰色格子，表示每个模型在它自己语言上的表现。"],[192.91,196.36,93,"Some of them help other languages a bit, but they're uneven.","有些模型对其他语言也有一点帮助，但很不均衡。"],[196.71,198.89,93,"The bottom block is the interesting part.","最下面这一块才是有意思的部分。"],[199.24,204.09,93,"Averaging the weights of the per-language models gives thirty-three point five on average.","把各语言模型的权重做平均，平均分是三十三点五。"],[204.44,209.74,93,"Training one model on all languages jointly gives forty-one point five on average.","而用所有语言联合训练一个模型，平均分达到四十一点五。"],[210.09,214.73,93,"That's better than any single-language model, and better on every individual language.","这比任何单语言模型都好，而且在每一种语言上都更好。"],[215.08,218.5,93,"Even English improves, from thirty-nine to forty-five.","就连英语也提升了，从三十九分提高到四十五分。"],[218.85,223.58,93,"So medical knowledge learned in one language transfers to others.","所以，在一种语言中学到的医学知识可以迁移到其他语言。"],[223.93,229.23,93,"For low-resource languages, that's great news: they can borrow knowledge from high-resource ones.","对低资源语言来说，这是个好消息：它们可以从高资源语言那里借用知识。"],[230.48,234.45,94,"Here are Apollo's results across languages and model sizes.","这是 Apollo 在不同语言和不同模型规模上的结果。"],[234.8,241.3,94,"The Apollo models are at the bottom, from zero point five billion to seventy-two billion parameters.","Apollo 模型在最下面，参数规模从五亿到七百二十亿。"],[241.65,245.48,94,"The rows above are closed-source and open-source baselines.","上面的行是闭源和开源的基线模型。"],[245.83,253.38,94,"At each size, Apollo was the best open-source model at the time, and even the small ones beat much larger general models.","在每个规模上，Apollo 都是当时最好的开源模型，就连小模型也能打败大得多的通用模型。"],[253.73,257.12,94,"But I want to be honest about the sentence at the bottom.","但我想坦诚地谈谈底部这句话。"],[257.47,264.86,94,"GPT-4 is still better than us on the non-Chinese benchmarks: English, French, Spanish, Arabic and Hindi.","在非中文的基准上，GPT-4 仍然比我们强：英语、法语、西班牙语、阿拉伯语和印地语。"],[265.21,270.95,94,"Our largest model's average edges past GPT-4 mainly because of the Chinese columns.","我们最大模型的平均分略微超过 GPT-4，主要是靠中文这几列。"],[271.3,278.31,94,"That's typical: you can beat a frontier model on average while still trailing it in many specific settings.","这很典型：你可以在平均分上超过前沿模型，却在很多具体场景里仍然落后。"],[278.66,281.78,94,"Always look at the breakdown, not just the average.","一定要看细分结果，而不只是平均分。"],[283.03,286.56,95,"The next step was scaling from six languages to fifty.","下一步是从六种语言扩展到五十种。"],[286.91,294.04,95,"The map shows the coverage, and the box makes the point: covering fifty languages brings us close to the entire world population.","这张地图展示了覆盖范围，下面的框点明了重点：覆盖五十种语言，几乎就覆盖了全世界的人口。"],[294.39,298.17,95,"But fifty languages raises a real engineering problem.","但是五十种语言带来了一个真正的工程难题。"],[298.52,301.45,95,"You can't afford fifty separate models.","你负担不起五十个独立的模型。"],[301.8,310.61,95,"And putting fifty languages into one dense model creates interference: low-resource languages get crowded out by high-resource ones.","而把五十种语言塞进一个稠密模型，又会产生干扰：低资源语言会被高资源语言挤占。"],[310.96,314.71,95,"How do you share what should be shared, and separate what shouldn't?","怎样才能共享该共享的，又分开不该共享的？"],[315.06,317.29,95,"That's the question Apollo-2 answers.","这正是 Apollo-2 要回答的问题。"],[318.54,323.07,96,"Apollo-2's answer is a mixture of language-family experts.","Apollo-2 的答案是：语言家族专家混合模型。"],[323.42,330.31,96,"Look at the diagram: in the Transformer block, the feed-forward layer is replaced with a mixture-of-experts layer.","看这张图：在 Transformer 块中，前馈层被替换成了混合专家层。"],[330.66,336.16,96,"The router sends tokens to experts associated with groups of related languages.","路由器把 token 发送给与相关语言组对应的专家。"],[336.51,341.74,96,"In the example, French input is routed to a French-family expert.","在这个例子里，法语输入被路由到了法语家族的专家。"],[342.09,343.57,96,"Why language families?","为什么按语言家族划分？"],[343.92,353.37,96,"Related languages, say the Romance languages or the Indic languages, share vocabulary and structure, so they benefit from sharing parameters.","相关的语言，比如罗曼语族或印度语族，共享词汇和结构，所以它们能从参数共享中受益。"],[353.72,358.17,96,"Meanwhile, unrelated languages are kept from interfering with each other.","同时，不相关的语言之间就不会互相干扰。"],[358.52,362.56,96,"It's a middle ground between one shared model and one model per language.","这是介于“一个共享模型”和“每种语言一个模型”之间的折中方案。"],[362.91,370.67,96,"This is the same mixture-of-experts idea from the efficiency discussions, used here for linguistic structure.","这和我们在效率部分讨论过的混合专家思想是一样的，只是在这里用于语言结构。"],[371.02,375.51,96,"Apollo-2 was published at ICLR two thousand twenty-five.","Apollo-2 发表在 ICLR 二零二五上。"],[376.76,382.94,97,"That completes the roadmap of capabilities: perception, reasoning, generation and languages.","到这里，能力路线图就讲完了：感知、推理、生成和多语言。"],[383.29,387.47,97,"If it all sounds rosy, this part is the reality check.","如果这一切听起来都很美好，那么这一部分就是现实检验。"],[387.82,390.36,97,"Three big challenges stand in the way.","前面横着三大挑战。"],[390.71,398.42,97,"Medical data is scattered across hospitals, models are hard to interpret, and benchmarks saturate as fast as we build them.","医疗数据分散在各家医院，模型难以解释，而基准测试被刷满的速度和我们构建它们的速度一样快。"],[398.77,400.66,97,"Let's take them one at a time.","我们一个一个来看。"],[401.91,405.64,98,"Challenge one: medical data is decentralized.","挑战一：医疗数据是分散的。"],[405.99,414.47,98,"It lives in individual hospitals, behind privacy rules, in different formats, and no single organization can collect all of it.","它存放在各家医院里，受隐私规定保护，格式各不相同，没有任何一个机构能把它全部收集起来。"],[414.82,418.5,98,"You've seen these triangles before, but notice what's changed.","这些三角形你们之前见过，但请注意有什么变化。"],[418.85,423.39,98,"Top-down, OpenAI and similar companies build one model for all.","自上而下，OpenAI 这类公司构建一个通用于所有任务的模型。"],[423.74,429.58,98,"Bottom-up, the academic community builds Lego blocks, specialized models, and merges them.","自下而上，学术界搭建一块块乐高积木，也就是专用模型，再把它们合并起来。"],[429.93,438.37,98,"The reason the bottom-up path is necessary, not just convenient, is the phrase at the bottom: since data are decentralized.","自下而上的路径之所以是必需的，而不只是方便，原因就在底部这句话：因为数据是分散的。"],[438.72,445.38,98,"A hospital may never share its pathology archive, but it might help train a pathology model on site.","一家医院也许永远不会共享它的病理档案，但它可能愿意在本地帮助训练一个病理模型。"],[445.73,452.33,98,"So specialization isn't only a research choice; it's often forced by where the data live.","所以，专用化不只是一种研究选择，它往往是由数据所在的位置决定的。"],[453.58,458.69,99,"If we accept that some specialization is needed, when should we specialize?","如果我们承认需要一定程度的专用化，那么什么时候应该专用化？"],[459.04,468.85,99,"When the task involves modalities beyond text, like pathology slides, EEG or dental images, which general models handle poorly.","当任务涉及文本之外的模态时，比如病理切片、脑电图或牙科影像，通用模型往往处理得不好。"],[469.2,476.49,99,"And where existing models fail; rare diseases are a good example, since general models see too few examples to be reliable.","还有现有模型失效的地方；罕见病就是个好例子，因为通用模型见过的样本太少，不够可靠。"],[476.84,480.9,99,"Then, since training resources are limited, where should we spend them?","其次，既然训练资源有限，我们应该把它们花在哪里？"],[481.25,487.8,99,"On private deployments, where a hospital can't send data to an external API, and on-site training actually improves things.","花在私有化部署上：医院不能把数据发给外部 API，而本地训练确实能带来提升。"],[488.15,493.16,99,"On what most people need: the common conditions with the largest population impact.","花在大多数人需要的地方：影响人群最广的常见病。"],[493.51,497.64,99,"And on social impact: areas that commercial players may neglect.","以及花在有社会影响力的地方：那些商业公司可能忽视的领域。"],[497.99,505.63,99,"These are practical questions, and you should ask them for your own projects too: where does specialization actually buy you something?","这些都是很实际的问题，你们在自己的项目里也应该问一问：专用化到底能给你带来什么？"],[506.88,513.8,100,"So what's the relationship between specialist and generalist models: competition or cooperation?","那么，专用模型和通用模型之间是什么关系：竞争还是合作？"],[514.15,522.2,100,"The figure on the right, from our survey on specialized medical LLMs, maps disease-specific models onto the body.","右边这张图来自我们关于专用医疗大模型的综述，它把针对特定疾病的模型映射到人体上。"],[522.55,530.05,100,"There are models for stroke, Alzheimer's, glaucoma, dental conditions, lung cancer, diabetes and many more.","有针对中风、阿尔茨海默病、青光眼、口腔疾病、肺癌、糖尿病等等的模型。"],[530.4,531.82,100,"There are a lot of them.","数量非常多。"],[532.17,534.77,100,"On the left are the possible relationships.","左边列出的是可能的几种关系。"],[535.12,539.37,100,"Replacement: a generalist eventually makes specialists obsolete.","替代：通用模型最终让专用模型变得过时。"],[539.72,543.46,100,"Routing: a router sends each query to the right specialist.","路由：由一个路由器把每个查询发给合适的专用模型。"],[543.81,551.4,100,"Specialists as tools: a generalist agent calls specialist models like functions, as you saw in the agents lecture.","专用模型作为工具：通用智能体像调用函数一样调用专用模型，就像你们在智能体那一讲里看到的那样。"],[551.75,556.17,100,"Distillation: specialist knowledge is distilled into one big model.","蒸馏：把专用模型的知识蒸馏到一个大模型中。"],[556.52,561.98,100,"And mixture of experts: specialists become experts inside one model.","还有混合专家：专用模型变成一个模型内部的专家。"],[562.33,569.91,100,"I think the realistic near-term answer is mostly cooperative: routing and tools now, distillation over time.","我认为，近期比较现实的答案主要是合作：现在用路由和工具，随着时间推移再做蒸馏。"],[571.16,573.37,101,"Here's divide-and-conquer in practice.","这就是分而治之的实践。"],[573.72,582.95,101,"We build specialist models one at a time: a dental LLM, a TCM LLM, an EEG LLM and a pathology LLM.","我们一个一个地构建专用模型：口腔大模型、中医大模型、脑电大模型和病理大模型。"],[583.3,587.65,101,"We've already seen TCM and EEG; this slide highlights dentistry.","中医和脑电我们之前已经看过了；这张幻灯片重点介绍口腔。"],[588.0,596.09,101,"DentalGPT focuses on complex multimodal diagnosis in dentistry, from intraoral photos and other images.","DentalGPT 专注于口腔领域复杂的多模态诊断，输入包括口内照片和其他影像。"],[596.44,598.23,101,"Look at the affiliations.","看一下作者单位。"],[598.58,608.26,101,"It was built with the University of Hong Kong's Faculty of Dentistry, and the Shenzhen Stomatology Hospital in Pingshan, part of Southern Medical University.","它是和香港大学牙医学院，以及南方医科大学深圳口腔医院坪山院区一起合作完成的。"],[608.61,610.8,101,"That's typical of specialist work.","这在专用模型的工作中很典型。"],[611.15,617.71,101,"You can't do it without clinical partners who have the data, the expertise and the real use case.","没有拥有数据、专业知识和真实应用场景的临床合作伙伴，这件事是做不成的。"],[618.96,625.23,102,"And here's how many specialist models can become one foundation model, through knowledge distillation.","这里展示的是，许多专用模型如何通过知识蒸馏变成一个基础模型。"],[625.58,632.39,102,"On the left are many small medical models, each specialized by department, task or modality.","左边是许多医疗小模型，每一个都针对某个科室、任务或模态做了专门化。"],[632.74,642.87,102,"Lung CT segmentation, retinopathy classification from fundus photos, skin-lesion detection, brain MRI analysis, and pathology classification.","肺部 CT 分割、基于眼底照片的视网膜病变分类、皮肤病变检测、脑部 MRI 分析，以及病理分类。"],[643.22,650.85,102,"In the middle, their knowledge is distilled through soft labels, feature alignment and relational knowledge transfer.","中间部分，它们的知识通过软标签、特征对齐和关系知识迁移被蒸馏出来。"],[651.2,658.99,102,"On the right, one unified multimodal medical foundation model takes CT, MRI, fundus, skin and pathology images, plus text.","右边是一个统一的多模态医疗基础模型，可以接收 CT、MRI、眼底、皮肤和病理图像，以及文本。"],[659.34,666.13,102,"It supports segmentation, classification, detection, report generation and question answering.","它支持分割、分类、检测、报告生成和问答。"],[666.48,668.72,102,"The benefits are listed at the bottom.","底部列出了它的优势。"],[669.07,677.23,102,"It integrates knowledge across specialties, generalizes better, is cheaper to deploy as one system, and is more robust.","它整合了多个专科的知识，泛化能力更强，作为一个统一系统部署成本更低，而且更加稳健。"],[677.58,682.92,102,"That robustness comes because knowledge from different sources reinforces each other.","之所以更稳健，是因为来自不同来源的知识可以相互补充、相互强化。"],[683.27,686.14,102,"That's the bottom-up path made concrete.","这就是把自下而上的路径具体落地了。"],[687.39,689.45,103,"Challenge two: interpretation.","挑战二：可解释性。"],[689.8,693.69,103,"In medicine, a correct answer without an explanation isn't enough.","在医学中，只有正确答案而没有解释是不够的。"],[694.04,699.01,103,"Doctors need to know why, and regulators need to audit decisions.","医生需要知道原因，监管机构也需要审查决策。"],[699.36,706.07,103,"Chain of Diagnosis, or CoD, is our attempt to make a diagnostic agent interpretable.","诊断链，也就是 CoD，是我们让诊断智能体变得可解释的一次尝试。"],[706.42,711.18,103,"Look at the CoD response on the left: it goes through five explicit steps.","看左边的 CoD 回答：它经历了五个明确的步骤。"],[711.53,717.04,103,"Abstract the symptoms, recall candidate diseases, and reason about which one fits.","抽取症状，召回候选疾病，并推理哪种疾病最符合。"],[717.39,721.27,103,"Then assign a confidence to each candidate, and finally decide.","然后为每个候选疾病给出置信度，最后做出决策。"],[721.62,725.84,103,"If the top confidence is above a threshold, it gives a diagnosis.","如果最高置信度超过阈值，就给出诊断。"],[726.19,731.2,103,"If not, it asks the patient about the symptom that would best reduce uncertainty.","如果没有超过，就向患者询问最能降低不确定性的那个症状。"],[731.55,738.66,103,"That symptom is chosen by how much it is expected to reduce the entropy of the confidence distribution.","这个症状的选择依据是：它预计能在多大程度上降低置信度分布的熵。"],[739.01,743.09,103,"So the model shows its reasoning, and knows when it doesn't know enough.","所以，模型会展示它的推理过程，并且知道自己什么时候知道得还不够。"],[743.44,748.36,103,"That's exactly the calibrated property we'll need for trustworthy medical AI.","这正是可信医疗 AI 所需要的“校准”特性。"],[749.61,754.21,104,"A second angle on interpretability is understanding how models generalize.","理解可解释性的第二个角度，是弄清楚模型是如何泛化的。"],[754.56,762.26,104,"We noticed something surprising in medical multimodal models: they could sometimes handle combinations they'd never seen in training.","我们在医疗多模态模型中发现了一件令人惊讶的事：它们有时能处理训练中从未见过的组合。"],[762.61,765.17,104,"The diagram explains it with a cartoon.","这张图用一个卡通例子来解释。"],[765.52,770.6,104,"If you train on white cats and black dogs, can the model recognize a black cat?","如果你用白猫和黑狗来训练，模型能认出黑猫吗？"],[770.95,775.3,104,"That's compositional generalization: recombining known parts.","这就是组合泛化：把已知的部分重新组合起来。"],[775.65,783.03,104,"The medical version: train on MRI images of the brain and CT images of the lung, then test on CT of the brain.","医学版本是：用脑部 MRI 图像和肺部 CT 图像训练，然后在脑部 CT 上测试。"],[783.38,789.56,104,"The model has seen the modality, CT, and the anatomy, brain, but never the two together.","模型见过 CT 这种模态，也见过大脑这个部位，但从未见过两者的组合。"],[789.91,796.34,104,"If models can do this, we don't need training data for every combination of modality, body part and task.","如果模型能做到这一点，我们就不需要为模态、身体部位和任务的每一种组合都准备训练数据。"],[796.69,801.74,104,"That matters a lot in medicine, where the space of combinations is huge.","这在医学中非常重要，因为组合的空间非常巨大。"],[802.99,806.27,105,"To study this systematically, we built Med-MAT.","为了系统地研究这一点，我们构建了 Med-MAT。"],[806.62,810.31,105,"We gathered one hundred and six medical image datasets.","我们收集了一百零六个医学影像数据集。"],[810.66,819.17,105,"Then we labeled every example along three axes: eleven modalities, fourteen anatomical areas, and thirteen task types.","然后我们沿着三个维度给每个样本打标签：十一种模态、十四个解剖部位和十三种任务类型。"],[819.52,825.4,105,"Each dataset was turned into a uniform question-answer format, as in the middle of the figure.","每个数据集都被转换成统一的问答格式，就像图中间展示的那样。"],[825.75,831.78,105,"With every sample tagged by modality, area and task, you can design controlled experiments.","每个样本都标注了模态、部位和任务，你就可以设计受控实验。"],[832.13,838.94,105,"Train on certain combinations, hold out others, and test whether the model generalizes to the held-out ones.","在某些组合上训练，留出另一些组合，然后测试模型能否泛化到留出的组合上。"],[839.29,843.63,105,"The experiments showed clear and significant compositional generalization.","实验显示出了清晰而显著的组合泛化效应。"],[843.98,853.12,105,"That's both an interpretability result, telling us how these models generalize, and a practical recipe for choosing training data efficiently.","这既是一个可解释性方面的结论，告诉我们这些模型如何泛化，也是一个高效选择训练数据的实用方法。"],[854.37,856.52,106,"Challenge three: benchmarking.","挑战三：基准评测。"],[856.87,861.02,106,"We've seen why it's hard; here's what the community is building.","我们已经看到了它为什么困难；下面看看社区正在构建什么。"],[861.37,871.18,106,"Agent benchmarks, like GAIA and the medical portion of Humanity's Last Exam, test multi-step problem solving rather than single answers.","智能体基准，比如 GAIA 和“人类最后的考试”中的医学部分，考察的是多步骤解决问题，而不是单个答案。"],[871.53,875.3,106,"Then there are HealthBench-style rubrics, shown on the right.","然后是 HealthBench 风格的评分细则，如右图所示。"],[875.65,885.11,106,"For each case, doctors write criteria with points, like advising to call emergency services immediately, worth plus ten points.","对每个案例，医生会写出带分值的评分标准，比如“建议立即呼叫急救服务”，加十分。"],[885.46,889.19,106,"Then a model grades the response against those criteria.","然后由一个模型根据这些标准给回答打分。"],[889.54,896.13,106,"We'd like to extend this with multilingual criteria, specialized medical areas, and multi-turn evaluations.","我们希望在此基础上扩展：加入多语言标准、专科医学领域，以及多轮对话评测。"],[896.48,903.01,106,"LiveClinical, which we'll see later as LiveClin, keeps refreshing its cases, so there's no data leakage.","LiveClinical，也就是后面会看到的 LiveClin，会不断更新病例，因此不存在数据泄露。"],[903.36,907.63,106,"And arena-style benchmarks let users compare models head to head.","而竞技场式的基准让用户可以对模型进行一对一的比较。"],[907.98,917.2,106,"Notice how each one answers one of the limitations from earlier: difficulty, interactivity, leakage, and expert judgment at scale.","注意，每一种都回应了前面提到的一个局限：难度、交互性、数据泄露，以及规模化的专家评判。"]]},{"n":8,"title":"From Models to Environments: Patients and Hospitals","blurb":"Why models alone may hit a wall: AI standardized patients, patient trajectories and clinical world models, and the agentic, digitalized hospital as a sandbox.","file":"lecture09_part8.mp4","poster":"lecture09_part8.jpg","duration":1200.2,"first":107,"last":127,"slides":[{"n":107,"title":"6 Our Vision: From Models to Environments","t":0.8},{"n":108,"title":"Trustworthy Medical AI: The Necessary Intermediate Step","t":48.48},{"n":109,"title":"Has the Model Alone Hit a Wall?","t":117.89},{"n":110,"title":"An Environment Stack for Medicine","t":192.59},{"n":111,"title":"Model–Environment Co-Evolution","t":260.89},{"n":112,"title":"6.1 Scaling Standardized Patients","t":318.35},{"n":113,"title":"Scaling Standardized Patients with AI","t":346.33},{"n":114,"title":"Virtual Patients for Medical Education","t":427.59},{"n":115,"title":"Application: AI Standardized Patients for Medical Training","t":482.56},{"n":116,"title":"6.2 Patient Trajectories and Clinical World Models","t":544.06},{"n":117,"title":"A Patient Is a Trajectory, Not a Vignette","t":568.53},{"n":118,"title":"Clinical World Models","t":631.21},{"n":119,"title":"Clinical World Model: Sepsis Case Study","t":701.68},{"n":120,"title":"6.3 The Agentic Hospital","t":769.38},{"n":121,"title":"The Agentic Hospital: Four Layers of Simulation","t":794.28},{"n":122,"title":"Hospital Simulation: Who Pays in an Aging Society?","t":861.97},{"n":123,"title":"Why Connect to a Real Hospital Information System (HIS)?","t":929.9},{"n":124,"title":"Digitalized Hospital: Simulating the Full Clinical Workflow","t":977.11},{"n":125,"title":"A Sandbox for Hospital Operations","t":1052.6},{"n":126,"title":"Digitalized Hospitals as a Tool for Agents","t":1100.04},{"n":127,"title":"A Sandbox for AI Applications","t":1146.35}],"sents":[[0.8,9.12,107,"We've covered why medical AI, our HuatuoGPT story, the GMAI goal, the capability roadmap and the challenges.","我们已经讲了为什么要做医疗 AI、华佗GPT 的故事、GMAI 的目标、能力路线图以及面临的挑战。"],[9.47,11.77,107,"Now for what I think comes next.","接下来谈谈我认为下一步会是什么。"],[12.12,16.66,107,"My claim is that models trained on static text are reaching their limit.","我的观点是：在静态文本上训练的模型正在接近它们的极限。"],[17.01,23.15,107,"The next leap will come from environments where medical AI can act, fail safely and learn.","下一次飞跃将来自环境，在那里医疗 AI 可以行动、安全地犯错并从中学习。"],[23.5,27.87,107,"This part has seven short sections, going up and down a stack.","这一部分有七个小节，会在一个层级结构中上下穿梭。"],[28.22,35.02,107,"Simulated patients, patient trajectories and clinical world models, and an agentic hospital.","模拟病人，病人轨迹和临床世界模型，以及智能体医院。"],[35.37,41.85,107,"Then virtual cells and organs, community evidence, the infrastructure under all of it.","然后是虚拟细胞和器官，社区证据，以及支撑这一切的基础设施。"],[42.2,47.08,107,"And finally, how environments feed back into better foundation models.","最后是环境如何反哺出更好的基础模型。"],[48.33,54.99,108,"Before environments, let me place trust on the map, because it's the bridge between today and the final goal.","在讲环境之前，我先把“可信”放到地图上，因为它是连接今天和最终目标的桥梁。"],[55.34,62.96,108,"On the left is where we are today: capable but unverified LLMs, good at exams, unproven in care.","左边是我们今天所处的位置：能力很强但未经验证的大模型，擅长考试，但在临床照护中尚未得到证明。"],[63.31,67.58,108,"On the right is the final goal: generalist medical AI.","右边是最终目标：通用医疗人工智能。"],[67.93,76.0,108,"In the middle is the necessary intermediate step: trustworthy medical AI, narrower in scope, but safe to use today.","中间是必要的中间步骤：可信医疗 AI，范围更窄，但今天就可以安全使用。"],[76.35,80.05,108,"What does trustworthy mean concretely? Four properties.","“可信”具体意味着什么？四个特性。"],[80.4,85.23,108,"Evidence-grounded: every claim can be traced to a guideline or the literature.","有证据支撑：每一个论断都可以追溯到指南或文献。"],[85.58,90.59,108,"Calibrated: it knows when it doesn't know, and asks or refers.","经过校准：它知道自己什么时候不知道，并会追问或转诊。"],[90.94,96.16,108,"Auditable: its reasoning and actions are logged and can be reviewed.","可审计：它的推理和行动都有记录，可以被审查。"],[96.51,101.12,108,"Bounded: clear scope, permissions and human oversight.","有边界：清晰的范围、权限，以及人类监督。"],[101.47,105.1,108,"Why not jump straight to GMAI? Read the box at the bottom.","为什么不直接跳到 GMAI？看看底部这个框。"],[105.45,112.24,108,"Trust earns deployment, deployment earns real feedback and data, and that feedback makes the next model more general.","信任带来部署，部署带来真实的反馈和数据，而这些反馈让下一个模型更加通用。"],[112.59,116.49,108,"It's a flywheel, and trust is what starts it turning.","这是一个飞轮，而信任就是让它转起来的那股力量。"],[117.74,122.33,109,"Here's the core argument for environments. Has the model alone hit a wall?","这是支持环境的核心论点。单靠模型本身，是不是已经撞墙了？"],[122.68,125.9,109,"On the left is what static data gave us.","左边是静态数据带给我们的东西。"],[126.25,134.77,109,"Medical exam QA is close to saturated; top models score above ninety percent on MedQA-style tests.","医学考试问答已接近饱和；顶尖模型在 MedQA 类测试上的得分超过百分之九十。"],[135.12,140.72,109,"Public medical text is largely used up, and the private data is locked in hospitals.","公开的医学文本已经基本用尽，而私有数据被锁在医院里。"],[141.07,144.68,109,"And exam scores don't predict bedside performance.","而且考试分数并不能预测床旁的实际表现。"],[145.03,147.81,109,"On the right is what real medicine requires.","右边是真实医疗所需要的东西。"],[148.16,154.87,109,"Interaction under incomplete information: asking, examining, ordering tests.","在信息不完整的情况下进行交互：问诊、查体、开检查。"],[155.22,159.3,109,"Sequential decisions whose effects unfold over hours or years.","序贯决策，其效果会在数小时乃至数年中逐渐显现。"],[159.65,163.67,109,"Working inside teams, systems, rules and payment schemes.","在团队、系统、规章和支付体系中工作。"],[164.02,167.58,109,"And learning from outcomes, not from answer keys.","以及从结果中学习，而不是从标准答案中学习。"],[167.93,171.61,109,"None of the right-hand column exists in a static dataset.","右边这一列的内容，没有一项存在于静态数据集中。"],[171.96,179.74,109,"It has to be learned by acting in an environment, which is exactly the era of experience argument from Silver and Sutton.","它必须通过在环境中行动来学习，这正是 Silver 和 Sutton 提出的“经验时代”的观点。"],[180.09,183.58,109,"So the environment is what we must build.","所以，环境才是我们必须构建的东西。"],[183.93,191.19,109,"If you remember the agentic RL part of Lecture six, this is the same idea: the environment defines what the agent can learn.","如果你还记得第六讲中智能体强化学习的部分，这是同一个思想：环境决定了智能体能学到什么。"],[192.44,194.17,110,"What environments do we need?","我们需要什么样的环境？"],[194.52,202.43,110,"This slide organizes them as a stack, from small to large scale, with the section where each one comes up on the right.","这张幻灯片把它们组织成一个层级结构，从小尺度到大尺度，右边标出了每一层对应的小节。"],[202.78,209.77,110,"At the bottom, cells and molecules: perturbations, drugs and genes, which means virtual cells.","最底层是细胞和分子：扰动、药物和基因，对应的是虚拟细胞。"],[210.12,216.44,110,"Then organs: physiology, imaging and response to therapy, which means virtual organs.","然后是器官：生理、影像和对治疗的反应，对应的是虚拟器官。"],[216.79,224.76,110,"Then the patient: dialogue, symptoms and vital-sign trajectories, which means standardized patients and clinical world models.","然后是病人：对话、症状和生命体征轨迹，对应的是标准化病人和临床世界模型。"],[225.11,233.32,110,"Then the hospital: workflows, teams, the hospital information system and payments, which means the agentic hospital.","然后是医院：工作流程、团队、医院信息系统和支付，对应的是智能体医院。"],[233.67,242.72,110,"And at the top, community and society: evidence, guidelines and public health, which means community evidence-based medicine.","最顶层是社区和社会：证据、指南和公共卫生，对应的是基于社区的循证医学。"],[243.07,246.02,110,"The sentence at the bottom is the unifying idea.","底部这句话是统一的核心思想。"],[246.37,254.7,110,"Every layer is an environment where agents, human or AI doctors, can act, receive feedback and improve.","每一层都是一个环境，智能体，无论是人类医生还是 AI 医生，都可以在其中行动、获得反馈并不断改进。"],[255.05,259.49,110,"We'll go through them roughly from the patient outward, then down to cells.","我们大致从病人这一层向外讲，然后再往下讲到细胞。"],[260.74,264.7,111,"And here's why environments matter so much: they set up a loop.","这就是环境如此重要的原因：它们构成了一个循环。"],[265.05,270.79,111,"Start at the top: environments, like simulated patients, hospitals and cells.","从顶部开始：环境，比如模拟病人、医院和细胞。"],[271.14,277.51,111,"They generate tasks and feedback, meaning verifiable outcomes and rubric-based rewards.","它们产生任务和反馈，也就是可验证的结果和基于评分细则的奖励。"],[277.86,281.61,111,"Training with RL inside those environments produces better models.","在这些环境中用强化学习训练，就能得到更好的模型。"],[281.96,285.06,111,"Better models in turn power better simulators.","更好的模型反过来又能驱动更好的模拟器。"],[285.41,290.96,111,"A stronger model makes a more realistic simulated patient, or a more faithful world model.","更强的模型能做出更逼真的模拟病人，或者更忠实的世界模型。"],[291.31,295.66,111,"And better simulators make better environments, so the loop continues.","更好的模拟器又造就更好的环境，循环就这样继续下去。"],[296.01,302.28,111,"The phrase in the center is the key claim: recursive self-improvement, grounded in medicine.","中间这句话是关键论点：扎根于医学的递归式自我改进。"],[302.63,307.05,111,"At this point the model is no longer the bottleneck; the environment is.","到了这个阶段，瓶颈不再是模型，而是环境。"],[307.4,313.35,111,"Whoever builds the best medical environments will be able to train the best medical models.","谁能构建最好的医疗环境，谁就能训练出最好的医疗模型。"],[313.7,316.95,111,"That's why our group is investing heavily here.","这就是我们团队在这方面大力投入的原因。"],[318.2,320.42,112,"Let's start with the patient layer.","我们从病人这一层开始。"],[320.77,328.82,112,"Diagnosis is an interactive problem: you learn it by talking to patients, asking the right questions, and noticing what's missing.","诊断是一个交互式的问题：你要通过和病人交谈、问对问题、注意到缺失的信息来学会它。"],[329.17,334.79,112,"Both medical students and AI doctors need many realistic patients to practise on.","无论是医学生还是 AI 医生，都需要大量逼真的病人来练习。"],[335.14,339.65,112,"And real patients obviously can't be used as practice material.","而真实的病人显然不能被当作练习材料。"],[340.0,344.93,112,"The answer is simulated, standardized patients, at scale.","答案就是大规模的模拟标准化病人。"],[346.18,357.45,113,"In medical schools, standardized patients are trained actors who play a patient with a specific case, so students can practise history-taking and communication.","在医学院里，标准化病人是经过训练的演员，他们扮演患有特定疾病的病人，让学生练习问诊和沟通。"],[357.8,364.05,113,"Look at the why box: actors are costly, scarce and usually limited to common cases.","看左边的“为什么”框：演员成本高、数量少，而且通常只能演常见病例。"],[364.4,367.33,113,"Diagnosis is learned by talking to many patients.","诊断是通过和很多病人交谈学会的。"],[367.68,372.33,113,"And AI doctors also need patients to practise on, safely.","而且 AI 医生也需要可以安全练习的病人。"],[372.68,377.97,113,"On the right is how we build an AI standardized patient, in four layers.","右边是我们构建 AI 标准化病人的方法，分为四层。"],[378.32,385.47,113,"First, a case card from real records: history, findings, and hidden answers the student has to discover.","第一，来自真实病历的病例卡：病史、检查结果，以及学生需要去发现的隐藏答案。"],[385.82,390.87,113,"Second, a persona: age, culture, emotion and health literacy.","第二，人设：年龄、文化、情绪和健康素养。"],[391.22,398.23,113,"That matters because the same disease presents differently in an anxious grandmother and a stoic young man.","这很重要，因为同一种疾病，在一位焦虑的老奶奶和一位隐忍的年轻人身上，表现会很不一样。"],[398.58,405.92,113,"Third, voice and face: our HealthTTS, TalkVid and MedGen work, so patients sound and look ill.","第三，声音和面孔：用我们的 HealthTTS、TalkVid 和 MedGen 工作，让病人听起来、看起来都像真的生病了。"],[406.27,413.49,113,"And fourth, realism checks, co-designed with medical learners in a CHI two thousand twenty-six study.","第四，真实性检验，这是在一项 CHI 二零二六的研究中与医学学习者共同设计的。"],[413.84,420.21,113,"The bottom box is the scaling idea: diseases times personas times languages times difficulty.","底部的框是规模化的思路：疾病乘以人设，乘以语言，再乘以难度。"],[420.56,426.19,113,"And the same patients can train students, train AI doctors, and evaluate both.","而且同一批病人既可以训练学生，也可以训练 AI 医生，还能同时评估两者。"],[427.44,431.24,114,"Here's what that looks like as a product for medical education.","这是它作为医学教育产品的样子。"],[431.59,433.99,114,"Each phone screen is part of the app.","每一个手机屏幕都是这个应用的一部分。"],[434.34,441.08,114,"The first screen is a consultation in progress: the virtual patient is an elderly woman with a cough.","第一个屏幕是正在进行的问诊：虚拟病人是一位咳嗽的老奶奶。"],[441.43,448.23,114,"The student asks questions in a chat, with a limited number of questions, as you can see from the counter at the top.","学生在聊天中提问，提问次数是有限的，你可以从上方的计数器看到。"],[448.58,455.99,114,"The second screen is the case introduction: repeated cough and phlegm for five years, and fever for the last ten days.","第二个屏幕是病例介绍：反复咳嗽咳痰五年，近期伴发热十天。"],[456.34,461.89,114,"The third is the student's history of practice cases, each with a score.","第三个是学生的练习病例记录，每个病例都有一个分数。"],[462.24,467.15,114,"The fourth is a follow-up quiz on the knowledge points the student got wrong.","第四个是针对学生答错的知识点进行的后续测验。"],[467.5,475.71,114,"Everything is built in-house: MedGen for video, TTS-LoRAHub for speech, and HeadVid for audio-driven digital humans.","所有技术都是自研的：用 MedGen 生成视频，用 TTS-LoRAHub 合成语音，用 HeadVid 生成音频驱动的数字人。"],[476.06,481.16,114,"That stack lets us create patients that look, sound and behave realistically.","这套技术栈让我们能创造出在外表、声音和行为上都很逼真的病人。"],[482.41,490.47,115,"And here's an application already in use at a partner university, Anhui University of Science and Technology.","这里有一个已经在合作高校安徽理工大学投入使用的应用。"],[490.82,501.03,115,"The idea in the top banner: simulate the entire consultation with AI to train clinical thinking, using virtual patients plus real-time feedback.","顶部横幅里的理念是：用 AI 模拟整个问诊过程来训练临床思维，结合虚拟病人和实时反馈。"],[501.38,508.51,115,"On the right is the interface: a chat with the patient on the left, and a body diagram in the middle for the physical exam.","右边是界面：左侧是和病人的对话，中间是用于体格检查的人体图。"],[508.86,515.79,115,"Patient information and an AI teaching assistant on the right give feedback as the student works.","右侧是病人信息和一个 AI 助教，在学生操作的过程中给出反馈。"],[516.14,518.06,115,"The teaching value is on the left.","左边是教学价值。"],[518.41,523.77,115,"For students: practise diagnostic reasoning, and reduce missed or wrong diagnoses.","对学生来说：练习诊断推理，减少漏诊和误诊。"],[524.12,530.6,115,"For teachers: lower costs than hiring standardized-patient actors, and teaching that is digital and traceable.","对老师来说：比雇用标准化病人演员成本更低，教学过程也是数字化、可追溯的。"],[530.95,536.69,115,"The goals include full-workflow feasibility, effective feedback and live demonstration.","目标包括：全流程可行、有效反馈和现场演示。"],[537.04,542.66,115,"Plus real-time correction, analysis of the student's reasoning, and personalized practice.","还有实时纠错、学生推理过程分析，以及个性化练习。"],[543.91,546.91,116,"Standardized patients capture one consultation.","标准化病人捕捉的是一次问诊。"],[547.26,555.97,116,"But a patient isn't a static vignette; the body responds to every action we take, and it changes over hours and days.","但病人不是一个静态的病例片段；身体会对我们采取的每一个行动做出反应，并在数小时乃至数天内不断变化。"],[556.32,562.63,116,"To train agents that make treatment decisions, models must learn how patient states evolve over time.","要训练能做治疗决策的智能体，模型必须学会病人状态如何随时间演变。"],[562.98,567.13,116,"That's the idea of patient trajectories and clinical world models.","这就是病人轨迹和临床世界模型的思想。"],[568.38,572.75,117,"Here's an illustrative example: a septic-shock patient.","这里有一个示意性的例子：一位感染性休克病人。"],[573.1,574.51,117,"Time runs to the right.","时间轴向右延伸。"],[574.86,578.62,117,"The red line is mean arterial pressure, or MAP.","红线是平均动脉压，也就是 MAP。"],[578.97,583.44,117,"The gray line is lactate, a marker of tissue under-perfusion.","灰线是乳酸，它是组织灌注不足的标志物。"],[583.79,589.3,117,"At first, MAP falls and lactate rises: the patient is deteriorating.","一开始，MAP 下降、乳酸上升：病人在恶化。"],[589.65,593.87,117,"At the dashed line, the team gives fluids and a vasopressor.","在虚线处，医疗团队给予了补液和血管升压药。"],[594.22,598.37,117,"Afterwards, MAP recovers and lactate gradually falls.","之后，MAP 回升，乳酸逐渐下降。"],[598.72,603.64,117,"The response isn't instant; it unfolds over time, and it's noisy.","这种反应不是即时的；它随着时间逐步展开，而且带有噪声。"],[603.99,605.38,117,"That's the right-hand box.","这就是右边这个框要说的。"],[605.73,611.51,117,"A model must learn state, action, next state, with delayed and noisy treatment effects.","模型必须学会“状态、动作、下一个状态”，以及延迟且带噪声的治疗效果。"],[611.86,614.09,117,"Exam questions never ask for this.","考试题目从来不会考这些。"],[614.44,622.67,117,"To scale it, we need trajectories: ICU records like the MIMIC database, physiology simulators, and learned generators.","要实现规模化，我们需要轨迹数据：像 MIMIC 数据库这样的 ICU 记录、生理模拟器，以及学习得到的生成器。"],[623.02,629.81,117,"Scaling patients really means scaling physiology over time, which is the data a sequential decision maker needs.","规模化病人，本质上就是规模化随时间变化的生理过程，这正是序贯决策者所需要的数据。"],[631.06,633.66,118,"That leads to clinical world models.","这就引出了临床世界模型。"],[634.01,641.81,118,"The formula at the top is the whole idea: the next state, s t plus one, is sampled from W of s t and a t.","顶部的公式就是全部思想：下一个状态 s t 加一，是从 W 关于 s t 和 a t 的分布中采样得到的。"],[642.16,648.2,118,"In words: given the patient's current state and an action, predict how the patient will respond.","换句话说：给定病人当前的状态和一个动作，预测病人会如何反应。"],[648.55,653.08,118,"It's the same world-model idea from RL, now applied to patients.","这和强化学习中的世界模型思想是一样的，只是现在用在了病人身上。"],[653.43,655.42,118,"The four boxes define each part.","这四个框分别定义了每个部分。"],[655.77,660.54,118,"The state is vitals, labs, notes, images and history.","状态是生命体征、化验结果、病历记录、影像和病史。"],[660.89,666.41,118,"The action is a clinical order: tests, drugs, fluids, procedures.","动作是临床医嘱：检查、用药、补液和操作。"],[666.76,672.29,118,"The transition W is learned from electronic health records plus physiology knowledge.","转移函数 W 是从电子病历加上生理学知识中学习得到的。"],[672.64,677.1,118,"The reward is the outcome: stabilization, survival, cost.","奖励就是结果：病情稳定、存活和费用。"],[677.45,679.16,118,"And here's what you can do with it.","下面是你能用它做的事情。"],[679.51,684.09,118,"Train: run RL for clinical agents without risk to real patients.","训练：为临床智能体做强化学习，而不会给真实病人带来风险。"],[684.44,689.69,118,"Ask what if: compare counterfactual treatments for the same patient.","提问“如果……会怎样”：对同一个病人比较反事实的治疗方案。"],[690.04,694.23,118,"Evaluate: score agents on outcomes, not answer keys.","评估：根据结果给智能体打分，而不是根据标准答案。"],[694.58,700.28,118,"The red line at the bottom sums it up: the agent proposes, the world model answers.","底部的红字做了总结：智能体提出方案，世界模型给出回应。"],[701.53,705.18,119,"Here's a concrete case study from our group, on sepsis.","这是我们团队关于脓毒症的一个具体案例研究。"],[705.53,713.25,119,"On the left is the initial state: septic shock, MAP fifty-eight and falling, lactate two point eight and rising.","左边是初始状态：感染性休克，MAP 为五十八且在下降，乳酸为二点八且在上升。"],[713.6,717.37,119,"In the middle is the loop between the agent and the world model.","中间是智能体和世界模型之间的交互循环。"],[717.72,723.19,119,"The SepsisAgent assesses the patient and proposes three treatment options.","SepsisAgent 先评估病人，然后提出三个治疗方案。"],[723.54,727.21,119,"For each option, the world model simulates the result.","对每个方案，世界模型都会模拟出结果。"],[727.56,734.55,119,"Option one leads to MAP seventy-two and lactate one point eight, which looks good.","方案一使 MAP 达到七十二，乳酸降到一点八，看起来不错。"],[734.9,739.84,119,"Option two leaves MAP around fifty-eight, and option three makes things worse.","方案二让 MAP 停留在五十八左右，而方案三让情况变得更糟。"],[740.19,746.17,119,"The agent picks the best option as the final treatment, and the world model produces the next state.","智能体选择最好的方案作为最终治疗，世界模型再生成下一个状态。"],[746.52,752.94,119,"On the right, the patient is stabilized: MAP up to seventy-two, lactate down to one point eight.","右边，病人病情稳定了：MAP 升到七十二，乳酸降到一点八。"],[753.29,759.89,119,"The design pattern is important: the LLM agent doesn't have to know the physiology perfectly by itself.","这个设计模式很重要：大模型智能体不必自己完美地掌握生理学知识。"],[760.24,767.98,119,"It can imagine, simulate and compare before acting, the way a careful clinician mentally runs scenarios.","它可以在行动之前先想象、模拟和比较，就像一位细心的临床医生在脑海中推演各种情况一样。"],[769.23,770.78,120,"Patients are one layer.","病人只是其中一层。"],[771.13,779.09,120,"But medicine happens in workflows: triage, consultations, tests, prescriptions and payments, across departments and people.","但医疗是在工作流程中进行的：分诊、问诊、检查、开药和付费，跨越不同的科室和人员。"],[779.44,782.78,120,"For AI to help, it has to enter those workflows.","AI 要想帮上忙，就必须进入这些流程。"],[783.13,790.69,120,"That's risky to do directly, so the plan is to first build simulated hospitals that speak the language of real ones.","直接这样做风险很大，所以计划是先构建模拟医院，让它们说真实医院的“语言”。"],[791.04,792.88,120,"That's the agentic hospital.","这就是智能体医院。"],[794.13,797.45,121,"An agentic hospital needs four layers of simulation.","一个智能体医院需要四层模拟。"],[797.8,805.96,121,"People: virtual patients and doctors with realistic audio and video, using HealthTTS, TalkVid and MedGen.","人：拥有逼真音视频的虚拟病人和医生，用到了 HealthTTS、TalkVid 和 MedGen。"],[806.31,812.2,121,"Social interaction: the dialogue, reports, orders and payments between all those roles.","社会交互：所有这些角色之间的对话、报告、医嘱和付费。"],[812.55,819.55,121,"Physical space: a 3D hospital reconstructed from floor plans and drone video, using Gaussian splatting.","物理空间：利用高斯泼溅技术，从平面图和无人机视频重建出三维医院。"],[819.9,828.0,121,"And world mechanisms: insurance, triage, scheduling, and the incentives of both people and institutions.","以及世界机制：医保、分诊、排班，以及个人和机构双方的激励。"],[828.35,835.49,121,"The most important design choice is in the box: the bridge is a real hospital information system, the HIS.","最重要的设计选择在这个框里：桥梁是一个真实的医院信息系统，也就是 HIS。"],[835.84,845.16,121,"If all our simulated hospitals speak the same HIS language as real hospitals, any tool built in simulation can plug into a real hospital.","如果我们所有的模拟医院都和真实医院说同一种 HIS 语言，那么在模拟中构建的任何工具都能直接接入真实医院。"],[845.51,854.9,121,"Related work worth knowing: Agent Hospital from Tsinghua, in two thousand twenty-four, trains doctor agents on simulated patients.","值得了解的相关工作：清华大学二零二四年的 Agent Hospital，用模拟病人来训练医生智能体。"],[855.25,860.57,121,"Our emphasis is on connecting the simulation to real hospital systems.","我们的重点是把模拟和真实的医院系统连接起来。"],[861.82,865.93,122,"Why simulate the world mechanisms, not just the medicine?","为什么要模拟世界机制，而不只是医学本身？"],[866.28,871.12,122,"Because in an aging society, the hard problem is often who pays.","因为在老龄化社会中，难题往往是谁来买单。"],[871.47,875.37,122,"On the left are the modules of a hospital information system.","左边是医院信息系统的各个模块。"],[875.72,880.44,122,"Clinical modules for outpatient, inpatient, nursing and electronic records.","临床模块，包括门诊、住院、护理和电子病历。"],[880.79,885.46,122,"Financial modules for billing, pricing and the health-insurance interface.","财务模块，包括收费、价格管理和医保接口。"],[885.81,891.62,122,"Then pharmacy management, and others like medical records, materials and human resources.","然后是药品管理，以及病案、物资和人力资源等其他模块。"],[891.97,895.27,122,"Medicine and money are woven together in the same system.","医疗和资金在同一个系统里交织在一起。"],[895.62,899.9,122,"On the right are the stakeholders, and their often conflicting goals.","右边是各方利益相关者，以及他们常常相互冲突的目标。"],[900.25,904.97,122,"Government sets medical policy, outputs, payments and assessments.","政府负责医疗政策，关注产出、支付和考核。"],[905.32,912.22,122,"Hospitals care about throughput, service lines, workflows, resources, and revenue versus cost.","医院关心吞吐量、服务产品线、服务流程、医疗资源，以及收益与成本。"],[912.57,916.35,122,"Doctors care about value, quality and cost.","医生关心价值、质量和成本。"],[916.7,920.78,122,"Patients want fair access, good quality and reasonable fees.","病人希望公平可及、质量良好、费用合理。"],[921.13,928.5,122,"A hospital simulation lets you test how a policy or an AI tool shifts that balance before you try it for real.","医院模拟让你在真正实施之前，就能测试一项政策或一个 AI 工具会如何改变这种平衡。"],[929.75,935.7,123,"So why insist on connecting to a real hospital information system, rather than building a clean toy one?","那么，为什么坚持连接真实的医院信息系统，而不是搭一个干净的玩具系统？"],[936.05,941.14,123,"Because then data move seamlessly between the virtual and the real hospital.","因为这样一来，数据就可以在虚拟医院和真实医院之间无缝流动。"],[941.49,946.79,123,"And any AI tool built in the virtual hospital plugs directly into the real system.","而且在虚拟医院中构建的任何 AI 工具，都可以直接接入真实系统。"],[947.14,950.16,123,"No rewrite, no new integration project.","不需要重写，也不需要新的集成项目。"],[950.51,960.04,123,"And this isn't hypothetical: CUHK-Shenzhen Hospital has deployed a real HIS on our university servers, with controlled sample data.","而且这不是假设：港中大（深圳）医院已经在我们大学的服务器上部署了一套真实的 HIS，使用受控的样本数据。"],[960.39,967.06,123,"So our students and agents can work against the same software real clinicians use, without touching real patient records.","所以我们的学生和智能体可以使用真实临床医生所用的同一套软件，而不会接触到真实的病人记录。"],[967.41,970.93,123,"Sim-to-real transfer is a well-known problem in robotics.","从仿真到现实的迁移，是机器人领域一个众所周知的难题。"],[971.28,975.71,123,"Using the real system's interface is how we keep that gap small for hospitals.","使用真实系统的接口，就是我们在医院场景中缩小这一差距的方法。"],[976.96,980.18,124,"Here's the digitalized hospital in more detail.","这里更详细地展示了数字化医院。"],[980.53,991.05,124,"On the left, the HIS at the center connects all the roles: triage, doctors, instruments, wards, pharmacy, insurance and patients.","左边，位于中心的 HIS 连接了所有角色：分诊、医生、仪器、病房、药房、医保和病人。"],[991.4,994.13,124,"On the right is the full outpatient workflow.","右边是完整的门诊流程。"],[994.48,1000.79,124,"The patient arrives, gets triage guidance, sees the doctor, pays, collects medicine and leaves.","病人到达，接受导诊分诊，看医生，付费，取药，然后离开。"],[1001.14,1009.06,124,"Each step expands into sub-steps, like pre-consultation and registration, and insurance versus self-pay.","每一步都会展开成子步骤，比如预问诊和挂号，以及医保支付还是个人支付。"],[1009.41,1012.77,124,"There is also prescription and queuing at the pharmacy.","还有药房的处方和排队取药。"],[1013.12,1018.07,124,"The top row adds branches for tests, follow-up visits and hospitalization.","最上面一行增加了检查、复诊和住院的分支。"],[1018.42,1022.09,124,"Why go to this trouble? Because of what we learned in deployment.","为什么要费这么大功夫？因为我们在部署中学到了经验。"],[1022.44,1029.89,124,"HuatuoGPT is connected to twelve public hospitals and around two hundred community health centers in Longgang.","华佗GPT 已接入龙岗区的十二家公立医院和大约两百家社区健康服务中心。"],[1030.24,1035.65,124,"It is used for pre-triage, pre-consultation and family-doctor services.","它被用于预分诊、预问诊和家庭医生服务。"],[1036.0,1043.36,124,"But real hospital systems are complex and heterogeneous, so embedding AI is hard.","但真实的医院系统复杂且异构，所以嵌入 AI 很困难。"],[1043.71,1051.2,124,"The strategy is to harden full-workflow AI in a virtual hospital first, then migrate it gradually into real ones.","我们的策略是先在虚拟医院中把全流程 AI 打磨成熟，再逐步迁移到真实医院。"],[1052.45,1058.4,125,"Once you have a digital hospital, you can ask operational questions that are hard to test in a real one.","一旦有了数字医院，你就可以提出一些在真实医院里很难测试的运营问题。"],[1058.75,1059.81,125,"Here's an example.","这里有一个例子。"],[1060.16,1064.02,125,"In many clinics, a human assistant does pre-consultation.","在很多诊所里，有一位人工助理负责预问诊。"],[1064.37,1071.45,125,"The patient checks in, the assistant collects information, then routes them to a doctor's office, like the picture on the right.","病人登记后，助理收集信息，再把病人分配到某个医生的诊室，就像右边这张图一样。"],[1071.8,1073.18,125,"Is that step worth it?","这一步值得吗？"],[1073.53,1075.59,125,"What happens if we remove the assistant?","如果去掉这个助理会怎样？"],[1075.94,1082.35,125,"Can AI replace it, and with what trade-offs in waiting time, accuracy and doctor workload?","AI 能取代它吗？在等待时间、准确性和医生工作量上又有哪些取舍？"],[1082.7,1088.81,125,"And does the answer differ across departments? Pediatrics may need it more than dermatology, for example.","答案在不同科室会不同吗？比如，儿科可能比皮肤科更需要这一步。"],[1089.16,1094.62,125,"In a real hospital, each of these is a risky experiment with real patients.","在真实医院里，每一个这样的问题都是一次对真实病人有风险的实验。"],[1094.97,1098.64,125,"In a sandbox, it's a simulation you can run a thousand times.","而在沙盒里，它只是一次可以运行一千遍的模拟。"],[1099.89,1104.34,126,"The sandbox works for agents too, not only for human planners.","这个沙盒不仅适用于人类规划者，也适用于智能体。"],[1104.69,1109.17,126,"Here, the digitalized hospital becomes a tool that agents use.","在这里，数字化医院变成了智能体使用的工具。"],[1109.52,1118.18,126,"An agent can try an operational or management strategy, such as a new triage rule, a scheduling change or a staffing plan.","智能体可以尝试一种运营或管理策略，比如新的分诊规则、排班调整或人员配置方案。"],[1118.53,1124.75,126,"It sees what happens in the simulated hospital, reflects on the feedback, and adjusts.","它观察模拟医院里发生了什么，对反馈进行反思，然后做出调整。"],[1125.1,1131.95,126,"Connect this to Lecture seven: the agent's harness now includes an entire hospital simulation as its environment.","把这和第七讲联系起来：智能体的运行框架现在把整个医院模拟当作它的环境。"],[1132.3,1138.06,126,"The agent proposes, the hospital responds, and the agent learns from the outcome.","智能体提出方案，医院做出回应，智能体再从结果中学习。"],[1138.41,1144.95,126,"It's the same loop as the clinical world model, just at the scale of an institution instead of one patient.","这和临床世界模型是同一个循环，只是尺度从一个病人变成了一个机构。"],[1146.2,1151.67,127,"And of course the sandbox is a place to develop AI applications themselves.","当然，沙盒也是开发 AI 应用本身的地方。"],[1152.02,1157.6,127,"Here's a concrete one: medical-record writing, which takes up a huge share of doctors' time.","这里有一个具体例子：病历书写，它占用了医生大量的时间。"],[1157.95,1164.97,127,"The plan is to train with rubric-based RL, where the rubric comes directly from the official requirements for medical records.","计划是用基于评分细则的强化学习来训练，评分细则直接来自官方的病历书写要求。"],[1165.32,1172.3,127,"The score comes from the hospital's own quality-control system, the same software that checks human-written records.","分数来自医院自己的质控系统，也就是检查人工书写病历的同一套软件。"],[1172.65,1179.05,127,"To write a good record, the model needs access to all the patient's information, such as inpatient records.","要写出好的病历，模型需要能获取病人的全部信息，比如住院记录。"],[1179.4,1182.51,127,"It also needs evidence sources like UpToDate.","它还需要像 UpToDate 这样的证据来源。"],[1182.86,1186.67,127,"And this runs on an upgraded HuatuoGPT.","而这一切运行在升级版的华佗GPT 上。"],[1187.02,1192.78,127,"Notice the pattern: the reward isn't invented by us; it's the institution's own standard.","注意这个模式：奖励不是我们自己发明的，而是机构自身的标准。"],[1193.13,1198.33,127,"That's what makes the trained behaviour directly useful in the real hospital.","正是这一点，让训练出来的行为可以直接在真实医院中派上用场。"]]},{"n":9,"title":"Virtual Cells, Evidence, Benchmarks and HuatuoGPT-III","blurb":"Virtual cells and organs, community-based evidence-based medicine, live clinical benchmarks, and how environments feed back into HuatuoGPT-III with RL-only adaptation.","file":"lecture09_part9.mp4","poster":"lecture09_part9.jpg","duration":1192.9,"first":128,"last":148,"slides":[{"n":128,"title":"6.4 Virtual Cells and Virtual Organs","t":0.8},{"n":129,"title":"Virtual Cells: Simulating Biology for Drug Discovery","t":27.14},{"n":130,"title":"From Cells to Organs to Patients: Multi-Scale Digital Twins","t":101.92},{"n":131,"title":"6.5 Community-Based Evidence-Based Medicine","t":169.6},{"n":132,"title":"Community-Based Evidence-Based Medicine","t":193.91},{"n":133,"title":"UpToDate: Today's Point-of-Care Reference","t":259.28},{"n":134,"title":"AI-Native UpToDate","t":295.82},{"n":135,"title":"Our Path: Education → Community → Trustworthy Agents → GMAI","t":357.82},{"n":136,"title":"Final Goal: Open, Community-Driven Medical Agents","t":414.04},{"n":137,"title":"6.6 Data, Evaluation and Infrastructure","t":493.88},{"n":138,"title":"Data and Infrastructure Underneath Everything","t":512.7},{"n":139,"title":"Evaluation as Infrastructure: Benchmark Engineering","t":578.07},{"n":140,"title":"LiveClin: A Live Clinical Benchmark","t":615.67},{"n":141,"title":"Doctors' Last Exam: Design","t":681.58},{"n":142,"title":"Dentists' Last Exam","t":771.04},{"n":143,"title":"Evaluation Through Agent Routing","t":833.81},{"n":144,"title":"6.7 Back to Better Foundation Models","t":884.08},{"n":145,"title":"From Environments Back to Better Foundation Models","t":906.41},{"n":146,"title":"Better Foundation Models: HuatuoGPT-III","t":966.13},{"n":147,"title":"HuatuoGPT-III: RL-Only Domain Adaptation","t":1043.57},{"n":148,"title":"HuatuoGPT-III Roadmap","t":1122.8}],"sents":[[0.8,5.59,128,"We've gone from patients up to hospitals. Now let's go down the stack.","我们已经从病人讲到了医院。现在我们沿着层级往下走。"],[5.94,10.67,128,"Below the patient lies biology: cells, tissues and organs.","病人之下是生物学：细胞、组织和器官。"],[11.02,17.29,128,"If we can simulate those, medical AI connects to drug discovery and personalized therapy.","如果我们能模拟这些，医疗 AI 就能与药物发现和个性化治疗联系起来。"],[17.64,21.6,128,"This section is more forward-looking and less about our own results.","这一节更具前瞻性，较少涉及我们自己的成果。"],[21.95,25.74,128,"But I think it's where some of the biggest long-term opportunities are.","但我认为，一些最大的长期机会就在这里。"],[26.99,30.78,129,"Here is the virtual cell idea in one row at the top.","顶部这一行概括了虚拟细胞的思想。"],[31.13,35.44,129,"Start from a cell's state, measured as single-cell gene expression.","从细胞的状态出发，用单细胞基因表达来度量。"],[35.79,39.95,129,"Apply a perturbation: a gene knockout, a drug, a dose.","施加一个扰动：基因敲除、一种药物、一个剂量。"],[40.3,44.08,129,"A virtual-cell model predicts how the cell responds.","虚拟细胞模型预测细胞会如何反应。"],[44.43,51.95,129,"Then do an in-silico screen: rank candidate targets and drugs by predicted effect, before anything goes into a lab.","然后做计算机模拟筛选：在进入实验室之前，按预测效果对候选靶点和药物进行排序。"],[52.3,53.61,129,"Where is the field?","这个领域目前进展如何？"],[53.96,62.7,129,"Arc Institute's State model was trained on about one hundred seventy million observational cells and over one hundred million perturbed cells.","Arc 研究所的 State 模型在大约一亿七千万个观测细胞和超过一亿个扰动细胞上进行了训练。"],[63.05,71.18,129,"Their Virtual Cell Challenge in two thousand twenty-five drew more than five thousand participants from one hundred and fourteen countries.","他们在二零二五年举办的虚拟细胞挑战赛，吸引了来自一百一十四个国家的五千多名参赛者。"],[71.53,75.04,129,"And the two thousand twenty-six edition is zero-shot.","而二零二六年的比赛是零样本的。"],[75.39,81.05,129,"An honest caveat: beating simple baselines is still hard. This field is early.","坦白说：要超过简单的基线仍然很难。这个领域还处于早期。"],[81.4,86.66,129,"Our angle: MicroVerse, which generates micro-world videos from text.","我们的切入点是：MicroVerse，它能根据文本生成微观世界的视频。"],[87.01,94.02,129,"And using language as the interface, so you can ask a virtual cell questions and get explanations.","以及把语言作为接口，这样你就可以向虚拟细胞提问并得到解释。"],[94.37,100.52,129,"If we can simulate how cells respond, drug discovery becomes search in an environment.","如果我们能模拟细胞如何反应，药物发现就变成了在环境中的搜索。"],[101.77,103.19,130,"Cells are one scale.","细胞只是一个尺度。"],[103.54,111.15,130,"The bigger vision is multi-scale digital twins: cell, then tissue, then organ, then the whole patient.","更宏大的愿景是多尺度数字孪生：从细胞，到组织，到器官，再到整个病人。"],[111.5,116.75,130,"A perturbation response at the cell level leads to growth or inflammation in tissue.","细胞层面的扰动反应，会导致组织的生长或炎症。"],[117.1,125.68,130,"That leads to changes in heart rhythm or lung mechanics at the organ level, and finally to whole-body physiology.","进而导致器官层面心律或肺力学的变化，最终影响全身的生理状态。"],[126.03,127.38,130,"There are three uses.","它有三种用途。"],[127.73,134.78,130,"Drug development: predict efficacy and toxicity before trials, maybe even with in-silico trial arms.","药物研发：在临床试验之前预测药效和毒性，甚至可能使用计算机模拟的试验组。"],[135.13,141.84,130,"Personalized therapy: simulate a specific patient's organ, say their heart, before treating it.","个性化治疗：在治疗之前，先模拟某个特定病人的器官，比如他的心脏。"],[142.19,147.29,130,"Training environments: agents learn treatment strategies on twins, not on people.","训练环境：智能体在数字孪生上学习治疗策略，而不是在真人身上。"],[147.64,152.06,130,"The open question at the bottom is a real research question, and I don't know the answer.","底部这个开放问题是一个真正的研究问题，我也不知道答案。"],[152.41,159.12,130,"Do we want one foundation model that speaks every scale, from molecules to cells to organs to clinical language?","我们是想要一个能“说”所有尺度语言的基础模型，从分子到细胞、到器官、再到临床语言？"],[159.47,163.05,130,"Or many coupled simulators that talk to each other?","还是想要许多相互耦合、彼此对话的模拟器？"],[163.4,168.2,130,"It's the generalist versus specialist question again, now across scales.","这又是通用与专用之争，只不过现在是跨尺度的。"],[169.45,173.63,131,"Now the top of the stack: community and society.","现在来到层级的顶端：社区与社会。"],[173.98,179.65,131,"Medical evidence changes every day: new trials, new guidelines, new drug warnings.","医学证据每天都在变化：新的试验、新的指南、新的药物警告。"],[180.0,182.89,131,"No single model's training data can keep up.","没有任何一个模型的训练数据能跟得上。"],[183.24,192.51,131,"So the question is how a community of experts, helped by AI, can keep medical knowledge alive and trustworthy.","所以问题是：一个在 AI 辅助下的专家社区，如何让医学知识保持鲜活和可信。"],[193.76,199.27,132,"Recall evidence-based medicine, and the evidence pyramid on the left.","回顾一下循证医学，以及左边的证据金字塔。"],[199.62,205.93,132,"At the top are guidelines and systematic reviews, then randomized controlled trials.","最顶层是指南和系统综述，然后是随机对照试验。"],[206.28,213.44,132,"Then cohort and case-control studies, and at the bottom, case reports and expert opinion.","然后是队列研究和病例对照研究，最底层是病例报告和专家意见。"],[213.79,216.1,132,"The higher you go, the more you can trust it.","越往上，可信度就越高。"],[216.45,222.44,132,"On the right is our proposal for keeping that evidence up to date with AI and a community.","右边是我们的方案：借助 AI 和社区让这些证据保持最新。"],[222.79,226.43,132,"AI drafts content from guidelines and literature.","AI 根据指南和文献起草内容。"],[226.78,231.1,132,"Experts edit and sign it, getting credit and incentives.","专家编辑并署名，从而获得认可和激励。"],[231.45,234.18,132,"Users give feedback from inside agent apps.","用户在智能体应用中给出反馈。"],[234.53,240.18,132,"And everything is exposed as an evidence API, so every medical agent can retrieve from it.","所有内容都以证据 API 的形式开放，这样每个医疗智能体都能从中检索。"],[240.53,250.01,132,"The market signal at the bottom: OpenEvidence, an evidence-grounded assistant, reports use by about sixty-five percent of US physicians.","底部是市场信号：OpenEvidence，一个以证据为基础的助手，据称约百分之六十五的美国医生在使用它。"],[250.36,251.89,132,"Doctors clearly want this.","医生们显然需要这样的工具。"],[252.24,257.88,132,"Our goal is an open version: an AI-native UpToDate maintained by a community.","我们的目标是一个开放的版本：一个由社区维护的、AI 原生的 UpToDate。"],[259.13,265.93,133,"For those who haven't seen it, this is UpToDate, the point-of-care reference that many clinicians worldwide use.","如果你没见过，这就是 UpToDate，全世界很多临床医生都在使用的床旁参考工具。"],[266.28,276.14,133,"A doctor types a clinical question and gets an expert-written, regularly updated topic review with recommendations and grades of evidence.","医生输入一个临床问题，就能得到一篇由专家撰写、定期更新的专题综述，附有推荐意见和证据等级。"],[276.49,282.07,133,"It's excellent, but it's a commercial subscription product, written by a closed group of experts.","它非常优秀，但它是一个商业订阅产品，由一个封闭的专家群体撰写。"],[282.42,287.21,133,"And it's designed for humans to read, rather than for agents to query.","而且它是为人类阅读而设计的，而不是供智能体查询的。"],[287.56,294.42,133,"Those three properties, closed, expensive and human-oriented, are exactly what we'd like to change.","封闭、昂贵、面向人类，这三个特点恰恰是我们想要改变的。"],[295.67,299.71,134,"Here's what an AI-native UpToDate could look like.","这就是一个 AI 原生的 UpToDate 可能的样子。"],[300.06,308.72,134,"First, AI drafts the core medical content: a complete, evidence-based body of knowledge built from guidelines and sources like Wikipedia.","第一，AI 起草核心医学内容：基于指南和维基百科等来源，构建一个完整的、以证据为基础的知识体系。"],[309.07,312.09,134,"Second, the community keeps it updated.","第二，由社区负责持续更新。"],[312.44,319.24,134,"Experts can take pride in editing; think of a hospital-certified pediatrician signing an article.","专家可以以参与编辑为荣；想象一位经医院认证的儿科医生在一篇文章上署名。"],[319.59,326.76,134,"AI helps them do it faster, and incentives, like free access to model APIs, reward contributors.","AI 帮助他们更快地完成工作，而像免费使用模型 API 这样的激励则用来回报贡献者。"],[327.11,336.27,134,"Related work in our group, KBAgent, uses AI plus professional documents to build general and specialist knowledge graphs.","我们团队的相关工作 KBAgent，利用 AI 加专业文档来构建通用和专科知识图谱。"],[336.62,341.88,134,"In KBAgent, experts verify the content and user feedback refines it.","在 KBAgent 中，专家负责核实内容，用户反馈则不断完善它。"],[342.23,349.4,134,"Finally, everything is exposed as an evidence API with a retriever, so it plugs into any medical agent.","最后，所有内容都以带检索器的证据 API 形式开放，可以接入任何医疗智能体。"],[349.75,356.42,134,"Think of it as Wikipedia's community model, plus AI drafting, plus expert sign-off.","可以把它理解为：维基百科的社区模式，加上 AI 起草，再加上专家署名把关。"],[357.67,362.62,135,"Let me put the community pieces together into a path. Read it from the bottom up.","我把社区相关的各个部分串成一条路径。请从下往上看。"],[362.97,365.04,135,"It starts with medical education.","它从医学教育开始。"],[365.39,372.73,135,"AI helps medical students learn faster, and trains the next generation of doctors to work with AI.","AI 帮助医学生学得更快，并培养下一代能与 AI 协作的医生。"],[373.08,383.16,135,"On that base we build a medical community that links the AI industry, hospitals, doctors, students and the public, and co-develops specialist models.","在此基础上，我们构建一个医学社区，把 AI 产业、医院、医生、学生和公众连接起来，共同开发专科模型。"],[383.51,390.15,135,"Those specialist models are then fused into trustworthy medical agents, refined together with the community.","然后，这些专科模型被融合成可信的医疗智能体，并与社区一起不断打磨。"],[390.5,392.35,135,"That's the first real milestone.","这是第一个真正的里程碑。"],[392.7,396.21,135,"And finally, generalist medical AI.","最终，实现通用医疗人工智能。"],[396.56,398.26,135,"Why start with education?","为什么从教育开始？"],[398.61,406.38,135,"Because education is low-risk, has a clear benefit, and creates the people and relationships everything else needs.","因为教育风险低、收益明确，而且能培养出其他一切所需要的人才和人脉关系。"],[406.73,412.64,135,"You can't build trusted clinical AI without doctors who understand AI and want to help build it.","如果没有懂 AI 并且愿意参与构建的医生，你就无法打造值得信赖的临床 AI。"],[413.89,419.4,136,"And here's the full picture of the final goal: open, community-driven medical agents.","这是最终目标的全貌：开放的、由社区驱动的医疗智能体。"],[419.75,425.86,136,"On the left are the LLMs: DeepSeek, Qwen, Baichuan, and our HuatuoGPT.","左边是各种大模型：DeepSeek、Qwen、百川，以及我们的华佗GPT。"],[426.21,432.76,136,"Then specialized models, o1-style reasoning models, cost-effective models and local models.","然后是专科模型、类 o1 的推理模型、高性价比模型和本地模型。"],[433.11,438.95,136,"Note the comment: there's no single model that's always the best, so cost-effectiveness matters.","注意这条说明：没有哪个模型永远是最好的，所以性价比很重要。"],[439.3,449.28,136,"In the middle is the agent layer: LLM routing, an agent framework, text embeddings, confidence estimation and trustworthy retrieval sources.","中间是智能体层：大模型路由、智能体框架、文本嵌入、置信度估计，以及可信的检索来源。"],[449.63,452.34,136,"A leaderboard connects models and agents.","一个排行榜把模型和智能体连接起来。"],[452.69,458.74,136,"Below, everything accesses data through the MCP protocol, with access control.","在下方，一切都通过带访问控制的 MCP 协议来访问数据。"],[459.09,465.64,136,"That covers local data, personal data, online data and services, and specialized models.","包括本地数据、个人数据、在线数据和服务，以及专科模型。"],[465.99,473.68,136,"On the right is the community: users from medical education, science popularization, seminars and medical schools.","右边是社区：来自医学教育、科普、研讨会和医学院的用户。"],[474.03,481.09,136,"There is also a medical tool hub over MCP, plus corpora, benchmarks and collaborative specialist models.","还有基于 MCP 的医疗工具中心，以及语料、基准评测和协作开发的专科模型。"],[481.44,485.53,136,"The community provides needs and feedback, and we help build the community.","社区提供需求和反馈，而我们帮助建设社区。"],[485.88,492.48,136,"This should feel familiar from the agents lecture: it's a harness, applied to medicine at the scale of an ecosystem.","这在智能体那一讲里应该很熟悉：这就是一个运行框架，只不过是以生态系统的规模应用在医学上。"],[493.73,500.53,137,"All these environments sound exciting, but every one of them rests on less glamorous foundations.","所有这些环境听起来都很激动人心，但每一个都建立在不那么光鲜的基础之上。"],[500.88,505.58,137,"That means data, evaluation and infrastructure that someone has to build.","那就是数据、评测和基础设施，总得有人去构建它们。"],[505.93,511.3,137,"This short section is about that layer, and especially about evaluation as infrastructure.","这一小节讲的就是这一层，尤其是把评测当作基础设施。"],[512.55,515.61,138,"Six pieces sit underneath everything we've discussed.","在我们讨论过的一切之下，有六块基石。"],[515.96,524.02,138,"Data: trustworthy corpora like our Med-Pajama, interleaved multimodal data, patient trajectories, and rubrics.","数据：可信语料，比如我们的 Med-Pajama，图文交错的多模态数据、病人轨迹，以及评分细则。"],[524.37,533.35,138,"Compute and privacy: on-premise deployment, HIS sandboxes, and privacy-preserving training, because hospital data often can't leave the hospital.","算力与隐私：本地化部署、HIS 沙盒和隐私保护训练，因为医院的数据往往不能离开医院。"],[533.7,539.58,138,"Tools: a medical tool hub over MCP, and skills for clinical tasks.","工具：基于 MCP 的医疗工具中心，以及面向临床任务的技能。"],[539.93,548.0,138,"Evaluation: live, leakage-free benchmarks like LiveClin and Doctors' Last Exam, graded with rubrics.","评测：实时更新、无数据泄露的基准，比如 LiveClin 和 Doctors' Last Exam，并用评分细则打分。"],[548.35,554.61,138,"Community: doctors, students and engineers who label, edit and use.","社区：负责标注、编辑和使用的医生、学生和工程师。"],[554.96,560.35,138,"And governance: consent, audit trails, ethics review and liability.","以及治理：知情同意、审计追踪、伦理审查和责任界定。"],[560.7,565.35,138,"The line at the bottom is the punchline: unglamorous but decisive.","底部这句话是点睛之笔：不光鲜，但具有决定性。"],[565.7,569.73,138,"Whoever builds this layer sets the standards for medical AI.","谁构建了这一层，谁就为医疗 AI 制定了标准。"],[570.08,576.67,138,"If you're looking for research directions with lasting impact, this layer is often a better bet than another model.","如果你在寻找有持久影响力的研究方向，这一层往往比再做一个模型更值得押注。"],[577.92,583.34,139,"Let me zoom in on evaluation as infrastructure, which I'd call benchmark engineering.","我们聚焦一下作为基础设施的评测，我把它称为基准工程。"],[583.69,591.52,139,"The single most important lesson we learned is on this slide: evaluation needs consensus and support from the leading players.","我们学到的最重要的一课就在这张幻灯片上：评测需要领先参与者的共识和支持。"],[591.87,595.68,139,"A technically perfect benchmark that nobody uses is worthless.","一个技术上完美、却没人使用的基准是毫无价值的。"],[596.03,604.52,139,"A benchmark matters when the major model developers, hospitals and companies agree to report on it, and when they help keep it fresh.","只有当主要的模型开发者、医院和企业都同意在上面报告结果，并帮助它保持更新时，一个基准才真正有意义。"],[604.87,610.82,139,"So building a benchmark is as much a social and organizational project as a technical one.","所以，构建基准既是一个技术项目，也同样是一个社会和组织层面的项目。"],[611.17,614.27,139,"The next few slides show how we're trying to do that.","接下来几张幻灯片展示了我们是如何尝试做到这一点的。"],[615.52,625.14,140,"LiveClin, a live clinical benchmark without leakage, published at ICLR two thousand twenty-six, is our answer to two of the earlier problems.","LiveClin 是一个无数据泄露的实时临床基准，发表于 ICLR 二零二六，它是我们对前面两个问题的回答。"],[625.49,628.23,140,"Those problems are saturation and leakage.","这两个问题就是饱和和泄露。"],[628.58,634.62,140,"Look at the example. It isn't a single question; it follows one patient through six stages over time.","看这个例子。它不是单个问题，而是跟随一位病人，在时间上经历六个阶段。"],[634.97,642.04,140,"A young woman with knee pain: initial assessment from an X-ray, and a diagnostic work-up with MRI.","一位膝盖疼痛的年轻女性：先根据 X 光做初步评估，再用 MRI 做诊断检查。"],[642.39,647.56,140,"Then a pathologic diagnosis from histology, and therapy planning.","然后根据组织学做病理诊断，再制定治疗方案。"],[647.91,654.68,140,"Then disease progression to the spine twenty months later, and management of refractory metastatic disease.","然后是二十个月后疾病进展到脊柱，以及难治性转移性疾病的处理。"],[655.03,658.47,140,"Each stage has new images and a new question.","每个阶段都有新的影像和新的问题。"],[658.82,660.97,140,"Two things make it hard to game.","有两点让它很难被刷分。"],[661.32,668.29,140,"It's live: the case set keeps being refreshed with new cases, so they post-date model training and can't have leaked.","第一，它是实时的：病例集不断用新病例更新，这些病例晚于模型训练时间，因此不可能被泄露。"],[668.64,675.95,140,"And the multi-stage, multimodal structure tests reasoning over a trajectory, not recall of a single fact.","第二，多阶段、多模态的结构考察的是对整个轨迹的推理，而不是对单个事实的记忆。"],[676.3,680.18,140,"Next, the broader design we're building on top of this.","接下来，是我们在此基础上构建的更全面的设计。"],[681.43,685.67,141,"Building on LiveClin, here is the design of Doctors' Last Exam.","在 LiveClin 的基础上，这是 Doctors' Last Exam 的设计。"],[686.02,693.5,141,"Updates are rolling, monthly or quarterly, with a white paper, as we did for LiveClin with Ant Healthcare.","更新是滚动进行的，按月或按季度，并配有白皮书，就像我们和蚂蚁健康合作的 LiveClin 那样。"],[693.85,698.72,141,"There are two leaderboards: board A releases the questions but not the answers.","有两个排行榜：A 榜公开题目但不公开答案。"],[699.07,703.32,141,"Board B hides both, so models must be submitted for testing.","B 榜题目和答案都不公开，模型必须提交上来进行测试。"],[703.67,711.84,141,"For production, experts write questions, and a parallel track synthesizes them with agents, eventually replacing manual writing.","在出题方面，由专家撰写题目，同时有一条并行路线用智能体来合成题目，最终取代人工出题。"],[712.19,714.97,141,"Every item is e-signed by an expert.","每道题都有专家的电子签名。"],[715.32,724.14,141,"Each question also carries structured attributes from the start, such as specialty, difficulty, type and knowledge points.","每道题从一开始就带有结构化属性，比如所属学科、难度、题型和涉及的知识点。"],[724.49,731.67,141,"The format is rubric-based grading in the spirit of HealthBench; rubrics are preferred, but not mandatory.","题目形式采用 HealthBench 风格的评分细则打分；优先使用评分细则，但不是强制的。"],[732.02,740.0,141,"Evaluations can be launched on the platform or through an SDK, and both produce an automatic report.","评测可以在平台上发起，也可以通过 SDK 发起，两种方式都会自动生成评测报告。"],[740.35,745.48,141,"Technical and medical experts can review and certify those reports.","技术专家和医学专家还可以对这些报告进行复核认证。"],[745.83,752.58,141,"It is co-built with industry partners, such as Ubiquant, Baichuan, Ant Healthcare and SenseTime Healthcare.","它是与产业伙伴共同建设的，比如九坤、百川、蚂蚁健康和商汤医疗。"],[752.93,760.47,141,"Hospitals that want to collaborate can also contribute de-identified internal data to build specialty benchmarks together.","愿意合作的医院，还可以提供内部脱敏数据，共同建设专科评测集。"],[760.82,769.64,141,"And quality over quantity: every item has a named expert author, and a committee reviews items and rewards good ones.","以及质量优先于数量：每道题都有署名的专家作者，并由委员会审核题目、奖励优质题目。"],[770.89,777.33,142,"Here's that design made concrete in one specialty: Dentists' Last Exam, which is live online.","这是这一设计在一个专科中的具体落地：Dentists' Last Exam，已经在线上运行。"],[777.68,780.98,142,"The flowchart is the life cycle of a single question.","这张流程图展示的是一道题的完整生命周期。"],[781.33,783.64,142,"A dentist creates a draft question.","一位牙医创建一道题目草稿。"],[783.99,788.91,142,"Several representative models answer it, and a judge LLM scores them.","几个代表性模型作答，再由一个评判大模型打分。"],[789.26,792.46,142,"Then the first gate: are all the models defeated?","然后是第一道关卡：所有模型都被难倒了吗？"],[792.81,798.67,142,"If some model already gets it right, the dentist is asked to revise the question to make it harder.","如果某个模型已经答对了，就会要求牙医修改题目，让它更难。"],[799.02,802.32,142,"Next comes a privacy and searchability check.","接下来是隐私和可搜索性检测。"],[802.67,808.47,142,"It makes sure the item contains no patient information and can't simply be looked up online.","确保题目不含病人信息，也不能简单地在网上搜到答案。"],[808.82,813.64,142,"Then three committee members review it independently and vote.","然后由三位委员独立盲审并投票。"],[813.99,821.02,142,"Finally, a board does the final review, and either publishes it to the question bank or archives it.","最后由理事会做终审，要么发布到题库，要么归档。"],[821.37,826.05,142,"Notice how much human expertise goes into every single item.","注意，每一道题都凝聚了大量的人类专业知识。"],[826.4,832.41,142,"That's deliberate: quality over quantity, and every question has a named expert behind it.","这是有意为之的：质量优先于数量，每一道题背后都有一位署名专家。"],[833.66,839.1,143,"Benchmarks are one side. The other side is measuring how agents actually perform in use.","基准只是一方面。另一方面是衡量智能体在实际使用中的表现。"],[839.45,841.77,143,"Here's the observation behind this slide.","这张幻灯片背后的观察是这样的。"],[842.12,850.03,143,"Agent applications live or die by reputation and traffic; a single developer's video can make a product spread.","智能体应用的成败取决于口碑和流量；一个开发者的视频就能让一个产品火起来。"],[850.38,856.29,143,"So instead of only testing in the lab, we can measure real effectiveness inside agent applications.","所以，与其只在实验室里测试，我们可以在智能体应用内部衡量真实的效果。"],[856.64,864.92,143,"For example, we can look at which models get routed to, kept and preferred by real users of medical agents.","比如，我们可以观察，在医疗智能体的真实用户中，哪些模型被路由选中、被保留和被偏好。"],[865.27,873.52,143,"And we can publish that regularly as a quarterly technical report, much like OpenRouter publishes usage statistics across models.","然后定期发布季度技术报告，就像 OpenRouter 发布各模型的使用统计那样。"],[873.87,879.25,143,"That's evaluation through routing: real usage becomes a signal of real value.","这就是通过路由来评测：真实的使用情况成为真实价值的信号。"],[879.6,882.68,143,"It complements expert-built benchmarks nicely.","它和专家构建的基准形成了很好的互补。"],[883.93,888.24,144,"We've climbed the whole environment stack and looked at the infrastructure beneath it.","我们已经爬完了整个环境层级，也看了它下面的基础设施。"],[888.59,891.5,144,"But environments aren't the end in themselves.","但环境本身并不是终点。"],[891.85,898.59,144,"Their real value is that they produce tasks and rewards that train the next, better foundation model.","它们真正的价值在于，能产生任务和奖励，用来训练下一个更好的基础模型。"],[898.94,905.01,144,"This short section closes the loop, back to models, with HuatuoGPT-III.","这一小节把循环闭合，回到模型本身，也就是华佗GPT-III。"],[906.26,909.34,145,"Here's the loop laid out from left to right.","这里把整个循环从左到右展开。"],[909.69,916.83,145,"Environments, meaning patients, hospitals and cells, generate tasks and rewards: verifiable outcomes and rubrics.","环境，也就是病人、医院和细胞，产生任务和奖励：可验证的结果和评分细则。"],[917.18,920.55,145,"Rubric RL trains the model on what actually matters.","基于评分细则的强化学习，让模型在真正重要的事情上接受训练。"],[920.9,924.15,145,"The result is a foundation model, HuatuoGPT-III.","结果就是一个基础模型：华佗GPT-III。"],[924.5,927.14,145,"It gets deployed and collects real feedback.","它被部署出去，收集真实的反馈。"],[927.49,932.91,145,"And that feedback flows back, along the dashed arrow, to refine the environments.","这些反馈再沿着虚线箭头流回去，用来改进环境。"],[933.26,941.21,145,"The message in the box: the model remains the core asset, but it's now trained by environments rather than only by text.","框里的信息是：模型仍然是核心资产，但它现在是由环境训练的，而不仅仅是由文本训练的。"],[941.56,953.01,145,"Concretely, HuatuoGPT-III does RL-only domain adaptation from a base model, with trustworthy mid-training on Med-Pajama and rubric-based RL.","具体来说，华佗GPT-III 从基座模型出发，只用强化学习做领域适配，并结合基于 Med-Pajama 的可信中期训练和基于评分细则的强化学习。"],[953.36,960.37,145,"Compare that with HuatuoGPT one, which was SFT on dialogue data plus a bit of RL.","对比一下第一代华佗GPT，它是在对话数据上做 SFT，再加一点强化学习。"],[960.72,964.73,145,"The center of gravity has moved from imitation to reinforcement.","重心已经从模仿转向了强化。"],[965.98,968.83,146,"Here are the ingredients of HuatuoGPT-III.","这是华佗GPT-III 的几个关键要素。"],[969.18,978.63,146,"Rubric RL, with multimodal inputs and tool calls, so the reward comes from clinician-written rubrics, in the spirit of HealthBench.","基于评分细则的强化学习，支持多模态输入和工具调用，奖励来自临床医生撰写的评分细则，秉承 HealthBench 的思路。"],[978.98,982.41,146,"Mid-training on trustworthy corpora, Med-Pajama.","在可信语料 Med-Pajama 上做中期训练。"],[982.76,984.59,146,"Evidence-based retrieval.","基于证据的检索增强。"],[984.94,993.12,146,"And reusing existing small vision models and rich interleaved multimodal data, rather than training everything from scratch.","以及复用已有的小型视觉模型和丰富的图文交错多模态数据，而不是一切从零开始训练。"],[993.47,999.7,146,"The table shows an 8B base model, Qwen3-8B-Base, trained in different ways.","这张表展示的是一个 8B 的基座模型 Qwen3-8B-Base，用不同方式训练的结果。"],[1000.05,1008.12,146,"HealthBench is the open-ended benchmark, and Medbullets, MMLU-Pro medicine and MedXpertQA are closed-ended ones.","HealthBench 是开放式基准，而 Medbullets、MMLU-Pro 医学部分和 MedXpertQA 是封闭式基准。"],[1008.47,1012.72,146,"Pure RL from the base model already helps a lot on HealthBench.","直接从基座模型做纯强化学习，在 HealthBench 上就已经有很大帮助。"],[1013.07,1025.33,146,"Our one-stage method, OnePO, which skips the separate SFT stage, beats the usual SFT-then-RL pipeline on every column, whichever teacher model is used.","我们的单阶段方法 OnePO 跳过了单独的 SFT 阶段，无论使用哪个教师模型，它在每一列上都超过了常规的先 SFT 再 RL 的流程。"],[1025.68,1030.29,146,"Compare the HealthBench totals with the leading proprietary models at the top.","把 HealthBench 的总分和顶部领先的闭源模型比较一下。"],[1030.64,1035.29,146,"On this rubric-graded benchmark, the 8B model matches or exceeds them.","在这个用评分细则打分的基准上，这个 8B 模型达到甚至超过了它们。"],[1035.64,1042.17,146,"The two papers at the bottom cover the rubric-to-principles alignment and the one-stage optimization.","底部的两篇论文分别介绍了从评分细则到原则的对齐方法，以及单阶段优化方法。"],[1043.42,1045.89,147,"And here are the scaled-up results.","这是规模扩大后的结果。"],[1046.24,1052.44,147,"The table shares the same backbone experiments as before, now labeled SeedRL.","这张表和之前共享同样的骨干实验，现在标记为 SeedRL。"],[1052.79,1067.19,147,"SeedRL is RL-only domain adaptation, seeded with off-policy data from a stronger teacher model, either GPT-5-Chat or DeepSeek-V3.2-Thinking.","SeedRL 是只用强化学习的领域适配，用来自更强教师模型的离策略数据做种子，教师模型是 GPT-5-Chat 或 DeepSeek-V3.2-Thinking。"],[1067.54,1072.66,147,"Again, SeedRL beats SFT-then-RL across the board.","同样，SeedRL 全面超过了先 SFT 再 RL 的方法。"],[1073.01,1078.78,147,"And compared with pure RL, the biggest gains are on the hard HealthBench subset.","而和纯强化学习相比，提升最大的是 HealthBench 的困难子集。"],[1079.13,1083.67,147,"At the bottom are the scaled HuatuoGPT-3 models.","底部是规模扩大后的华佗GPT-3 模型。"],[1084.02,1090.82,147,"The 8B model scores sixty-seven point five on HealthBench, and the 32B scores seventy point three.","8B 模型在 HealthBench 上得分六十七点五，32B 模型得分七十点三。"],[1091.17,1100.24,147,"Both are above the strongest proprietary baselines listed: GPT-5.2 at fifty-nine point nine, and Gemini at fifty-four point five.","两者都超过了表中最强的闭源基线：GPT-5.2 为五十九点九，Gemini 为五十四点五。"],[1100.59,1106.63,147,"On closed-ended exam questions, the frontier models are still ahead, especially on MedXpertQA.","在封闭式考试题上，前沿模型仍然领先，尤其是在 MedXpertQA 上。"],[1106.98,1109.16,147,"So here is the honest summary.","所以，坦诚的总结是这样的。"],[1109.51,1117.66,147,"On open-ended, rubric-graded clinical communication, RL with good rubrics lets a small open model compete with the frontier.","在开放式、用评分细则打分的临床沟通上，借助好的评分细则做强化学习，能让一个小型开源模型与前沿模型一较高下。"],[1118.01,1121.4,147,"On hard knowledge questions, scale still matters.","而在困难的知识型问题上，规模仍然很重要。"],[1122.65,1128.25,148,"And here's the roadmap around HuatuoGPT-III, which shows how the whole lecture fits together.","这是围绕华佗GPT-III 的路线图，它展示了整节课的内容如何串联在一起。"],[1128.6,1133.65,148,"HuatuoGPT-III itself focuses on mid-training for evidence-based medicine.","华佗GPT-III 本身专注于面向循证医学的中期训练。"],[1134.0,1138.12,148,"We built Med-Pajama, a high-quality trustworthy medical corpus.","我们构建了 Med-Pajama，一个高质量、可信的医学语料库。"],[1138.47,1144.85,148,"And we combine large-scale mid-training with retrieval to reduce hallucination.","并且把大规模中期训练和检索结合起来，以减少幻觉。"],[1145.2,1149.57,148,"HuatuoGPT-Vision-II will be a multimodal medical foundation model.","华佗GPT-Vision-II 将是一个多模态医疗基础模型。"],[1149.92,1158.16,148,"It will distill many existing expert vision models, exactly the many-specialists-to-one-model picture from part five.","它将蒸馏许多已有的专家视觉模型，这正是第五部分中“多个专科模型合成一个模型”的图景。"],[1158.51,1163.24,148,"And it will learn from large interleaved multimodal data from PubMed.","它还会从 PubMed 的大规模图文交错多模态数据中学习。"],[1163.59,1173.44,148,"HuatuoGPT-o3 targets stronger multimodal reasoning: reading case images like a doctor, zooming in and out and panning.","华佗GPT-o3 的目标是更强的多模态推理：像医生一样阅读病例影像，放大、缩小和平移。"],[1173.79,1184.09,148,"And there is an audio line: a HuatuoGPT-Audio voice assistant, MedASR for real-time medical-record writing, and HealthTTS for virtual patients.","还有一条音频路线：华佗GPT-Audio 语音助手、用于实时病历书写的 MedASR，以及用于虚拟病人的 HealthTTS。"],[1184.44,1191.05,148,"Every item connects back to something we discussed today: knowledge, perception, reasoning, environments.","每一项都和我们今天讨论过的内容相呼应：知识、感知、推理和环境。"]]},{"n":10,"title":"Applications and Ecosystem: From Triage to Open Source","blurb":"Real deployments in Longgang and at the CUHK-Shenzhen hospital, medical skills for agents, health education, startups, and the FreedomAI open-source ecosystem.","file":"lecture09_part10.mp4","poster":"lecture09_part10.jpg","duration":860.3,"first":149,"last":165,"slides":[{"n":149,"title":"7 Applications and Ecosystem","t":0.8},{"n":150,"title":"Deployment 1: Regional Triage Platform in Longgang","t":22.15},{"n":151,"title":"Deployment 2: AI Family Doctor in Longgang","t":86.67},{"n":152,"title":"Deployment 3: Simulated Patients for Training Doctors","t":160.96},{"n":153,"title":"Deployment 4: Health Education with Video Generation","t":212.08},{"n":154,"title":"Deployment 5: Personal Health Assistant","t":265.23},{"n":155,"title":"Deployment 6: Specialist Product — Dental Analysis","t":309.38},{"n":156,"title":"Medical Skills for Agents","t":369.56},{"n":157,"title":"OpenClaw at CUHK-Shenzhen Hospital (1)","t":424.83},{"n":158,"title":"OpenClaw at CUHK-Shenzhen Hospital (2)","t":464.46},{"n":159,"title":"Medical Education: Happy-Medical-AI","t":514.0},{"n":160,"title":"Health Education in the Community","t":583.37},{"n":161,"title":"Health Education: Dental Science (1)","t":626.78},{"n":162,"title":"Health Education: Dental Science (2)","t":662.4},{"n":163,"title":"Startups from Our Team","t":703.89},{"n":164,"title":"We Open-Source Everything: FreedomAI","t":762.44},{"n":165,"title":"Sharing Our Research with the Community","t":820.73}],"sents":[[0.8,5.48,149,"That completes our vision, from models to environments and back to models.","到这里，我们的愿景就讲完了：从模型到环境，再回到模型。"],[5.83,12.26,149,"But research only matters when it reaches patients, doctors and students, and when it's shared openly.","但研究只有在触达病人、医生和学生，并且被开放共享时，才真正有意义。"],[12.61,20.75,149,"So in this part, I'll show where our work is actually deployed today, how we use it for education, and how we share it with the community.","所以在这一部分，我会展示我们的工作目前实际部署在哪里，如何用于教育，以及如何与社区共享。"],[22.0,29.39,150,"The first deployment is a regional triage platform in Longgang district, Shenzhen, which covers about five million people.","第一个部署是深圳龙岗区的区域分诊平台，覆盖大约五百万人口。"],[29.74,36.02,150,"HuatuoGPT passed public testing by the Shenzhen Health Commission in June two thousand twenty-three.","华佗GPT 于二零二三年六月通过了深圳市卫健委的公开测试。"],[36.37,41.56,150,"It was then deployed across eleven hospitals in Longgang, every district public hospital.","随后它被部署到龙岗的十一家医院，覆盖了区内每一家公立医院。"],[41.91,47.09,150,"Patients access it through the district's health WeChat account, the screenshot on the left.","病人通过区里的健康微信公众号使用它，也就是左边这张截图。"],[47.44,51.96,150,"They describe their symptoms, and the system recommends which department to visit.","他们描述自己的症状，系统就会推荐应该去哪个科室就诊。"],[52.31,63.68,150,"The numbers: around three hundred thousand users, more than five hundred twenty thousand interactions, and ninety-five point four percent triage accuracy.","数据是：大约三十万用户，超过五十二万次交互，分诊准确率达百分之九十五点四。"],[64.03,69.05,150,"It was China's first region-wide, multi-hospital LLM deployment.","这是中国首个覆盖全区、多家医院的大模型部署。"],[69.4,74.71,150,"Triage is a smart first use case: it's high-volume, and it saves patients time.","分诊是一个很明智的首个应用场景：它的使用量大，而且能节省病人的时间。"],[75.06,81.07,150,"And a mistake means visiting the wrong department, not receiving the wrong treatment.","而且就算出错，也只是去错了科室，而不是接受了错误的治疗。"],[81.42,85.27,150,"Building on that, the next step was a broader service.","在此基础上，下一步是更广泛的服务。"],[86.52,90.33,151,"The second deployment is an AI family doctor in Longgang.","第二个部署是龙岗的 AI 家庭医生。"],[90.68,99.25,151,"It's a mini-program built on HuatuoGPT that offers health queries, AI consultation and report interpretation.","这是一个基于华佗GPT 构建的小程序，提供健康问询、AI 问诊和报告解读等服务。"],[99.6,108.66,151,"It is deployed in twelve hospitals and more than one hundred eighty community health centers, in a district that serves five million people.","它已部署在十二家医院和一百八十多家社区健康服务中心，所在的辖区服务五百万人口。"],[109.01,117.31,151,"On the left is the health-management side: key indicators like blood sugar, blood pressure, heart rate and BMI.","左边是健康管理部分：血糖、血压、心率、BMI 等关键指标。"],[117.66,123.4,151,"Users can track trends over time, and enter readings by hand or by uploading a photo.","用户可以查看指标随时间的变化趋势，也可以手动录入，或者拍照上传。"],[123.75,132.97,151,"It brings together check-up reports, imaging and wearable data, and generates personalized health plans, including mental-health support.","它整合了体检报告、影像资料和可穿戴设备的数据，并生成个性化的健康方案，其中也包括心理健康干预。"],[133.32,135.9,151,"On the right is the AI health consultation.","右边是 AI 健康咨询。"],[136.25,145.23,151,"It accepts voice, images and text, so a user can simply photograph a medicine box and the model explains what the medicine is.","它支持语音、图片和文字输入，用户只要拍一张药盒的照片，模型就会解释这是什么药。"],[145.58,152.97,151,"It already covers high-frequency scenarios like symptom questions, report interpretation and chronic-disease management.","它已经覆盖了症状问询、报告解读和慢病管理等高频医疗场景。"],[153.32,159.56,151,"The design goal is zero barrier: most users find it easier to use than traditional channels.","设计目标是零门槛：大多数用户都觉得它比传统渠道更方便。"],[160.81,165.43,152,"The third deployment brings simulated patients into training doctors.","第三个部署是把模拟病人用于医生培训。"],[165.78,170.98,152,"We synthesize many AI-generated simulated patients from real cases.","我们从真实病例出发，合成大量 AI 生成的模拟病人。"],[171.33,179.31,152,"We start from a large amount of real patient data, and generate patients that feel real but carry no privacy risk.","我们从大量真实的病人数据出发，生成感觉真实、却没有隐私风险的病人。"],[179.66,186.57,152,"Several models work together here: talking-face generation for video, and conditional text-to-speech for the voice.","这里融合了多种模型：用说话人脸生成来做视频，用条件文本转语音来生成声音。"],[186.92,191.81,152,"The doctor interviews the virtual patient in a chat and makes a diagnosis.","医生在对话中问诊虚拟病人，并做出诊断。"],[192.16,198.68,152,"Then HuatuoGPT scores the diagnosis, and analyzes the knowledge gaps behind any inaccurate answers.","然后，华佗GPT 给这个诊断打分，并分析诊断不准背后的知识漏洞。"],[199.03,203.57,152,"Finally, HuatuoGPT turns those gaps into targeted follow-up questions.","最后，华佗GPT 把这些知识漏洞转化成有针对性的后续题目。"],[203.92,210.68,152,"So the training is targeted at each doctor's weaknesses, while the questions still stay diverse.","这样，训练既能针对每位医生的薄弱环节，题目又保持了很好的多样性。"],[211.93,214.84,153,"From training doctors to educating the public.","从培训医生，到教育公众。"],[215.19,223.16,153,"The fourth deployment uses our MedGen video-generation model to produce health-education videos.","第四个部署是用我们的 MedGen 视频生成模型来制作健康科普视频。"],[223.51,232.25,153,"You've seen these categories before: science popularization, surgical simulation, medical animation, imaging and patient simulation.","这些类别你们之前见过：科普、手术模拟、医学动画、医学影像和病人模拟。"],[232.6,233.84,153,"Why does this matter?","为什么这很重要？"],[234.19,238.4,153,"Health education is one of the most cost-effective interventions there is.","健康教育是性价比最高的干预手段之一。"],[238.75,244.69,153,"But making good videos is slow and expensive, and there are far more topics than any team can film.","但制作好的视频既慢又贵，而且需要覆盖的主题远远多于任何团队能拍摄的数量。"],[245.04,256.56,153,"A model that turns a script into an accurate, engaging video lets a hospital or a public-health department cover many more topics, in more languages and styles.","一个能把脚本变成准确、生动视频的模型，能让医院或公共卫生部门用更多语言和风格覆盖更多主题。"],[256.91,263.83,153,"The key word is accurate, which is why a medical-specific model, rather than a general one, matters here.","关键词是“准确”，这正是为什么这里需要医学专用模型，而不是通用模型。"],[265.08,268.87,154,"The fifth deployment is about where the model runs.","第五个部署关注的是模型在哪里运行。"],[269.22,275.74,154,"The device in the photo is a small box with our university logo; it runs a medical model locally.","照片里的设备是一个印有我们校徽的小盒子，它在本地运行一个医疗模型。"],[276.09,283.5,154,"The idea on the slide: in the future, consultation can happen on your own device, and private data never leaves the phone.","幻灯片上的理念是：未来，问诊可以在你自己的设备上进行，隐私数据永远不会离开手机。"],[283.85,291.94,154,"Health data is about the most sensitive personal data there is, and many people, rightly, don't want it sent to a cloud server.","健康数据几乎是最敏感的个人数据，很多人不希望它被传到云端服务器，这是完全合理的。"],[292.29,296.56,154,"Small, efficient medical models make local deployment possible.","小而高效的医疗模型让本地部署成为可能。"],[296.91,300.81,154,"This connects directly to Lecture eleven on efficiency.","这和第十一讲关于效率的内容直接相关。"],[301.16,307.98,154,"Quantization, distillation and small models aren't just about saving money; in medicine they're also about privacy.","量化、蒸馏和小模型不只是为了省钱；在医学领域，它们也关乎隐私。"],[309.23,316.46,155,"The sixth deployment is a specialist product: dental analysis, building on the DentalGPT work we saw earlier.","第六个部署是一个专科产品：口腔分析，它建立在我们前面看到的 DentalGPT 工作之上。"],[316.81,319.53,155,"Let's walk through the screens from left to right.","我们从左到右看一下这些界面。"],[319.88,330.01,155,"The user takes photos of their teeth with guided, standardized angles: front, left and right forty-five degrees, and upper and lower arches.","用户按照引导，以标准化的角度拍摄牙齿照片：正面、左右四十五度，以及上下颌面。"],[330.36,333.96,155,"Real-time quality feedback makes sure the photos are usable.","实时的质量反馈确保照片是可用的。"],[334.31,337.88,155,"The model then produces an oral-analysis report.","然后，模型生成一份口腔分析报告。"],[338.23,347.91,155,"It includes per-view findings, flagged issues like gum inflammation, a comparison with the previous check-up, and personalized care advice.","其中包括每个视角的检查结果、标记出的问题比如牙龈炎、与上一次检查的对比，以及个性化的护理建议。"],[348.26,356.91,155,"At the far right, notice the cited references, like WHO oral-health criteria and Chinese periodontal guidelines.","在最右边，请注意引用的参考文献，比如世卫组织的口腔健康评估标准和中国牙周病防治指南。"],[357.26,362.09,155,"That last detail is the evidence-grounded property from the trustworthy-AI slide.","最后这个细节，正是可信 AI 那张幻灯片里提到的“有证据支撑”的特性。"],[362.44,368.16,155,"A consumer health product earns trust by showing where its advice comes from.","一个面向消费者的健康产品，要靠展示建议的来源来赢得信任。"],[369.41,374.37,156,"Now a very current topic: skills for agents, which connects straight to Lecture seven.","现在讲一个非常前沿的话题：智能体技能，它和第七讲直接相关。"],[374.72,381.88,156,"You'll remember that modern agent harnesses can load skills: packaged instructions and tools for specific tasks.","你们应该还记得，现代智能体框架可以加载技能，也就是为特定任务打包好的指令和工具。"],[382.23,392.03,156,"This is OpenClaw-Medical-Skills, an open-source repository from our group: a library of medical skills for the OpenClaw agent framework.","这是 OpenClaw-Medical-Skills，我们团队的一个开源仓库：为 OpenClaw 智能体框架打造的医学技能库。"],[392.38,397.21,156,"At this snapshot, it had about eight hundred sixty-nine curated skills.","在截图的这个时间点，它有大约八百六十九个精选技能。"],[397.56,403.7,156,"They cover clinical tasks, genomics, drug discovery, bioinformatics and medical devices.","覆盖临床任务、基因组学、药物发现、生物信息学和医疗器械。"],[404.05,407.9,156,"And it had about one point four thousand GitHub stars.","并且在 GitHub 上获得了大约一千四百颗星。"],[408.25,416.36,156,"The point is that domain expertise can now be packaged not only as a fine-tuned model, but as skills a general agent loads on demand.","关键在于，领域专业知识现在不仅可以打包成一个微调模型，还可以打包成通用智能体按需加载的技能。"],[416.71,423.43,156,"That's a much lighter-weight way to bring medical knowledge into agents, and it's easy for the community to contribute to.","这是把医学知识引入智能体的一种轻量得多的方式，而且社区也很容易参与贡献。"],[424.68,431.47,157,"And here's that agent stack in a real hospital: OpenClaw at CUHK-Shenzhen Hospital.","这是这套智能体技术栈在真实医院中的应用：港中大（深圳）医院的 OpenClaw。"],[431.82,437.9,157,"On the left, a doctor is consulting with a patient, with the AI assistant on the screen.","左边，一位医生正在为病人问诊，屏幕上就是 AI 助手。"],[438.25,444.21,157,"On the desk, and in the photo on the right, is a small NVIDIA DGX Spark machine.","桌上，以及右边照片里的，是一台小巧的 NVIDIA DGX Spark 主机。"],[444.56,446.23,157,"Why does a local box matter?","为什么一台本地主机很重要？"],[446.58,452.33,157,"Because the model and the agent run inside the hospital, so patient data doesn't leave the building.","因为模型和智能体都在医院内部运行，病人数据就不会离开医院。"],[452.68,456.48,157,"That's the bounded and privacy-preserving deployment we talked about.","这就是我们前面谈到的有边界、保护隐私的部署方式。"],[456.83,463.06,157,"A few years ago this would have needed a server room; now a desktop-sized device can serve a clinic.","几年前这还需要一整间机房；现在一台桌面大小的设备就能服务一个诊室。"],[464.31,470.78,158,"Here's what the doctor sees: an intelligent medical-record assistant at CUHK-Shenzhen Hospital.","这是医生看到的界面：港中大（深圳）医院的智能病历辅助系统。"],[471.13,474.35,158,"The agent, called OpenClaw-Med, is on the right.","右边就是名为 OpenClaw-Med 的智能体。"],[474.7,476.14,158,"It works in two stages.","它分两个阶段工作。"],[476.49,485.6,158,"In stage one, once the doctor selects a patient, the agent reads the patient's historical records and generates a basic reference for the new record.","第一阶段，医生选定病人后，智能体读取该病人的历史病历，为新病历生成基础参考。"],[485.95,494.14,158,"In stage two, after the doctor enters the physical exam and test results, the agent generates suggestions for diagnosis and management.","第二阶段，医生录入查体和辅助检查结果后，智能体生成诊断和处置建议。"],[494.49,499.95,158,"The doctor stays in charge, and copies what's useful into the actual record on the left.","医生始终掌握主导权，把有用的内容复制到左边的正式病历中。"],[500.3,509.0,158,"Notice the design: the AI fits into an existing workflow, the record form doctors already fill in, rather than asking them to adopt a new chatbot.","注意这个设计：AI 融入了现有的工作流程，也就是医生本来就要填写的病历表单，而不是让他们去用一个新的聊天机器人。"],[509.35,512.6,158,"That's workflows over chatbots, in practice.","这就是“工作流优先于聊天机器人”的实践。"],[513.85,517.99,159,"Let's turn to education, which I said is the foundation of our path.","我们来谈谈教育，我说过它是我们这条路径的基础。"],[518.34,526.48,159,"The Happy-Medical-AI project, linked on the slide, is our open initiative for medical education with AI.","幻灯片上给出链接的 Happy-Medical-AI 项目，是我们用 AI 开展医学教育的开放计划。"],[526.83,528.19,159,"It has three strands.","它包括三个方向。"],[528.54,533.67,159,"AI training for health professionals: helping doctors learn to collaborate with AI.","面向医疗专业人员的 AI 培训：帮助医生学会与 AI 协作。"],[534.02,538.19,159,"Doctor education with patient twins: simulated patients for training.","基于病人孪生体的医生教育：用模拟病人来培训。"],[538.54,550.33,159,"We evaluated these in two studies cited at the bottom: a CHI two thousand twenty-six co-design study with medical learners, and a comparison of human versus LLM standardized patients.","我们在底部引用的两项研究中做了评估：一项是 CHI 二零二六上与医学学习者的共同设计研究，另一项比较了人类和大模型扮演的标准化病人。"],[550.68,558.35,159,"Audio and video technology for this is developing fast: lip-sync, digital humans and HealthTTS.","相关的音视频技术正在快速发展：唇形同步、数字人和 HealthTTS。"],[558.7,566.57,159,"And full-modality patient synthesis is, I'd argue, the best training environment for both AI and human doctors.","而全模态的病人合成，我认为，是 AI 医生和人类医生最好的训练环境。"],[566.92,575.05,159,"The third strand is public health education, with video generation, illustration generation and the micro-world simulator.","第三个方向是公共健康教育，包括视频生成、插图生成和微观世界模拟器。"],[575.4,581.97,159,"The last line is my strong belief: start AI education early; it pays off for generations.","最后一行是我坚定的信念：AI 教育要尽早开始，它会惠及好几代人。"],[583.22,586.75,160,"This is the same project seen from the community side.","这是从社区角度看同一个项目。"],[587.1,591.48,160,"AI training for health professionals happens both online and offline.","面向医疗专业人员的 AI 培训，线上线下同时进行。"],[591.83,597.62,160,"Patient twins with audio and video are developing quickly; you can see the virtual patient app in the middle again.","带音视频的病人孪生体正在快速发展；你可以在中间再次看到那个虚拟病人应用。"],[597.97,602.75,160,"And there's public health education, and AI training courses for doctors.","还有公共健康教育，以及面向医生的 AI 培训课程。"],[603.1,609.33,160,"The image on the right, tiny construction workers repairing teeth, comes from our health-education work.","右边这张图，小小的建筑工人在修理牙齿，来自我们的健康科普工作。"],[609.68,612.03,160,"The next two slides show more of it.","接下来两张幻灯片会展示更多。"],[612.38,616.19,160,"The logo near the middle is the Central Academy of Fine Arts.","中间附近的标志是中央美术学院。"],[616.54,622.28,160,"Good health education needs artists and designers, as well as doctors and engineers.","好的健康教育既需要医生和工程师，也需要艺术家和设计师。"],[622.63,625.38,160,"Again, start AI education early.","再强调一次，AI 教育要尽早开始。"],[626.63,631.3,161,"Here's an example of AI-generated health education for dental science.","这是一个 AI 生成的口腔健康科普例子。"],[631.65,636.24,161,"This image shows tiny workers in hard hats, cleaning and repairing teeth.","这张图展示了戴着安全帽的小工人们正在清洁和修理牙齿。"],[636.59,644.86,161,"It's the kind of playful visual that makes children, and adults, actually pay attention to brushing and dental check-ups.","这种有趣的画面，能让孩子们，还有大人们，真正关注刷牙和口腔检查。"],[645.21,650.85,161,"The serious point behind the fun picture: health messages only work if people engage with them.","有趣画面背后的严肃观点是：健康信息只有在人们愿意关注时才会起作用。"],[651.2,655.6,161,"Generative models let us produce engaging, varied material quickly.","生成模型让我们能快速制作出生动、多样的素材。"],[655.95,661.0,161,"But every piece still has to be checked for medical accuracy before it goes out.","但每一份素材在发布之前，仍然必须经过医学准确性的核查。"],[662.25,667.56,162,"And a second dental example: an animated character introducing periodontal disease.","第二个口腔例子：一个介绍牙周病的动画角色。"],[667.91,671.21,162,"The Chinese text on the screen means periodontal disease.","屏幕上的中文意思就是“牙周病”。"],[671.56,681.44,162,"This series was released with the Shenzhen Stomatology Hospital in Pingshan, part of Southern Medical University, the same clinical partner as our dental model.","这一系列是与南方医科大学深圳口腔医院坪山院区联合发布的，也就是我们口腔模型的同一家临床合作伙伴。"],[681.79,685.5,162,"That partnership is the pattern I want you to notice.","我希望大家注意这种合作模式。"],[685.85,692.2,162,"The AI team generates content at scale, and the hospital's dentists check it and put their name on it.","AI 团队大规模生成内容，医院的牙医负责审核并署上自己的名字。"],[692.55,698.62,162,"Generation plus expert sign-off is how you make AI-produced health education trustworthy.","生成加上专家署名把关，就是让 AI 制作的健康科普内容值得信赖的方法。"],[698.97,702.49,162,"It's the same principle as the community evidence platform.","这和社区证据平台的原则是一样的。"],[703.74,708.6,163,"Another part of the ecosystem: people from our team have started companies.","生态的另一部分是：我们团队的成员创办了公司。"],[708.95,713.74,163,"Jianquan Li founded Freedom AI, working on medical education and medical AI.","Jianquan Li 创办了自由动脉（Freedom AI），专注于医学教育和医疗 AI。"],[714.09,722.23,163,"Zhihong Chen, a PhD graduate from our group, did a postdoc at Stanford, and then founded Cognita with Silicon Valley funding.","我们组的博士毕业生 Zhihong Chen，在斯坦福做完博士后之后，获得硅谷资本的投资，创办了 Cognita。"],[722.58,729.43,163,"Jianye Hou's Metastone provides high-performance computing and AI solutions, valued in the billions of RMB.","Jianye Hou 的是石科技（Metastone）提供高性能计算和 AI 解决方案，估值达数十亿元人民币。"],[729.78,731.45,163,"And students are building too.","学生们也在创业。"],[731.8,738.71,163,"Yang Xiao's Shuta AI has over a thousand daily users, with about sixty percent coverage at CUHK-Shenzhen.","Yang Xiao 的薯塔 AI 每天有一千多名用户，在港中大（深圳）的覆盖率约为百分之六十。"],[739.06,742.87,163,"Yuxuan Zhu's TennSync app quickly edits tennis-match highlights.","Yuxuan Zhu 的网事 TennSync 应用可以快速剪辑网球比赛集锦。"],[743.22,748.3,163,"It has over a thousand users, and has saved players more than five thousand hours.","它拥有一千多名用户，已为球员们节省了五千多个小时。"],[748.65,754.28,163,"I show this so you see that research and entrepreneurship aren't separate paths.","我展示这些，是想让大家看到：研究和创业并不是两条分开的路。"],[754.63,761.04,163,"Several of these started as research projects or course projects, maybe like yours.","其中好几个都是从研究项目或课程项目起步的，也许就和你们的项目一样。"],[762.29,766.56,164,"A principle we take seriously: we open-source whatever we can.","我们认真践行的一条原则是：能开源的都开源。"],[766.91,771.85,164,"Our organization is FreedomIntelligence, on both GitHub and Hugging Face.","我们的组织在 GitHub 和 Hugging Face 上都叫 FreedomIntelligence。"],[772.2,783.18,164,"On the left are the GitHub repositories you've heard about today: HuatuoGPT, HuatuoGPT-o1, HuatuoGPT-Vision, Huatuo-26M, and ALLaVA.","左边是你们今天听过的 GitHub 仓库：华佗GPT、HuatuoGPT-o1、HuatuoGPT-Vision、Huatuo-26M 和 ALLaVA。"],[783.53,792.27,164,"Also Soundwave, LongLLaVA, CMB, Apollo, Chain-of-Diagnosis and more, together with over ten thousand stars.","还有 Soundwave、LongLLaVA、CMB、Apollo、Chain-of-Diagnosis 等等，总共获得了一万多颗星。"],[792.62,798.47,164,"On the right are the Hugging Face collections, with millions of model and dataset downloads.","右边是 Hugging Face 上的模型集合，模型和数据集的下载量达数百万次。"],[798.82,804.1,164,"Hugging Face ranked the organization fourteenth among universities worldwide.","Hugging Face 把我们的组织列为全球高校中的第十四名。"],[804.45,805.63,164,"Why open-source?","为什么要开源？"],[805.98,810.47,164,"It multiplies impact far beyond what one lab can deploy.","它能把影响力放大到远超一个实验室自身所能部署的范围。"],[810.82,814.8,164,"It invites scrutiny, which is how trust gets built in medicine.","它欢迎外界审视，而这正是在医学领域建立信任的方式。"],[815.15,819.33,164,"And it gives students like you real artifacts to build on.","它也让像你们这样的学生，有真实的成果可以在此基础上继续开发。"],[820.58,824.91,165,"And here is the community impact in numbers.","这是用数字衡量的社区影响力。"],[825.26,827.74,165,"Over ten thousand GitHub stars.","超过一万颗 GitHub 星。"],[828.09,833.92,165,"More than a million model downloads, and more than a million dataset downloads on Hugging Face.","在 Hugging Face 上，模型下载量超过一百万次，数据集下载量也超过一百万次。"],[834.27,840.12,165,"And the CMB leaderboard, which many companies have used to report how their medical models perform.","还有 CMB 排行榜，很多公司都用它来报告自己医疗模型的表现。"],[840.47,843.09,165,"I'd highlight datasets and benchmarks again.","我想再次强调数据集和基准评测。"],[843.44,850.49,165,"Models are overtaken quickly, but a good dataset or benchmark can shape a whole field for years.","模型很快就会被超越，但一个好的数据集或基准，可以在很多年里塑造整个领域。"],[850.84,858.46,165,"If you want lasting impact from a course project or a thesis, consider releasing data or an evaluation, not just a model.","如果你希望课程项目或毕业论文产生持久的影响，不妨考虑发布数据或评测，而不只是一个模型。"]]},{"n":11,"title":"Outlook: Five Bets and AI Entrepreneurship","blurb":"Five bets for the future of medical AI, how AI changes startups, products and founders, and the lecture's final takeaways.","file":"lecture09_part11.mp4","poster":"lecture09_part11.jpg","duration":776.5,"first":166,"last":179,"slides":[{"n":166,"title":"8 Outlook","t":0.8},{"n":167,"title":"Outlook: Five Bets for Medical AI","t":22.94},{"n":168,"title":"AI Entrepreneurship","t":77.43},{"n":169,"title":"Organization: Smaller, Denser, More Decentralized","t":126.84},{"n":170,"title":"Example: A One-Person Telehealth Company","t":193.49},{"n":171,"title":"Product and Growth: Product as Marketing, Building in Public","t":259.7},{"n":172,"title":"Speed and Iteration","t":322.97},{"n":173,"title":"Example: Peter Steinberger and OpenClaw","t":377.96},{"n":174,"title":"Leverage and Competition","t":435.89},{"n":175,"title":"Product Paradigm: From Static Software to Living Systems","t":497.96},{"n":176,"title":"Founders: From Managing Resources to Amplifying Cognition","t":558.13},{"n":177,"title":"Join Us: PhD in AI Entrepreneurship at SLAI","t":622.4},{"n":178,"title":"Takeaways","t":682.16},{"n":179,"title":"Thanks","t":756.42}],"sents":[[0.8,3.76,166,"We've seen the research and its applications.","我们已经看过了研究成果及其应用。"],[4.11,11.47,166,"To close, let's look ahead: what medical AI needs next, and more broadly, how to build things in the AI era.","最后，我们来展望一下：医疗 AI 接下来需要什么，以及更广泛地说，在 AI 时代如何去创造。"],[11.82,16.56,166,"The second half of this part is less about medicine and more about AI entrepreneurship.","这一部分的后半段，讲医学的内容少一些，更多是关于 AI 创业。"],[16.91,21.54,166,"I think many of you will build products, and the rules are changing quickly.","因为我相信你们中很多人将来会做产品，而游戏规则正在快速变化。"],[22.79,30.24,167,"Here are my five bets for medical AI over the next few years, each a summary of something we discussed today.","这是我对未来几年医疗 AI 的五个判断，每一个都是对今天所讲内容的总结。"],[30.59,37.29,167,"Environments over datasets: the next gains come from places where AI can act and get feedback.","环境优先于数据集：下一轮的提升，来自 AI 能够行动并获得反馈的地方。"],[37.64,42.68,167,"Trust before generality: earn deployment one specialty at a time.","先可信，再通用：一个专科一个专科地赢得部署的机会。"],[43.03,51.79,167,"Workflows over chatbots: value appears when AI enters triage, records, orders and payments, not when it chats in a separate window.","工作流优先于聊天机器人：当 AI 进入分诊、病历、医嘱和支付环节时，价值才会出现，而不是在一个单独的窗口里聊天。"],[52.14,58.78,167,"Multi-scale simulation: from cells to hospitals, the substrate for drug discovery and clinical training.","多尺度模拟：从细胞到医院，这是药物发现和临床培训的基础。"],[59.13,67.2,167,"And open communities: open models, open evidence and open benchmarks, shared by doctors and engineers.","以及开放社区：开放的模型、开放的证据和开放的基准，由医生和工程师共同分享。"],[67.55,72.1,167,"These are bets, not certainties. Some of them may well be wrong.","这些是判断，而不是定论。其中一些很可能是错的。"],[72.45,76.03,167,"It would be a great exercise to argue against one of them.","试着反驳其中一个，会是一个很好的练习。"],[77.28,82.75,168,"Now a word about entrepreneurship, because it's a big part of how this technology reaches people.","现在谈谈创业，因为这是这项技术触达人们的一个重要途径。"],[83.1,91.38,168,"We actively encourage undergraduates to build consumer medical applications, for patients, for doctors, or for medical students.","我们积极鼓励本科生开发面向消费者的医疗应用，服务对象可以是病人、医生或医学生。"],[91.73,98.83,168,"You won't be alone: you'd be backed by our technical team, by SLAI and by the CUHK-Shenzhen School of Medicine.","你们不会孤军奋战：我们的技术团队、深圳河套学院和港中大（深圳）医学院都会支持你们。"],[99.18,106.66,168,"That support includes hardware like the NVIDIA DGX Spark you saw in the hospital, technical guidance, and small seed funds.","支持包括硬件，比如你们在医院里看到的 NVIDIA DGX Spark，还有技术指导和小额种子基金。"],[107.01,114.98,168,"We especially welcome projects that connect specialties for social impact, the kind of work commercial players might overlook.","我们特别欢迎那些连接不同专科、追求社会影响力的项目，也就是商业公司可能忽视的那类工作。"],[115.33,120.29,168,"If you have an idea, even a rough one from your final project, come talk to us.","如果你有想法，哪怕只是来自期末项目的一个粗略想法，也欢迎来找我们聊聊。"],[120.64,125.44,168,"The next few slides explain why I think this is an unusually good moment to try.","接下来几张幻灯片会解释，为什么我认为现在是一个格外好的尝试时机。"],[126.69,133.31,169,"How are AI-native organizations different? In one phrase: smaller, denser, more decentralized.","AI 原生的组织有什么不同？一句话：更小、更密、更去中心化。"],[133.66,142.01,169,"Organizations are getting radically smaller: from traditional companies to super individuals, and the rise of the one-person company.","组织正在急剧变小：从传统公司走向“超级个体”，一人公司开始兴起。"],[142.36,148.55,169,"Collaboration is global from day one: open-source communities are often the first organizational form.","协作从第一天起就是全球化的：开源社区往往是最早的组织形式。"],[148.9,154.14,169,"Enthusiasts join organically, and GitHub works as the coordination layer.","爱好者们自发加入，而 GitHub 充当协调层。"],[154.49,160.24,169,"Work, users and community come first, often before any formal company exists.","作品、用户和社区优先，它们往往在正式公司成立之前就已存在。"],[160.59,166.02,169,"Talent density matters more than rigid specialization; everyone is effectively full-stack.","人才密度比僵化的专业分工更重要；每个人实际上都是全栈的。"],[166.37,176.99,169,"And bottom-up innovation gets stronger, because ambitious young people can now start things directly, while large organizations pay a communication overhead.","自下而上的创新变得更强，因为有抱负的年轻人现在可以直接起步，而大型组织则要付出沟通成本。"],[177.34,189.93,169,"The core idea at the bottom: the basic unit of entrepreneurship is shifting from the large organization to the small team, the super individual and the globally coordinated community.","底部的核心观点是：创业的基本单元，正从大型组织转向小团队、超级个体和全球协作的社区。"],[190.28,192.09,169,"That's good news for students.","这对学生来说是个好消息。"],[193.34,198.69,170,"Here's a striking example, reported by Forbes in April two thousand twenty-six.","这里有一个惊人的例子，是《福布斯》在二零二六年四月报道的。"],[199.04,210.1,170,"Matthew Gallagher, forty-one, used about twenty thousand dollars and two months to build Medvi, a GLP-1 telehealth company, from his living room in Los Angeles.","四十一岁的 Matthew Gallagher 用大约两万美元和两个月时间，在洛杉矶的客厅里创办了 Medvi，一家 GLP-1 远程医疗公司。"],[210.45,216.61,170,"Look at the table, which compares it with Hims and Hers, a public company in the same market.","看这张表，它把 Medvi 和同一市场中的上市公司 Hims and Hers 做了对比。"],[216.96,227.57,170,"Medvi had about four hundred one million dollars of revenue in two thousand twenty-five, and a one point eight billion dollar run rate for two thousand twenty-six.","Medvi 在二零二五年的营收约为四亿零一百万美元，二零二六年的年化营收预计达十八亿美元。"],[227.92,232.55,170,"It has a sixteen percent net margin, two employees, and no outside funding.","它的净利润率为百分之十六，只有两名员工，没有外部融资。"],[232.9,238.74,170,"Hims and Hers had two point four billion dollars in revenue, with about two thousand four hundred employees.","而 Hims and Hers 的营收为二十四亿美元，员工约两千四百人。"],[239.09,247.37,170,"These are reported figures, and telehealth for weight-loss drugs is a special, highly regulated market, so don't take it as a recipe.","这些都是报道中的数字，而且减重药物的远程医疗是一个特殊的、受到严格监管的市场，所以别把它当成照搬的配方。"],[247.72,258.3,170,"But it shows the leverage that's now possible: one person plus a stack of APIs and AI tools can run what used to need a large organization.","但它展示了如今可能实现的杠杆效应：一个人加上一整套 API 和 AI 工具，就能运营过去需要一个大型组织才能运营的业务。"],[259.55,263.74,171,"The second shift: product and growth are fusing into one system.","第二个转变：产品和增长正在融合成一个系统。"],[264.09,273.49,171,"Product as marketing: growth is built into the product itself, and great products advertise themselves, especially in consumer markets.","产品即营销：增长内嵌于产品本身，好产品会自己做广告，尤其是在消费市场。"],[273.84,280.26,171,"Engineers go directly to market, so technical builders also need to think like product people.","工程师直接面向市场，所以技术开发者也需要像产品经理一样思考。"],[280.61,287.41,171,"The founder becomes part of the product and of distribution; people follow builders, not just brands.","创始人成为产品和分发渠道的一部分；人们追随的是创造者，而不只是品牌。"],[287.76,295.8,171,"Building in public becomes the default: sharing iterations, roadmaps, feedback and even problems openly.","公开构建成为默认方式：公开分享迭代、路线图、反馈，甚至问题。"],[296.15,304.49,171,"And that transparency is itself a competitive advantage, attracting users, developers, trust and community.","而这种透明本身就是一种竞争优势，能吸引用户、开发者、信任和社区参与。"],[304.84,313.83,171,"The core idea: growth, product design, distribution and founder identity are no longer separate functions; they reinforce one another.","核心观点是：增长、产品设计、分发和创始人身份不再是彼此独立的职能，而是相互强化。"],[314.18,321.57,171,"Notice how well this matches open-source research culture. Releasing your work openly is a form of building in public.","注意，这和开源的研究文化非常契合。公开发布你的工作，本身就是一种公开构建。"],[322.82,325.23,172,"Third: speed and iteration.","第三：速度与迭代。"],[325.58,332.6,172,"AI dramatically compresses the cost of experimentation, so speed and adaptability become central to survival.","AI 大幅压缩了试验的成本，因此速度和适应能力成为生存的关键。"],[332.95,338.32,172,"The pace is much faster, and rapid, agile development is the baseline.","节奏快了很多，快速敏捷的开发已经成为基本要求。"],[338.67,344.65,172,"Experimentation is cheaper: you can test an idea, pivot and switch direction far more easily.","试验更便宜了：你可以更轻松地验证想法、调整方向、转换赛道。"],[345.0,352.79,172,"Business models are validated faster, but also copied faster, because AI lowers both the cost of building and the cost of imitation.","商业模式验证得更快，但也被复制得更快，因为 AI 同时降低了构建的成本和模仿的成本。"],[353.14,358.6,172,"So the winners often aren't the most perfect products, but the ones that evolve fastest.","所以，胜出者往往不是最完美的产品，而是进化最快的产品。"],[358.95,363.39,172,"They learn and adjust continuously, instead of getting everything right on day one.","它们持续学习、不断调整，而不是在第一天就把一切做对。"],[363.74,370.06,172,"The core idea: the advantage isn't just being early; it's being able to evolve continuously.","核心观点是：优势不只是起步早，而是能够持续进化。"],[370.41,376.56,172,"That's also good advice for research: ship a small working version, get feedback, and iterate.","这对做研究也是很好的建议：先发布一个能用的小版本，获取反馈，然后迭代。"],[377.81,383.07,173,"Here's a concrete example you've already met today: Peter Steinberger and OpenClaw.","这是一个你们今天已经接触过的具体例子：Peter Steinberger 和 OpenClaw。"],[383.42,390.38,173,"OpenClaw is the open-source agent framework behind the medical skills and the hospital deployment we saw earlier.","OpenClaw 就是我们前面看到的医学技能库和医院部署背后的开源智能体框架。"],[390.73,392.6,173,"Look at the star history on the right.","看右边的 GitHub 星标增长曲线。"],[392.95,399.59,173,"For a long time the repository grew slowly, and then, around the turn of the year, it exploded.","很长一段时间里，这个仓库增长缓慢，然后在年末年初前后，它突然爆发了。"],[399.94,405.79,173,"It reached around one hundred eighty thousand GitHub stars within roughly two months.","在大约两个月内，它就获得了约十八万颗 GitHub 星。"],[406.14,409.45,173,"That's one of the fastest-growing open-source projects ever.","这是有史以来增长最快的开源项目之一。"],[409.8,413.47,173,"It illustrates almost every point from the last few slides.","它几乎印证了前面几张幻灯片里的每一个观点。"],[413.82,424.27,173,"A small team, or largely one person, building in public, the product as its own marketing, a global community joining organically, and very fast iteration.","一个小团队，或者说主要就是一个人，公开构建，产品本身就是营销，全球社区自发加入，以及极快的迭代。"],[424.62,434.49,173,"And it shows how quickly an ecosystem forms: within weeks, others, including our group, were building medical skills and deployments on top of it.","它还展示了生态系统形成得有多快：几周之内，包括我们团队在内的其他人，就已经在它之上构建医学技能和部署应用了。"],[435.74,438.41,174,"Fourth: leverage and competition.","第四：杠杆与竞争。"],[438.76,446.64,174,"AI gives individuals and small teams unprecedented leverage, but it also shortens how long any advantage lasts.","AI 给个人和小团队带来了前所未有的杠杆，但也缩短了任何优势能维持的时间。"],[446.99,453.73,174,"Extreme leverage: one person's productivity can match that of a hundred, or even ten thousand, people in the past.","极致的杠杆：一个人的生产力，可以相当于过去一百人、甚至一万人。"],[454.08,460.79,174,"Advantages scale faster but decay faster too: products spread quickly, and imitation happens just as quickly.","优势扩张得更快，但衰减得也更快：产品传播很快，模仿也同样迅速。"],[461.14,469.66,174,"Being first is no longer enough; you compete on iteration speed, user relationships, brand and the quality of your feedback loops.","仅仅做第一已经不够了；你要在迭代速度、用户关系、品牌和反馈循环的质量上竞争。"],[470.01,477.69,174,"So the moat shifts from static advantages, like owning a dataset, to dynamic ones: how fast you learn and compound.","所以护城河从静态优势，比如拥有某个数据集，转向了动态优势：你学习和积累的速度有多快。"],[478.04,482.55,174,"The core idea: AI amplifies both creation and competition.","核心观点是：AI 同时放大了创造和竞争。"],[482.9,487.73,174,"The new edge isn't just capability, but the speed at which capability compounds.","新的优势不只是能力本身，而是能力复利增长的速度。"],[488.08,493.46,174,"Recall the two thousand twenty-four pharmacist exam: our data advantage faded within a year.","回想一下二零二四年的药师考试：我们的数据优势在一年之内就消失了。"],[493.81,496.56,174,"Same lesson, research edition.","同样的教训，只不过是研究版本。"],[497.81,504.03,175,"Fifth: the product paradigm itself is changing, from static software to living systems.","第五：产品范式本身正在改变，从静态软件转向有生命的系统。"],[504.38,508.54,175,"AI products look more like living systems than static software.","AI 产品看起来更像有生命的系统，而不是静态的软件。"],[508.89,517.73,175,"Improvements in external models, a new frontier release for example, can upgrade your product's capabilities overnight, without you writing a line of code.","外部模型的进步，比如一个新的前沿模型发布，可以在一夜之间提升你产品的能力，而你一行代码都不用写。"],[518.08,525.91,175,"User and data loops matter more than shipping features; a sustainable feedback loop is worth more than any isolated function.","用户和数据的循环比发布新功能更重要；一个可持续的反馈循环，比任何孤立的功能都更有价值。"],[526.26,532.59,175,"Product boundaries blur, so cross-domain combinations become more natural and more powerful.","产品边界变得模糊，因此跨领域的融合变得更自然、更强大。"],[532.94,541.38,175,"And user expectations are extremely high while tolerance for failure is very low, which is especially true in medicine.","而且用户期望极高，对失败的容忍度却很低，这在医学领域尤其如此。"],[541.73,551.11,175,"The core idea: AI products are no longer one-time software artifacts; they're evolving systems that improve through interaction, data and iteration.","核心观点是：AI 产品不再是一次性的软件制品，而是通过交互、数据和迭代不断改进的演化系统。"],[551.46,556.73,175,"That's the model-environment loop from part six, seen from a business perspective.","这就是第六部分讲的模型与环境的循环，只不过是从商业的角度来看。"],[557.98,564.34,176,"And finally, what this means for founders: a shift from managing resources to amplifying cognition.","最后，这对创始人意味着什么：从管理资源，转向放大认知。"],[564.69,570.15,176,"The founder's core capability moves from controlling people and money to amplified thinking.","创始人的核心能力，从掌控人和钱，转向被放大的思考能力。"],[570.5,580.96,176,"The most important skills become identifying direction, framing problems, defining products quickly, and organizing collaboration between humans and AI.","最重要的技能变成：找准方向、定义问题、快速定义产品，以及组织人与 AI 之间的协作。"],[581.31,585.94,176,"AI becomes a force multiplier for both judgment and execution.","AI 成为判断力和执行力的倍增器。"],[586.29,594.41,176,"Capital efficiency matters more, so fundraising is no longer the only central story, because AI lowers the cost of starting.","资本效率变得更重要，融资不再是唯一的核心叙事，因为 AI 降低了创业的成本。"],[594.76,600.49,176,"And global markets matter even more, especially as geopolitics fragments the world.","而且全球市场变得更加重要，尤其是在地缘政治让世界走向碎片化的时候。"],[600.84,611.69,176,"The core idea: the future founder is less a manager of resources, and more an amplifier of judgment, creativity and execution through AI.","核心观点是：未来的创始人，不再主要是资源的管理者，而是借助 AI 放大判断力、创造力和执行力的人。"],[612.04,621.0,176,"Notice that these are exactly the skills a good PhD trains: picking problems, framing them, and executing with limited resources.","注意，这些恰恰是一个好的博士训练所培养的技能：选择问题、定义问题，以及用有限的资源去执行。"],[622.25,626.33,177,"If any of this resonates, here's a concrete opportunity.","如果这些让你有共鸣，这里有一个具体的机会。"],[626.68,638.26,177,"The Shenzhen Loop Area Institute, SLAI, is recruiting PhD students, including for AI entrepreneurship, for Fall two thousand twenty-six or Fall two thousand twenty-seven entry.","深圳河套学院，也就是 SLAI，正在招收博士生，包括 AI 创业方向，入学时间为二零二六年秋季或二零二七年秋季。"],[638.61,647.04,177,"The slide shows the Deep Search Program: one hundred twenty places in total for outstanding PhD students, across four tracks.","幻灯片上展示的是深荐计划：面向优秀博士生，总共一百二十个名额，分为四个赛道。"],[647.39,652.22,177,"A Deep Origin Talent track for original academic talent, with thirty places.","深源英才赛道，面向原创型学术人才，三十个名额。"],[652.57,658.34,177,"An Industrial Elite track with university-industry joint training, fifty places.","产业精英赛道，采用校企联合培养模式，五十个名额。"],[658.69,662.64,177,"An Academic Elite track, with thirty places.","学术精英赛道，三十个名额。"],[662.99,672.2,177,"And an Entrepreneurial Elite track, with ten places, which offers incubation and resource support for high-potential founders.","以及创业精英赛道，十个名额，为高潜力的创业者提供孵化和资源支持。"],[672.55,680.76,177,"If you're thinking about a PhD, and you care about building things that reach people, medical or otherwise, please come and talk to me.","如果你在考虑读博，并且希望做出能真正触达人们的东西，无论是不是医疗方向，都欢迎来找我聊聊。"],[682.01,684.35,178,"Let's wrap up with five takeaways.","我们用五个要点来做个总结。"],[684.7,692.84,178,"Why: medicine is high-value and high-stakes, which makes it the right domain for serious AI, and a sandbox for AGI.","为什么：医学价值高、风险高，这使它成为严肃 AI 的合适领域，也是通用人工智能的试验场。"],[693.19,702.66,178,"Story: HuatuoGPT, then HuatuoGPT-II, then o1, then III; in other words data, knowledge, reasoning, and RL.","故事：华佗GPT，然后是华佗GPT-II，然后是 o1，再到 III；换句话说，就是数据、知识、推理和强化学习。"],[703.01,705.92,178,"Each step fixed the limitation of the one before.","每一步都弥补了上一步的局限。"],[706.27,714.36,178,"Goal: generalist medical AI is the goal, and trustworthy medical AI is the necessary step on the way.","目标：通用医疗人工智能是目标，而可信医疗 AI 是通往目标的必经之路。"],[714.71,724.75,178,"Engine: build environments, standardized patients, trajectories and world models, agentic hospitals, virtual cells and community evidence.","引擎：构建环境，包括标准化病人、轨迹和世界模型、智能体医院、虚拟细胞和社区证据。"],[725.1,727.31,178,"That's where the next gains come from.","因为下一轮的提升就来自那里。"],[727.66,736.26,178,"And you: every layer needs data, evaluation and infrastructure, and people who care about both AI and patients.","还有你们：每一层都需要数据、评测和基础设施，也需要既关心 AI、又关心病人的人。"],[736.61,739.92,178,"Next is Lecture ten, multimodal LLMs.","下一讲是第十讲：多模态大语言模型。"],[740.27,748.24,178,"Today you saw multimodality from the application side, with HuatuoGPT-Vision, ShizhenGPT, speech and video.","今天你们从应用的角度看到了多模态，比如华佗GPT-Vision、时珍GPT、语音和视频。"],[748.59,755.02,178,"Next time we'll open up the architectures and training recipes behind those models in depth.","下一次，我们会深入剖析这些模型背后的架构和训练方法。"],[756.27,758.8,179,"That's all for today. Thank you for your attention.","今天就到这里。感谢大家的聆听。"],[759.15,760.61,179,"My email is on the slide.","我的邮箱就在幻灯片上。"],[760.96,770.99,179,"If you're interested in medical AI, in any of the projects you saw today, or in using our open models and datasets for your final project, feel free to write to me.","如果你对医疗 AI、对今天看到的任何项目感兴趣，或者想在期末项目中使用我们开源的模型和数据集，欢迎给我写邮件。"],[771.34,774.67,179,"See you next time for multimodal LLMs. Goodbye!","下次多模态大模型的课上见。再见！"]]}]};
